: 6, 'quantum': None, 'context': {'basis': 'US GAAP', 'currency': 'USD', 'dimensions': {}, 'entity': '0000320193', 'entity_scheme': 'http://www.sec.gov/CIK', 'perimeter': 'consolidated', 'period': {'end': '2023-12-30', 'start': '2023-10-01'}}, 'measurement': 'cash_flow'}\\n{'id': 'interim.cf.2023-12-30.investing', 'concept': 'us-gaap:NetCashProvidedByUsedInInvestingActivities', 'value': None, 'scale': 6, 'quantum': None, 'context': {'basis': 'US GAAP', 'currency': 'USD', 'dimensions': {}, 'entity': '0000320193', 'entity_scheme': 'http://www.sec.gov/CIK', 'perimeter': 'consolidated', 'period': {'end': '2023-12-30', 'start': '2023-10-01'}}, 'measurement': 'cash_flow'}\\n{'id': 'interim.cf.2023-12-30.financing', 'concept': 'us-gaap:NetCashProvidedByUsedInFinancingActivities', 'value': None, 'scale': 6, 'quantum': None, 'context': {'basis': 'US GAAP', 'currency': 'USD', 'dimensions': {}, 'entity': '0000320193', 'entity_scheme': 'http://www.sec.gov/CIK', 'perimeter': 'consolidated', 'period': {'end': '2023-12-30', 'start': '2023-10-01'}}, 'measurement': 'cash_flow'}\\n{'id': 'interim.cf.2023-12-30.closing', 'concept': 'us-gaap:CashCashEquivalentsRestrictedCashAndRestrictedCashEquivalents', 'value': None, 'scale': 6, 'quantum': None, 'context': {'basis': 'US GAAP', 'currency': 'USD', 'dimensions': {}, 'entity': '0000320193', 'entity_scheme': 'http://www.sec.gov/CIK', 'perimeter': 'consolidated', 'period': {'instant': '2023-12-30'}}, 'measurement': 'cash_including_restricted'}\\nacceptance {'accounting_validity': 'selected displayed identities only; no compliance determination', 'empirical_forecast_validity': 'not evaluated; no forecast generated', 'human_acceptance': 'pending', 'implemented': 'bounded reusable source/context/reconciliation adapter', 'specified_behavior': 'reviewed P02 plan', 'tested_invariants': 'see result.md for executed tests'}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_13\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '79,108p' docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex; sed -n '137,161p;249,265p' docs/design/chapters/13-reference-company.tex; sed -n '22,49p' tests/test_accounting_p03.py\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_13\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '79,108p' docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex; sed -n '137,161p;249,265p' docs/design/chapters/13-reference-company.tex; sed -n '22,49p' tests/test_accounting_p03.py\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\\nManagement behaviour normally uses only information available at the decision\\ndate. A perfect-foresight stress case is a separate, explicitly labelled\\npolicy. Scenarios should share the same underlying innovations when estimating\\npaired differences where appropriate, with stable stream identifiers so\\nbranch order does not change the draws. Common random numbers improve the\\ncomparability of paired simulations; they do not imply that every branch has\\nthe same economic event counts or shock distribution.\\n\\n\\\\section{Schedule and commit events}\\n\\nEach event carries an economic occurrence time, accrual interval when relevant,\\nsettlement time, entity, contract or cohort identifier, currency, inputs and\\nprovenance. Its ordering key consists of date, declared phase, dependency edges\\nand a deterministic tie identifier. The reference phases are: opening and\\nscheduled contractual changes; market observations and rate resets; business\\nevents and decisions; accrual and measurement; settlement; period closing and\\nreporting. A contract can require a more specific dependency. These phases are\\nan engineering starting point, not a universal description of market timing.\\n\\nTwo events may share a tie order only if their order is either specified or\\nirrelevant to the result. If payment before remeasurement and payment after\\nremeasurement differ, an unresolved ordering is a model ambiguity or an error.\\nThe engine does not conceal it behind alphabetical event IDs.\\n\\n\\\\begin{lstlisting}\\nexecute_event(event, state, run_context):\\n    verify prerequisites and information availability\\n    resolve applicable measurement and recognition rules\\n    compute proposed economic changes and measurements\\n\\n\\\\section{A correction changes what was knowable}\\n\\nThe original interim filing reported revenue of 120 and receivables of 30.\\nTen units of revenue had been recorded before delivery. Its tax expense was\\n3.5, profit 14 and equity 80. The annual filing subsequently corrected the\\ninterim revenue and receivable by 10 and recognised the excess tax payment as\\nprepaid tax of 2. Corrected interim profit is 6 and equity is 72, as above.\\nThe original statement remains an accurate record of what was published, even\\nthough its revenue recognition was wrong under the stated delivery rule.\\n\\nFor the temporal fixture, the original report becomes available on 1 August\\n2024 and is ingested on 3 August. The correction and annual report become\\navailable on 2 March 2025 and are ingested on 5 March. An investor-information\\nquery as of September 2024 returns 120. The same query as of 3 March 2025\\nreturns 110 when evaluated using the subsequently acquired archive. A query\\nthat additionally asks what the database contained on 4 March still returns\\n120. Publication and ingestion answer different questions.\\n\\nThe annual total 260 and corrected interim total 110 share revision group\\n\\\\code{v2}, so second-half revenue is $260-110=150$. Subtracting the original\\n120 would yield 140, but that result mixes incompatible revisions. The query\\nmust reject the subtraction unless a reviewed compatibility relationship\\nsupports it. A later date alone does not establish such a relationship.\\n\\n\\nTo demonstrate a source-to-forecast calculation, freeze the interim balance\\nsheet and apply a \\\\emph{marginal} financing stress for a following 13-week\\nperiod: a 200-basis-point rate increase, no principal change, no offsetting\\nhedge beyond the explicitly selected exposure, immediate cash settlement and\\nno tax effect. An assumed effective floating exposure $E=14{,}575$ million\\nproduces $0.02\\\\times(13/52)E=72.875$ million additional interest. This exposure\\nuses the annual notional as a conditional input; it is not asserted to be the\\ninterim net sensitivity. Under that condition, debit interest expense and\\ncredit cash by 72.875. The resulting marginal statements have cash 30,226.125,\\nassets 344,012.125, liabilities 277,327, equity 66,685.125, profit and comprehensive\\nincome of $-72.875$, and operating cash flow of $-72.875$ relative to the frozen\\nbaseline. The balance-sheet difference equals the equity difference exactly.\\n\\nIf exposure is instead only restricted to $0\\\\leq E\\\\leq14{,}575$, the\\nconditional added interest lies in $[0,72.875]$ before monetary rounding. That\\nrestriction is a stress assumption and is not claimed to bound every real\\nRENAMED = '''module FinancingStudy version \\\"2\\\";\\nuse DemoDebt version \\\"1\\\";\\nsource disclosure = external(\\\"synthetic-note-7\\\");\\nentity Beta functional USD;\\nbook Statutory entity Beta basis DemoDebt version \\\"1\\\";\\naccount Cash : Asset book Statutory;\\naccount Debt : Liability book Statutory;\\naccount InterestExpense : Expense book Statutory;\\naccount Retained : Equity book Statutory;\\nopening carried for Statutory from external(\\\"after-2025-close\\\");\\nobservation borrowing : Money<USD> instant @2025-12-31 = 150 USD from disclosure;\\nsymbol share : Real in [0, 1] because \\\"Fixed-rate proportion not disclosed\\\";\\ncontract facility : DebtMix book Statutory {\\n principal = value(borrowing); fixed_fraction = share;\\n fixed_rate = 0.05 per year; initial_floating_rate = 0.05 per year;\\n}\\nalternative fixed { assume share == 1; }\\nalternative floating { assume share == 0; }\\nscenario shock { set market_rate = constant(0.08 per year); }\\nreport financials for Statutory { mapping = external(\\\"DemoDebt.statements.v1\\\"); }\\n'''\\n\\n\\ndef bindings(principal=100, renamed=False):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Explicit synthetic evidence, separately authored from source and expected IR.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    p = F(principal); stamp = '2026-01-01T00:00:00Z'\\n    book, symbol = ('Statutory', 'share') if renamed else ('Local', 'alpha')\\n    names = ('fixed', 'floating') if renamed else ('allFixed', 'allFloating')\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nimport json,pathlib\\np=pathlib.Path('data/accounting-master/deliverables/P02/case.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text())\\nfor r in d['observations']:\\n if r['id'].startswith('interim.bs.2024-12-28.') and r['concept'] in ['us-gaap:Assets','us-gaap:Liabilities','us-gaap:StockholdersEquity','us-gaap:CashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue']:\\n  print(json.dumps(r)[:1900])\\nprint('process',pathlib.Path('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P05/plan-0.process.json').read_text())\\nPY\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nimport json,pathlib\\np=pathlib.Path('data/accounting-master/deliverables/P02/case.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text())\\nfor r in d['observations']:\\n if r['id'].startswith('interim.bs.2024-12-28.') and r['concept'] in ['us-gaap:Assets','us-gaap:Liabilities','us-gaap:StockholdersEquity','us-gaap:CashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue']:\\n  print(json.dumps(r)[:1900])\\nprint('process',pathlib.Path('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P05/plan-0.process.json').read_text())\\nPY\\\"\",\"aggreg