nThe helper closes its descriptor after validating the grant; the parent retains\\nthe lock, and restart cleans a positively identified abandoned worker before\\nanother phase runs. Stable pidfds protect recovery signalling from PID reuse.\\nRule publication is serialized and atomic, with an idempotent installation\\nreceipt for recovery between publication and the authorization record.\\n\\n\"\ntests/test_accounting_p08.py:1:\"\"\"Independent PV/cash-flow oracles and failure-atomicity checks for P08.\"\"\"\ntests/test_accounting_p08.py:99:    def test_sequence_duplicate_conflict_and_settlement_atomicity(self):\ndocs/design/research/p08-v1/unittest-output.txt:8:test_sequence_duplicate_conflict_and_settlement_atomicity (test_accounting_p08.FinancingTests.test_sequence_duplicate_conflict_and_settlement_atomicity) ... ok\ntests/test_accounting_master.py:496:    def test_atomic_json_and_duplicate_key_rejection(self):\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T164110-7313e7d0/controller-state-refresh/review_controller-0.stdin.txt:86:      \"test_atomic_json_and_duplicate_key_rejection\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T164110-7313e7d0/controller-state-refresh/review_controller-0.stdin.txt:118:    \"reviewed_evidence_contract_and_permission_scope\": \"\\n\\nQuestion: does the master execute bounded phases, actually repair failures,\\nrefresh reviewed next-phase plans, preserve evidence and resume without\\nduplicate successful work or repeated approvals?\\n\\nComparator: the current manual sequence and the frozen corpus/reference\\nbaseline. This is control-plane engineering, not a method-performance study.\\n\\nPrimary pass criteria: executable runner; exact allow-rule match; tested\\nphase state transitions; a real failed verification followed by executed\\nrepair and successful recheck; next-plan refresh containing the observed\\noutcome; a real bounded run with durable logs/state and honest residuals.\\n\\nVetoes: zero-test false pass; stale plan/control hashes; invalid worker\\nresponses; accepted results without deterministic checks/review; lost evidence;\\nconcurrent writers; unbounded child processes; arbitrary shell command injection;\\npromotion of all G1–G18 from phase-level evidence.\\n\\nExplanatory diagnostics: check/test counts, elapsed time, file counts and\\nnumber of repairs. They are not accounting accuracy or forecast metrics.\\n\\nArtifacts: scripts/run_accounting_master.py; scripts/accounting_master_catalog.json;\\ntests/test_accounting_master.py; docs/plans/accounting-master-program.md;\\ndata/accounting-master/{state.json,events.jsonl,next-plan.json,next-plan.md,runs/};\\ndocs/design/review/accounting-master-review.md; docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md.\\n\\n## Upfront permission package\\n\\nThe reviewed entrypoint will install only:\\n~/.codex/rules/accdsl-master.rules, matching\\npython3 /home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/scripts/run_accounting_master.py\\n\\nThe same exact prefix will be used for install-and-run, run/resume, status,\\nreview and refresh. The installer validates positive and negative matches\\nbefore installation and preserves existing rules. User settings and existing\\napprovals are not overwritten. Runtime-managed policy can still reject an\\naction; an allow file cannot override it.\\n\\nThe single approval request will expressly cover sequential sandboxed Codex\\nimplementation and read-only review workers for this master program, bounded\\npublic-source research and project-local code/test/artifact work. No paid data,\\nnew accounts, professional engagement, outbound messages, deployment, global\\npackage installation, permission bypass, Git initialization or source deletion.\\nNetwork/worker startup failures are diagnosed once and recorded.\\nWorker invocations disable unrelated apps/plugins/hooks/MCP startup and nested\\nagent capability for this command only. The configured model and authentication\\nare retained. Workers may not start detached jobs. Child process-group identity\\nis persisted; SIGTERM triggers cleanup, and resume checks for an existing prior\\nworker before it permits another writer. Ambiguous ownership stops for a scoped\\ndiagnostic rather than signalling an unrelated process.\\n\\nThe lifecycle guarantee is limited to the initial process group and ordinary\\nsupervisor interruption/restart. Workers are trusted not to escape that group\\nwith detached jobs; this is an explicit, unenforced operating assumption, not\\ncgroup containment or protection against a malicious worker. A cgroup-based\\nrunner would be a separate future hardening task if that threat model is needed.\\nThe current scope does not require new host privileges for cgroup management.\\nHandled signals are deferred across launch, identity capture and registration;\\nthe dedicated supervisor is single-threaded. Uncatchable termination between\\nfork and durable registration is outside this containment guarantee and is not\\nrepresented as safe resumable completion.\\n\\nInternal helper calls require a one-use capability and the inherited supervisor\\nlock. They cannot be started directly or overwrite a previous attempt's result.\\nThe helper closes its descriptor after validating the grant; the parent retains\\nthe lock, and restart cleans a positively identified abandoned worker before\\nanother phase runs. Stable pidfds protect recovery signalling from PID reuse.\\nRule publication is serialized and atomic, with an idempotent installation\\nreceipt for recovery between publication and the authorization record.\\n\\n\"\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/execution-1/repair-1.prompt.txt:247:          \"Run python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_accounting_p08.py' -v. Tests must exercise the actual parameterized implementation, with independently derived present-value and cash-flow expectations.\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/execution-1/repair-1.prompt.txt:250:          \"Test missing authority, wrong jurisdiction, out-of-period editions, overview-only or company-policy support, unsupported contract features, duplicate/conflicting events, out-of-order accruals, repeated settlement, insufficient cash and failure atomicity.\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/execution-1/repair-1.prompt.txt:289:          \"2. Record the skeptical audit before implementation. The old dossier is an arithmetic regression comparator, not an accounting oracle; journal balance is necessary but insufficient. Material assumptions are synthetic contract eligibility, comparable yield, annual timing, reporting basis, edition selection and settlement funding. Record each assumption's provenance, failure mode and early check. Source failures veto affected claims, not independent preparation. Failed invariants veto implementation acceptance. This revised scope avoids treating a financing example as the complete corporate package.\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/execution-1/repair-1.prompt.txt:293:          \"6. Produce exact multi-period cases dated within all selected editions. Use issue on 2024-01-01, coupons on 2024-12-31 and 2025-12-31, then alternative maturity settlements. Start with cash/equity 20 to fund redemption; proceeds/principal are 100, annual coupon 5, assumed comparable yield 10%, and conversion delivers ten shares. Independently derive initial liability 11050/121 and conversion equity 1050/121; subsequent liability after coupons is 1050/11 then 100, with total interest 2260/121. Expected ending cash is 10 for redemption and 110 for conversion. Generate journals, period movements and reconciled financing notes from the same state history. Label synthetic funding and yield explicitly.\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/execution-1/repair-1.prompt.txt:380:            \"text\": \"{\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Plan a source-supported compound-bond lifecycle with exact multi-period cases and matched standards comparisons, while preserving specific authority gaps and the wider corporate-method queue.\\\", \\\"steps\\\": [\\\"1. Preserve the recovery baseline. Create progress.md only in the implementation role. Record missing deliverables, relevant input hashes, declared new files and remaining checks. Use new scripts/corporate_financing_v1.py, scripts/check_accounting_p08.py and tests/test_accounting_p08.py; archive additional evidence under docs/design/research/p08-v1/. Do not change existing dossiers, shared engines, frozen corpus, controller or master plan.\\\", \\\"2. Record the skeptical audit before implementation. The old dossier is an arithmetic regression comparator, not an accounting oracle; journal balance is necessary but insufficient. Material assumptions are synthetic contract eligibility, comparable yield, annual timing, reporting basis, edition selection and settlement funding. Record each assumption's provenance, failure mode and early check. Source failures veto affected claims, not independent preparation. Failed invariants veto implementation acceptance. This revised scope avoids treating a financing example as the complete corporate package.\\\", \\\"3. Build authority-and-methods.json with versioned authority, claim, operation, comparison, research and follow-up records. Every authority record needs issuer, official URL, retrieval timestamp, retained path/hash, edition, jurisdiction/entity scope, effective-period and transition conditions, inspected paragraphs/pages, sho\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/execution-1/repair-1.prompt.txt:410:          \"text\": \"# P08 implementation checkpoint\\n\\n2026-10-03. Recovery and structured approved plan/review inspected. The two\\nrequired deliverables, engine, checker and test file are absent. Prior stopped\\nplanning work supplies no implementation evidence. Approved scope is a synthetic\\nissuer compound convertible bond; MC06/15/17/19/29/30 and G4/G7/G8 stay wider.\\n\\n## Pre-execution skeptical audit and evidence contract\\n\\nQuestion: can applicable primary authority support a parameterized, exact issuer\\nlifecycle and same-fact comparison? Comparator: existing compound-bond dossier\\n(arithmetic regression only), independently derived present values and cash flows.\\nPass: inspected applicable recognition/measurement/classification/settlement\\nanchors, parameterized atomic journals, both multi-period settlements, matched\\ninputs and reproducible notes. Vetoes: unsupported authority blocks the affected\\ntreatment; invalid dates, ineligible terms, imbalance, negative funding or state\\nmismatch block implementation acceptance. Source failures do not stop independent\\npreparation. No short check establishes accounting compliance, forecast validity,\\nhuman acceptance, superiority or whole-gap closure. Result and source/hash evidence\\nwill be preserved in authority-and-methods.json and result.md.\\n\\nDefaults audit: annual periods, two coupons, fixed shares, functional currency,\\nno fees/tax/options and 10% comparable yield come from the reviewed synthetic\\nexample (hypotheses, not real-market estimates). Wrong eligibility or yield can\\nproduce balanced but wrong accounting: reject unsupported clauses and independently\\ncheck PV, alternative parameters and authority applicability. Australian for-profit\\nTier 1 basis is a bounded scope choice; check edition and period-start limits.\\nOpening cash/equity 20 is synthetic settlement funding; test insufficient cash and\\natomic rollback. Exact rational arithmetic is an engineering choice; this does not\\nvalidate real currency rounding. Inspection dates do not substitute for\",\ndocs/design/research/p08-v1/authority-register.json:339:      \"support\": \"Retained technical specification distinguishes dated events, state changes and cash-flow functions.\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P06/execution-1/repair-1.prompt.txt:233:          \"Partitions: independently enumerate finite members and check disjointness and exhaustiveness. Test missing members, explicit residuals, duplicates and product/geography totals over the same population. Reject double counting even when each axis separately reconciles.\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T164110-7313e7d0/controller-phase-plan-repair/review_controller-0.prompt.txt:84:      \"test_atomic_json_and_duplicate_key_rejection\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T164110-7313e7d0/controller-phase-plan-repair/review_controller-0.prompt.txt:116:    \"reviewed_evidence_contract_and_permission_scope\": \"\\n\\nQuestion: does the master execute bounded phases, actually repair failures,\\nrefresh reviewed next-phase plans, preserve evidence and resume without\\nduplicate successful work or repeated approvals?\\n\\nComparator: the current manual sequence and the frozen corpus/reference\\nbaseline. This is control-plane engineering, not a method-performance study.\\n\\nPrimary pass criteria: executable runner; exact allow-rule match; tested\\nphase state transitions; a real failed verification followed by executed\\nrepair and successful recheck; next-plan refresh containing the observed\\noutcome; a real bounded run with durable logs/state and honest residuals.\\n\\nVetoes: zero-test false pass; stale plan/control hashes; invalid worker\\nresponses; accepted results without deterministic checks/review; lost evidence;\\nconcurrent writers; unbounded child processes; arbitrary shell command injection;\\npromotion of all G1–G18 from phase-level evidence.\\n\\nExplanatory diagnostics: check/test counts, elapsed time, file counts and\\nnumber of repairs. They are not accounting accuracy or forecast metrics.\\n\\nArtifacts: scripts/run_accounting_master.py; scripts/accounting_master_catalog.json;\\ntests/test_accounting_master.py; docs/plans/accounting-master-program.md;\\ndata/accounting-master/{state.json,events.jsonl,next-plan.json,next-plan.md,runs/};\\ndocs/design/review/accounting-master-review.md; docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md.\\n\\n## Upfront permission package\\n\\nThe reviewed entrypoint will install only:\\n~/.codex/rules/accdsl-master.rules, matching\\npython3 /home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/scripts/run_accounting_master.py\\n\\nThe same exact prefix will be used for install-and-run, run/resume, status,\\nreview and refresh. The installer validates positive and negative matches\\nbefore installation and preserves existing rules. User settings and existing\\napprovals are not overwritten. Runtime-managed policy can still reject an\\naction; an allow file cannot override it.\\n\\nThe single approval request will expressly cover sequential sandboxed Codex\\nimplementation and read-only review workers for this master program, bounded\\npublic-source research and project-local code/test/artifact work. No paid data,\\nnew accounts, professional engagement, outbound messages, deployment, global\\npackage installation, permission bypass, Git initialization or source deletion.\\nNetwork/worker startup failures are diagnosed once and recorded.\\nWorker invocations disable unrelated apps/plugins/hooks/MCP startup and nested\\nagent capability for this command only. The configured model and authentication\\nare retained. Workers may not start detached jobs. Child process-group identity\\nis persisted; SIGTERM triggers cleanup, and resume checks for an existing prior\\nworker before it permits another writer. Ambiguous ownership stops for a scoped\\ndiagnostic rather than signalling an unrelated process.\\n\\nThe lifecycle guarantee is limited to the initial process group and ordinary\\nsupervisor interruption/restart. Workers are trusted not to escape that group\\nwith detached jobs; this is an explicit, unenforced operating assumption, not\\ncgroup containment or protection against a malicious worker. A cgroup-based\\nrunner would be a separate future hardening task if that threat model is needed.\\nThe current scope does not require new host privileges for cgroup management.\\nHandled signals are deferred across launch, identity capture and registration;\\nthe dedicated supervisor is single-threaded. Uncatchable termination between\\nfork and durable registration is outside this containment guarantee and is not\\nrepresented as safe resumable completion.\\n\\nInternal helper calls require a one-use capability and the inherited supervisor\\nlock. They cannot be started directly or overwrite a previous attempt's result.\\nThe helper closes its descriptor after validating the grant; the parent retains\\nthe lock, and restart cleans a positively identified abandoned worker before\\nanother phase runs. Stable pidfds protect recovery signalling from PID reuse.\\nRule publication is serialized and atomic, with an idempotent installation\\nreceipt for recovery between publication and the authorization record.\\n\\n\"\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T164110-7313e7d0/manifest.json:29:  \"stop_reason\": \"Controller review requires repair: process-lifecycle: P1 — Cleanup remains interruptible after registration. bounded_process restores the original signal mask before monitoring, and its finally block calls terminate_group without blocking SIGTERM/SIGINT. If an ordinary exception already initiated final cleanup, one handled signal during its sleeps or proc.wait raises KeyboardInterrupt and aborts cleanup. Similarly, another handled signal during cleanup after an initial interruption can leave live workers behind. The outer finally restores the mask but does not finish cleanup, and exclusive_lock subsequently releases the writer lock. stop_recovered_group has the same interruptible teardown pattern. Repair: defer handled termination throughout teardown, retain ownership and the lock until quiescence or a durably recorded unresolved-cleanup veto, then restore the original mask and propagate interruption. Add focused coverage for interruption during exception-path cleanup and repeated interruption during shutdown; the supplied registration-deferral test name does not establish these cases.; process-lifecycle: P2 — stop_recovered_group can leak an acquired pidfd on an identity-read exception. After open_pidfd succeeds, the descriptor is not added to descriptors until process_identity and identity validation finish. If that read raises, for example ProcessLookupError during process exit or an I/O error, the outer finally cannot close this descriptor. Repair: register descriptor ownership immediately after acquisition, or use a per-descriptor try/finally that closes it unless ownership transfers to descriptors. Handle disappearance consistently as a vanished process while preserving fail-closed treatment of other identity-read failures. Verify that every successfully opened descriptor closes on validation failure and exception.; permissions-install: Invalid worker list: issues; worker-boundary: WB-1 — Response freshness is not enforced. In Master._worker_result, destination is folder / f'{role}-{attempt}.response.json'. An existing file is neither rejected nor distinguished from output of the current invocation. If that pathname is reused and the current child exits successfully without replacing it, destination.exists() succeeds and an old PLAN, AGREE or IMPLEMENTED response passes validation. The subsequent atomic_json rewrite makes the old response look like a newly persisted result. This is a stale-acceptance path unless callers guarantee fresh output paths, an interface invariant absent from the packet. Repair: allocate a fresh invocation-specific output pathname, reject unexpected pre-existing output, and consume only that invocation's validated response. Preserve earlier responses as evidence rather than deleting or overwriting them. If uniqueness is supplied by callers, document and enforce it at this boundary.; worker-boundary: WB-2 — Cleanup failure short-circuits integrity verification. In Master.process.finally, remaining group members cause ContinuationVeto before verify_hashes executes; failure to publish active-process.json also exits before that check. The outer worker finally provides partial coverage, but it does not explicitly include the process-local next-plan.json snapshot. Thus the supplied code does not implement the stated integrity-check coverage across all child failure paths. It already blocks continuation on survivors, so this finding is about missing integrity evidence and guard coverage, not permission to launch another writer. Repair: structure cleanup/status publication and integrity verification as independently attempted finalization operations, retain both failures and any available process result, and raise a continuation veto after collecting them. With live survivors, label the integrity snapshot provisional and require cleanup plus another integrity check before resume.; state-refresh: Blocked phases can stay blocked after the condition that blocked them changes. refresh() skips blocked_external when its stored signature matches input_fingerprint(), but that fingerprint excludes the phase's external inputs or availability. Include the specific inputs relevant to each block in the signature, or make the block explicitly retryable when they cannot be fingerprinted; test a changed external condition on resume.; state-refresh: A crash during refresh() can leave a partial next-plan.md and a next-plan.json that describes phase states not yet saved to state.json. Publish the refreshed state and plan as one recoverable generation, or add a recovery protocol that detects and rebuilds mismatched plan files before they are used; write Markdown atomically.; scheduler: Fresh reviewed plans are not enforced for subsequent phases. `controller_review(folder)` is called only once before the loop, while each later `self.refresh()` result is used immediately to select and execute the next phase. A repair or phase result can therefore alter eligibility or next actions without a new review/approval. Repair by attaching a reviewed-plan identity/hash to each refreshed plan and requiring a successful read-only review before every subsequent phase, including after repair-triggered refreshes; reject execution when that review is absent or stale.; scheduler: Protection is silently disabled when `data/financial-report-benchmark/release-manifest.json` is absent: `self.protected` becomes `{}`, after which `check_protection()` can perform no frozen-evidence comparison. This permits a run to proceed without the stated source/release/research/snapshot and controller-hash protection. Treat a missing or malformed release manifest as a continuation veto (or otherwise require an explicitly recorded, reviewed protection scope) and persist that failure in the run manifest.; scheduler: A pre-existing stop request is renamed to `prior-stop-request.json` before the scheduler loop, so `not stop.exists()` is true and the invocation proceeds. This can resume work despite an outstanding ordinary interruption request. Preserve the request as evidence but set the run outcome to `stop_requested` before phase execution (or leave an active stop marker until an explicit operator action clears it).; phase-plan-repair: scripts/run_accounting_master.py — Master.execute_phase resets the deletion baseline before every repair. If implementation deletes a pre-existing tracked file, changes_since detects it and raises MasterError. The next repair snapshots the already-damaged tree, so leaving that file absent no longer appears in changes['deleted']. Passing checks and AGREE can then accept the phase without restoring the prohibited deletion. A worker returning BLOCKED bypasses changes_since entirely, creating the same risk on resume. Preserve a durable phase-entry inventory and byte references across retries and resumed attempts; reconcile deletions after every editable worker outcome, including BLOCKED and handled failures. Require restoration of every outstanding prohibited deletion before acceptance. Keep cumulative changes available to the reviewer as well as the latest repair delta.; phase-plan-repair: scripts/run_accounting_master.py — Master.execute_phase handles BLOCKED only from plan and implementation/repair workers. A BLOCKED plan review is treated as a request for plan repair; a BLOCKED result review triggers another editable repair. Exhaustion becomes needs_plan_repair or needs_repair rather than blocked_external, defeating the stated rule that unchanged external blocks are skipped and potentially repeating work against an unavailable prerequisite. Handle BLOCKED explicitly after both review calls, preserve its issues and residuals, and use the existing external-block tracking path. If review roles cannot emit BLOCKED, that missing interface restriction must be stated and an explicit supported mechanism must convey external blockers discovered during review.; evidence: Preservation is not interruption-safe. preserve_editable writes directly to the final content-addressed destination with write_bytes. An ordinary interruption or write failure can leave a truncated file under the correct digest name. On resume, that file exists, so the function raises 'Preserved pre-edit content is corrupt' rather than recovering, even if the original bytes remain available. New copies are also not verified or fsynced before success is returned. Repair: write to a temporary sibling, verify its digest against the inventoried value, flush/fsync, atomically publish and fsync the directory. Recover an incomplete existing object only from bytes verified against the expected digest; otherwise stop while retaining evidence.; evidence: Hash-map composition silently discards conflicting protection requirements. release_hashes overwrites release-manifest entries with integrity-inventory entries; protected_hashes can overwrite earlier expected hashes with current filesystem hashes; check_protection merges controls over protected hashes. If overlapping entries disagree, only the last expectation is checked, so a protection check can pass despite violating an earlier frozen expectation. Repair: merge through a helper that permits duplicate paths only when expected hashes agree, rejects conflicts before execution, and never replaces an authoritative expected hash with a freshly observed hash.; evidence: Legacy-check failure logs are lost on the repair path. baseline captures stdout in StringIO but writes the log only after runpy.run_path returns normally. If a check raises or exits unsuccessfully, the captured diagnostic output disappears; stderr is not included either. This removes evidence needed to explain the failure and inform repair and subsequent review. Repair: persist captured output in a finally block, capture stderr as well, record the failure outcome, and propagate the original failure without converting it into acceptance.\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T164110-7313e7d0/controller-phase-plan-repair/review_controller-0.stdin.txt:84:      \"test_atomic_json_and_duplicate_key_rejection\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T164110-7313e7d0/controller-phase-plan-repair/review_controller-0.stdin.txt:116:    \"reviewed_evidence_contract_and_permission_scope\": \"\\n\\nQuestion: does the master execute bounded phases, actually repair failures,\\nrefresh reviewed next-phase plans, preserve evidence and resume without\\nduplicate successful work or repeated approvals?\\n\\nComparator: the current manual sequence and the frozen corpus/reference\\nbaseline. This is control-plane engineering, not a method-performance study.\\n\\nPrimary pass criteria: executable runner; exact allow-rule match; tested\\nphase state transitions; a real failed verification followed by executed\\nrepair and successful recheck; next-plan refresh containing the observed\\noutcome; a real bounded run with durable logs/state and honest residuals.\\n\\nVetoes: zero-test false pass; stale plan/control hashes; invalid worker\\nresponses; accepted results without deterministic checks/review; lost evidence;\\nconcurrent writers; unbounded child processes; arbitrary shell command injection;\\npromotion of all G1–G18 from phase-level evidence.\\n\\nExplanatory diagnostics: check/test counts, elapsed time, file counts and\\nnumber of repairs. They are not accounting accuracy or forecast metrics.\\n\\nArtifacts: scripts/run_accounting_master.py; scripts/accounting_master_catalog.json;\\ntests/test_accounting_master.py; docs/plans/accounting-master-program.md;\\ndata/accounting-master/{state.json,events.jsonl,next-plan.json,next-plan.md,runs/};\\ndocs/design/review/accounting-master-review.md; docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md.\\n\\n## Upfront permission package\\n\\nThe reviewed entrypoint will install only:\\n~/.codex/rules/accdsl-master.rules, matching\\npython3 /home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/scripts/run_accounting_master.py\\n\\nThe same exact prefix will be used for install-and-run, run/resume, status,\\nreview and refresh. The installer validates positive and negative matches\\nbefore installation and preserves existing rules. User settings and existing\\napprovals are not overwritten. Runtime-managed policy can still reject an\\naction; an allow file cannot override it.\\n\\nThe single approval request will expressly cover sequential sandboxed Codex\\nimplementation and read-only review workers for this master program, bounded\\npublic-source research and project-local code/test/artifact work. No paid data,\\nnew accounts, professional engagement, outbound messages, deployment, global\\npackage installation, permission bypass, Git initialization or source deletion.\\nNetwork/worker startup failures are diagnosed once and recorded.\\nWorker invocations disable unrelated apps/plugins/hooks/MCP startup and nested\\nagent capability for this command only. The configured model and authentication\\nare retained. Workers may not start detached jobs. Child process-group identity\\nis persisted; SIGTERM triggers cleanup, and resume checks for an existing prior\\nworker before it permits another writer. Ambiguous ownership stops for a scoped\\ndiagnostic rather than signalling an unrelated process.\\n\\nThe lifecycle guarantee is limited to the initial process group and ordinary\\nsupervisor interruption/restart. Workers are trusted not to escape that group\\nwith detached jobs; this is an explicit, unenforced operating assumption, not\\ncgroup containment or protection against a malicious worker. A cgroup-based\\nrunner would be a separate future hardening task if that threat model is needed.\\nThe current scope does not require new host privileges for cgroup management.\\nHandled signals are deferred across launch, identity capture and registration;\\nthe dedicated supervisor is single-threaded. Uncatchable termination between\\nfork and durable registration is outside this containment guarantee and is not\\nrepresented as safe resumable completion.\\n\\nInternal helper calls require a one-use capability and the inherited supervisor\\nlock. They cannot be started directly or overwrite a previous attempt's result.\\nThe helper closes its descriptor after validating the grant; the parent retains\\nthe lock, and restart cleans a positively identified abandoned worker before\\nanother phase runs. Stable pidfds protect recovery signalling from PID reuse.\\nRule publication is serialized and atomic, with an idempotent installation\\nreceipt for recovery between publication and the authorization record.\\n\\n\"\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/execution-1/repair-1.recovery.json:37:        \"text\": \"{\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Plan a source-supported compound-bond lifecycle with exact multi-period cases and matched standards comparisons, while preserving specific authority gaps and the wider corporate-method queue.\\\", \\\"steps\\\": [\\\"1. Preserve the recovery baseline. Create progress.md only in the implementation role. Record missing deliverables, relevant input hashes, declared new files and remaining checks. Use new scripts/corporate_financing_v1.py, scripts/check_accounting_p08.py and tests/test_accounting_p08.py; archive additional evidence under docs/design/research/p08-v1/. Do not change existing dossiers, shared engines, frozen corpus, controller or master plan.\\\", \\\"2. Record the skeptical audit before implementation. The old dossier is an arithmetic regression comparator, not an accounting oracle; journal balance is necessary but insufficient. Material assumptions are synthetic contract eligibility, comparable yield, annual timing, reporting basis, edition selection and settlement funding. Record each assumption's provenance, failure mode and early check. Source failures veto affected claims, not independent preparation. Failed invariants veto implementation acceptance. This revised scope avoids treating a financing example as the complete corporate package.\\\", \\\"3. Build authority-and-methods.json with versioned authority, claim, operation, comparison, research and follow-up records. Every authority record needs issuer, official URL, retrieval timestamp, retained path/hash, edition, jurisdiction/entity scope, effective-period and transition conditions, inspected paragraphs/pages, sho\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/execution-1/repair-1.recovery.json:67:      \"text\": \"# P08 implementation checkpoint\\n\\n2026-10-03. Recovery and structured approved plan/review inspected. The two\\nrequired deliverables, engine, checker and test file are absent. Prior stopped\\nplanning work supplies no implementation evidence. Approved scope is a synthetic\\nissuer compound convertible bond; MC06/15/17/19/29/30 and G4/G7/G8 stay wider.\\n\\n## Pre-execution skeptical audit and evidence contract\\n\\nQuestion: can applicable primary authority support a parameterized, exact issuer\\nlifecycle and same-fact comparison? Comparator: existing compound-bond dossier\\n(arithmetic regression only), independently derived present values and cash flows.\\nPass: inspected applicable recognition/measurement/classification/settlement\\nanchors, parameterized atomic journals, both multi-period settlements, matched\\ninputs and reproducible notes. Vetoes: unsupported authority blocks the affected\\ntreatment; invalid dates, ineligible terms, imbalance, negative funding or state\\nmismatch block implementation acceptance. Source failures do not stop independent\\npreparation. No short check establishes accounting compliance, forecast validity,\\nhuman acceptance, superiority or whole-gap closure. Result and source/hash evidence\\nwill be preserved in authority-and-methods.json and result.md.\\n\\nDefaults audit: annual periods, two coupons, fixed shares, functional currency,\\nno fees/tax/options and 10% comparable yield come from the reviewed synthetic\\nexample (hypotheses, not real-market estimates). Wrong eligibility or yield can\\nproduce balanced but wrong accounting: reject unsupported clauses and independently\\ncheck PV, alternative parameters and authority applicability. Australian for-profit\\nTier 1 basis is a bounded scope choice; check edition and period-start limits.\\nOpening cash/equity 20 is synthetic settlement funding; test insufficient cash and\\natomic rollback. Exact rational arithmetic is an engineering choice; this does not\\nvalidate real currency rounding. Inspection dates do not substitute for\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P06/execution-1/pre-edit-files.json:72:  \"docs/design/fixtures/northstar.json\": \"3ca1b8c9f128e2ad77bf2e618388caf7b139203fafc1f60bffde1d4094b71b2e\",\ndocs/design/research/backward-snowball.json:685:      \"inspected_context\": \"Sections 3.2--3.4, funding and portfolio equations, calibration/limitations discussion; relevant related-work/reference passages\",\ndocs/design/research/backward-snowball.json:707:      \"inspected_context\": \"Section 2 including setup, timing, funding rates and decisions; regulatory-constraint discussion; relevant related-work/reference passages\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T164110-7313e7d0/controller-permissions-install/review_controller-0.prompt.txt:85:      \"test_atomic_json_and_duplicate_key_rejection\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T164110-7313e7d0/controller-permissions-install/review_controller-0.prompt.txt:117:    \"reviewed_evidence_contract_and_permission_scope\": \"\\n\\nQuestion: does the master execute bounded phases, actually repair failures,\\nrefresh reviewed next-phase plans, preserve evidence and resume without\\nduplicate successful work or repeated approvals?\\n\\nComparator: the current manual sequence and the frozen corpus/reference\\nbaseline. This is control-plane engineering, not a method-performance study.\\n\\nPrimary pass criteria: executable runner; exact allow-rule match; tested\\nphase state transitions; a real failed verification followed by executed\\nrepair and successful recheck; next-plan refresh containing the observed\\noutcome; a real bounded run with durable logs/state and honest residuals.\\n\\nVetoes: zero-test false pass; stale plan/control hashes; invalid worker\\nresponses; accepted results without deterministic checks/review; lost evidence;\\nconcurrent writers; unbounded child processes; arbitrary shell command injection;\\npromotion of all G1–G18 from phase-level evidence.\\n\\nExplanatory diagnostics: check/test counts, elapsed time, file counts and\\nnumber of repairs. They are not accounting accuracy or forecast metrics.\\n\\nArtifacts: scripts/run_accounting_master.py; scripts/accounting_master_catalog.json;\\ntests/test_accounting_master.py; docs/plans/accounting-master-program.md;\\ndata/accounting-master/{state.json,events.jsonl,next-plan.json,next-plan.md,runs/};\\ndocs/design/review/accounting-master-review.md; docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md.\\n\\n## Upfront permission package\\n\\nThe reviewed entrypoint will install only:\\n~/.codex/rules/accdsl-master.rules, matching\\npython3 /home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/scripts/run_accounting_master.py\\n\\nThe same exact prefix will be used for install-and-run, run/resume, status,\\nreview and refresh. The installer validates positive and negative matches\\nbefore installation and preserves existing rules. User settings and existing\\napprovals are not overwritten. Runtime-managed policy can still reject an\\naction; an allow file cannot override it.\\n\\nThe single approval request will expressly cover sequential sandboxed Codex\\nimplementation and read-only review workers for this master program, bounded\\npublic-source research and project-local code/test/artifact work. No paid data,\\nnew accounts, professional engagement, outbound messages, deployment, global\\npackage installation, permission bypass, Git initialization or source deletion.\\nNetwork/worker startup failures are diagnosed once and recorded.\\nWorker invocations disable unrelated apps/plugins/hooks/MCP startup and nested\\nagent capability for this command only. The configured model and authentication\\nare retained. Workers may not start detached jobs. Child process-group identity\\nis persisted; SIGTERM triggers cleanup, and resume checks for an existing prior\\nworker before it permits another writer. Ambiguous ownership stops for a scoped\\ndiagnostic rather than signalling an unrelated process.\\n\\nThe lifecycle guarantee is limited to the initial process group and ordinary\\nsupervisor interruption/restart. Workers are trusted not to escape that group\\nwith detached jobs; this is an explicit, unenforced operating assumption, not\\ncgroup containment or protection against a malicious worker. A cgroup-based\\nrunner would be a separate future hardening task if that threat model is needed.\\nThe current scope does not require new host privileges for cgroup management.\\nHandled signals are deferred across launch, identity capture and registration;\\nthe dedicated supervisor is single-threaded. Uncatchable termination between\\nfork and durable registration is outside this containment guarantee and is not\\nrepresented as safe resumable completion.\\n\\nInternal helper calls require a one-use capability and the inherited supervisor\\nlock. They cannot be started directly or overwrite a previous attempt's result.\\nThe helper closes its descriptor after validating the grant; the parent retains\\nthe lock, and restart cleans a positively identified abandoned worker before\\nanother phase runs. Stable pidfds protect recovery signalling from PID reuse.\\nRule publication is serialized and atomic, with an idempotent installation\\nreceipt for recovery between publication and the authorization record.\\n\\n\"\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T164110-7313e7d0/controller-worker-boundary/review_controller-0.prompt.txt:84:      \"test_atomic_json_and_duplicate_key_rejection\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T164110-7313e7d0/controller-worker-boundary/review_controller-0.prompt.txt:116:    \"reviewed_evidence_contract_and_permission_scope\": \"\\n\\nQuestion: does the master execute bounded phases, actually repair failures,\\nrefresh reviewed next-phase plans, preserve evidence and resume without\\nduplicate successful work or repeated approvals?\\n\\nComparator: the current manual sequence and the frozen corpus/reference\\nbaseline. This is control-plane engineering, not a method-performance study.\\n\\nPrimary pass criteria: executable runner; exact allow-rule match; tested\\nphase state transitions; a real failed verification followed by executed\\nrepair and successful recheck; next-plan refresh containing the observed\\noutcome; a real bounded run with durable logs/state and honest residuals.\\n\\nVetoes: zero-test false pass; stale plan/control hashes; invalid worker\\nresponses; accepted results without deterministic checks/review; lost evidence;\\nconcurrent writers; unbounded child processes; arbitrary shell command injection;\\npromotion of