relle_Arelle-arelle_ModelInstanceObject.py:535:        \"\"\"(bool) -- fact is duplicate of other fact\ndocs/design/research/software/Arelle_Arelle-arelle_ModelInstanceObject.py:963:        (list) - List of ModelDimensionValues whose dimension concept could not be determined or which were duplicates\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T164110-7313e7d0/controller-evidence/review_controller-0.log:10:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"assumptions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Review is limited to the supplied code and stated interfaces; no tools were used.\\\",\\n    \\\"Workers are trusted, execution is sequential, and containment covers the initial process group and ordinary handled interruption.\\\",\\n    \\\"The packet does not show initialization or persistence of self.protected, or whether source_register always follows frozen-baseline verification. Those caller guarantees remain explicit interface assumptions.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"checks\\\": [\\n    \\\"Inspected hash composition, evidence collection, controller-test caching, baseline checks, source registration, preservation and change detection.\\\",\\n    \\\"The supplied report records 44 passing controller tests with hashes matching the supplied controller_hashes. Test bodies were not supplied; names and counts do not establish accounting correctness.\\\",\\n    \\\"Baseline and source-register outputs explicitly retain mission incompleteness and substantive residuals.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": [\\n    \\\"scripts/accounting_master_support.py\\\",\\n    \\\"scripts/run_accounting_master.py\\\",\\n    \\\"tests/test_accounting_master.py\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"issues\\\": [\\n    \\\"Preservation is not interruption-safe. preserve_editable writes directly to the final content-addressed destination with write_bytes. An ordinary interruption or write failure can leave a truncated file under the correct digest name. On resume, that file exists, so the function raises 'Preserved pre-edit content is corrupt' rather than recovering, even if the original bytes remain available. New copies are also not verified or fsynced before success is returned. Repair: write to a temporary sibling, verify its digest against the inventoried value, flush/fsync, atomically publish and fsync the directory. Recover an incomplete existing object only from bytes verified against the expected digest; otherwise stop while retaining evidence.\\\",\\n    \\\"Hash-map composition silently discards conflicting protection requirements. release_hashes overwrites release-manifest entries with integrity-inventory entries; protected_hashes can overwrite earlier expected hashes with current filesystem hashes; check_protection merges controls over protected hashes. If overlapping entries disagree, only the last expectation is checked, so a protection check can pass despite violating an earlier frozen expectation. Repair: merge through a helper that permits duplicate paths only when expected hashes agree, rejects conflicts before execution, and never replaces an authoritative expected hash with a freshly observed hash.\\\",\\n    \\\"Legacy-check failure logs are lost on the repair path. baseline captures stdout in StringIO but writes the log only after runpy.run_path returns normally. If a check raises or exits unsuccessfully, the captured diagnostic output disappears; stderr is not included either. This removes evidence needed to explain the failure and inform repair and subsequent review. Repair: persist captured output in a finally block, capture stderr as well, record the failure outcome, and propagate the original failure without converting it into acceptance.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"next_actions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Implement atomic, verified preservation with recovery for interrupted copies.\\\",\\n    \\\"Reject inconsistent overlapping protection hashes instead of silently overwriting them.\\\",\\n    \\\"Persist legacy-check diagnostics on both success and failure.\\\",\\n    \\\"Add focused regression coverage for these failure paths, rerun controller verification, and obtain fresh read-only review.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"residuals\\\": [\\n    \\\"source_register checks counts against two fields from coverage.json, not independently against the accepted 192-report panel. Its correctness therefore requires an upstream frozen-input check that guarantees the accepted panel and cannot be bypassed; that call-order guarantee is not supplied.\\\",\\n    \\\"Controller-test cache reuse assumes unchanged control hashes are sufficient despite possible environment changes and does not check that the referenced log still exists. The intended cache-validity and log-retention guarantees are not supplied.\\\",\\n    \\\"editable_files inventories selected directories and suffixes, rather than all tracked files. The stated guarantee that deleted tracked files fail requires either a narrower explicit meaning of 'tracked' or an additional deletion check outside this excerpt.\\\",\\n    \\\"Process bounds, exclusive locking, approval-rule behavior and full phase transitions cannot be independently verified from the supplied excerpts. Their stated interfaces are accepted for this bounded review.\\\",\\n    \\\"Source checks and scoped internal acceptance do not close accounting, scientific or human-acceptance gaps.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"steps\\\": [],\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Revise preservation recovery, conflicting protection-hash handling and failure-log retention. These defects affect resumability and durable evidence under ordinary failures.\\\",\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"REVISE\\\"\\n}\"}}\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261003T013709-90c553a6/P05/plan-0.prompt.txt:53:    \"objective\": \"Build an executable Northstar economic-event -> state/journal -> statements path using the existing known-history cases. Produce balance sheet, income/OCI, cash-flow and equity outputs from common journals; preserve event failures and supported scenario/history branches. Apply a supported bounded path to the prepared real case without inventing absent facts.\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261003T013709-90c553a6/P05/plan-0.prompt.txt:59:      \"Run actual event inputs, not the expected-result fixture; independently check journals and all statement bridges.\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261003T013709-90c553a6/P05/plan-0.prompt.txt:60:      \"Atomic rejection, duplicate events, economic funding default and unsupported operations have distinct outputs.\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261003T013709-90c553a6/P05/plan-0.prompt.txt:234:      \"Run actual event inputs, not the expected-result fixture; independently check journals and all statement bridges.\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261003T013709-90c553a6/P05/plan-0.prompt.txt:235:      \"Atomic rejection, duplicate events, economic funding default and unsupported operations have distinct outputs.\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T164110-7313e7d0/controller-scheduler/review_controller-0.prompt.txt:82:      \"test_atomic_json_and_duplicate_key_rejection\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T164110-7313e7d0/controller-scheduler/review_controller-0.prompt.txt:114:    \"reviewed_evidence_contract_and_permission_scope\": \"\\n\\nQuestion: does the master execute bounded phases, actually repair failures,\\nrefresh reviewed next-phase plans, preserve evidence and resume without\\nduplicate successful work or repeated approvals?\\n\\nComparator: the current manual sequence and the frozen corpus/reference\\nbaseline. This is control-plane engineering, not a method-performance study.\\n\\nPrimary pass criteria: executable runner; exact allow-rule match; tested\\nphase state transitions; a real failed verification followed by executed\\nrepair and successful recheck; next-plan refresh containing the observed\\noutcome; a real bounded run with durable logs/state and honest residuals.\\n\\nVetoes: zero-test false pass; stale plan/control hashes; invalid worker\\nresponses; accepted results without deterministic checks/review; lost evidence;\\nconcurrent writers; unbounded child processes; arbitrary shell command injection;\\npromotion of all G1–G18 from phase-level evidence.\\n\\nExplanatory diagnostics: check/test counts, elapsed time, file counts and\\nnumber of repairs. They are not accounting accuracy or forecast metrics.\\n\\nArtifacts: scripts/run_accounting_master.py; scripts/accounting_master_catalog.json;\\ntests/test_accounting_master.py; docs/plans/accounting-master-program.md;\\ndata/accounting-master/{state.json,events.jsonl,next-plan.json,next-plan.md,runs/};\\ndocs/design/review/accounting-master-review.md; docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md.\\n\\n## Upfront permission package\\n\\nThe reviewed entrypoint will install only:\\n~/.codex/rules/accdsl-master.rules, matching\\npython3 /home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/scripts/run_accounting_master.py\\n\\nThe same exact prefix will be used for install-and-run, run/resume, status,\\nreview and refresh. The installer validates positive and negative matches\\nbefore installation and preserves existing rules. User settings and existing\\napprovals are not overwritten. Runtime-managed policy can still reject an\\naction; an allow file cannot override it.\\n\\nThe single approval request will expressly cover sequential sandboxed Codex\\nimplementation and read-only review workers for this master program, bounded\\npublic-source research and project-local code/test/artifact work. No paid data,\\nnew accounts, professional engagement, outbound messages, deployment, global\\npackage installation, permission bypass, Git initialization or source deletion.\\nNetwork/worker startup failures are diagnosed once and recorded.\\nWorker invocations disable unrelated apps/plugins/hooks/MCP startup and nested\\nagent capability for this command only. The configured model and authentication\\nare retained. Workers may not start detached jobs. Child process-group identity\\nis persisted; SIGTERM triggers cleanup, and resume checks for an existing prior\\nworker before it permits another writer. Ambiguous ownership stops for a scoped\\ndiagnostic rather than signalling an unrelated process.\\n\\nThe lifecycle guarantee is limited to the initial process group and ordinary\\nsupervisor interruption/restart. Workers are trusted not to escape that group\\nwith detached jobs; this is an explicit, unenforced operating assumption, not\\ncgroup containment or protection against a malicious worker. A cgroup-based\\nrunner would be a separate future hardening task if that threat model is needed.\\nThe current scope does not require new host privileges for cgroup management.\\nHandled signals are deferred across launch, identity capture and registration;\\nthe dedicated supervisor is single-threaded. Uncatchable termination between\\nfork and durable registration is outside this containment guarantee and is not\\nrepresented as safe resumable completion.\\n\\nInternal helper calls require a one-use capability and the inherited supervisor\\nlock. They cannot be started directly or overwrite a previous attempt's result.\\nThe helper closes its descriptor after validating the grant; the parent retains\\nthe lock, and restart cleans a positively identified abandoned worker before\\nanother phase runs. Stable pidfds protect recovery signalling from PID reuse.\\nRule publication is serialized and atomic, with an idempotent installation\\nreceipt for recovery between publication and the authorization record.\\n\\n\"\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/execution-1/repair-1.stdin.txt:247:          \"Run python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_accounting_p08.py' -v. Tests must exercise the actual parameterized implementation, with independently derived present-value and cash-flow expectations.\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/execution-1/repair-1.stdin.txt:250:          \"Test missing authority, wrong jurisdiction, out-of-period editions, overview-only or company-policy support, unsupported contract features, duplicate/conflicting events, out-of-order accruals, repeated settlement, insufficient cash and failure atomicity.\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/execution-1/repair-1.stdin.txt:289:          \"2. Record the skeptical audit before implementation. The old dossier is an arithmetic regression comparator, not an accounting oracle; journal balance is necessary but insufficient. Material assumptions are synthetic contract eligibility, comparable yield, annual timing, reporting basis, edition selection and settlement funding. Record each assumption's provenance, failure mode and early check. Source failures veto affected claims, not independent preparation. Failed invariants veto implementation acceptance. This revised scope avoids treating a financing example as the complete corporate package.\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/execution-1/repair-1.stdin.txt:293:          \"6. Produce exact multi-period cases dated within all selected editions. Use issue on 2024-01-01, coupons on 2024-12-31 and 2025-12-31, then alternative maturity settlements. Start with cash/equity 20 to fund redemption; proceeds/principal are 100, annual coupon 5, assumed comparable yield 10%, and conversion delivers ten shares. Independently derive initial liability 11050/121 and conversion equity 1050/121; subsequent liability after coupons is 1050/11 then 100, with total interest 2260/121. Expected ending cash is 10 for redemption and 110 for conversion. Generate journals, period movements and reconciled financing notes from the same state history. Label synthetic funding and yield explicitly.\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/execution-1/repair-1.stdin.txt:380:            \"text\": \"{\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Plan a source-supported compound-bond lifecycle with exact multi-period cases and matched standards comparisons, while preserving specific authority gaps and the wider corporate-method queue.\\\", \\\"steps\\\": [\\\"1. Preserve the recovery baseline. Create progress.md only in the implementation role. Record missing deliverables, relevant input hashes, declared new files and remaining checks. Use new scripts/corporate_financing_v1.py, scripts/check_accounting_p08.py and tests/test_accounting_p08.py; archive additional evidence under docs/design/research/p08-v1/. Do not change existing dossiers, shared engines, frozen corpus, controller or master plan.\\\", \\\"2. Record the skeptical audit before implementation. The old dossier is an arithmetic regression comparator, not an accounting oracle; journal balance is necessary but insufficient. Material assumptions are synthetic contract eligibility, comparable yield, annual timing, reporting basis, edition selection and settlement funding. Record each assumption's provenance, failure mode and early check. Source failures veto affected claims, not independent preparation. Failed invariants veto implementation acceptance. This revised scope avoids treating a financing example as the complete corporate package.\\\", \\\"3. Build authority-and-methods.json with versioned authority, claim, operation, comparison, research and follow-up records. Every authority record needs issuer, official URL, retrieval timestamp, retained path/hash, edition, jurisdiction/entity scope, effective-period and transition conditions, inspected paragraphs/pages, sho\",\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/execution-1/repair-1.stdin.txt:410:          \"text\": \"# P08 implementation checkpoint\\n\\n2026-10-03. Recovery and structured approved plan/review inspected. The two\\nrequired deliverables, engine, checker and test file are absent. Prior stopped\\nplanning work supplies no implementation evidence. Approved scope is a synthetic\\nissuer compound convertible bond; MC06/15/17/19/29/30 and G4/G7/G8 stay wider.\\n\\n## Pre-execution skeptical audit and evidence contract\\n\\nQuestion: can applicable primary authority support a parameterized, exact issuer\\nlifecycle and same-fact comparison? Comparator: existing compound-bond dossier\\n(arithmetic regression only), independently derived present values and cash flows.\\nPass: inspected applicable recognition/measurement/classification/settlement\\nanchors, parameterized atomic journals, both multi-period settlements, matched\\ninputs and reproducible notes. Vetoes: unsupported authority blocks the affected\\ntreatment; invalid dates, ineligible terms, imbalance, negative funding or state\\nmismatch block implementation acceptance. Source failures do not stop independent\\npreparation. No short check establishes accounting compliance, forecast validity,\\nhuman acceptance, superiority or whole-gap closure. Result and source/hash evidence\\nwill be preserved in authority-and-methods.json and result.md.\\n\\nDefaults audit: annual periods, two coupons, fixed shares, functional currency,\\nno fees/tax/options and 10% comparable yield come from the reviewed synthetic\\nexample (hypotheses, not real-market estimates). Wrong eligibility or yield can\\nproduce balanced but wrong accounting: reject unsupported clauses and independently\\ncheck PV, alternative parameters and authority applicability. Australian for-profit\\nTier 1 basis is a bounded scope choice; check edition and period-start limits.\\nOpening cash/equity 20 is synthetic settlement funding; test insufficient cash and\\natomic rollback. Exact rational arithmetic is an engineering choice; this does not\\nvalidate real currency rounding. Inspection dates do not substitute for\",\ndocs/design/research/software/ledger_ledger-src_xact.cc:1268: * detect duplicate imports.\ndocs/design/research/raw/pierson2020-search.json:1:{\"meta\": {\"count\": 1, \"db_response_time_ms\": 12, \"page\": 1, \"per_page\": 3, \"groups_count\": null, \"x_query\": {\"oql\": \"works where title has (Operati