                           Aus100.2\\\\n93:DELETED IAS 32 TEXT\\\\n102:Australian Accounting Standard AASB 132 Financial Instruments: Presentation (as amended) is set out in paragraphs\\\\n103:AusCF1 – Aus100.2 and the Appendix. All the paragraphs have equal authority. Paragraphs in bold type state the\\\\n104:main principles. AASB 132 is to be read in the context of other Australian Accounting Standards, including\\\\n115:AASB 132 Financial Instruments: Presentation as amended incorporates IAS 32 Financial Instruments: Presentation\\\\n121:Tier 1\\\\n122:For-profit entities complying with AASB 132 also comply with IAS 32.\\\\n123:Not-for-profit entities’ compliance with IAS 32 will depend on whether any “Aus” paragraphs that specifically apply\\\\n139:The Australian Accounting Standards Board made Accounting Standard AASB 132 Financial Instruments:\\\\n141:This compiled version of AASB 132 applies to annual periods beginning on or after 1 January 2023 but before 1 July\\\\n157:                     Reporting Entity also applies. For-profit entities applying the Conceptual Framework for\\\\n158:                     Financial Reporting are set out in paragraph Aus1.1 of the Conceptual Framework.\\\\n173:                     Statements or AASB 128 Investments in Associates and Joint Ventures. However, in some\\\\n174:                     cases, AASB 10, AASB 127 or AASB 128 require or permit an entity to account for an\\\\n229:                     instruments is exempt from applying to these features paragraphs 15–32 and AG25–AG35\\\\n288:                              amount of cash or another financial asset for a fixed number of the entity’s own\\\\n305:                              amount of cash or another financial asset for a fixed number of the entity’s own\\\\n311:\\\\f                               fixed number of the entity’s own equity instruments for a fixed amount of any\\\\n381:                             another financial asset for a fixed number of its own equity instruments. For this\\\\n382:                             purpose, rights, options or warrants to acquire a fixed number of the entity’s own\\\\n591:            fixed number of its own equity instruments in exchange for a fixed amount of cash or another financial asset\\\\n593:            fixed number of the entity’s shares for a fixed price or for a fixed stated principal amount of a bond is an\\\\n614:        This includes a contract that will be settled by the entity receiving or delivering a fixed number of such\\\\n629:24      A contract that will be settled by the entity delivering or receiving a fixed number of its own equity\\\\n662:        Compound financial instruments (see also paragraphs AG30–\\\\n664:28      The issuer of a non-derivative financial instrument shall evaluate the terms of the financial\\\\n672:\\\\f29      An entity recognises separately the components of a financial instrument that (a) creates a financial liability\\\\n674:        of the entity. For example, a bond or similar instrument convertible by the holder into a fixed number of\\\\n678:        period of time, to convert it into a fixed number of ordinary shares of the entity). The economic effect of\\\\n683:30      Classification of the liability and equity components of a convertible instrument is not revised as a result of\\\\n690:31      AASB 9 deals with the measurement of financial assets and financial liabilities. Equity instruments are\\\\n700:32      Under the approach described in paragraph 31, the issuer of a bond convertible into ordinary shares first\\\\n896:        longer outstanding, a retrospective application of those amendments to AASB 132 would involve separating\\\\n924:           of this Standard as follows: amended paragraphs 3, 4, 8, 12, 23, 31, 42, 96C, AG2 and AG30 and deleted\\\\n942:Aus100.1            [Repealed]\\\\n946:Aus100.2            This Standard repeals AASB 132 Financial Instruments: Presentation issued in July 2004.\\\\n1050:         the holder to subscribe for or purchase a fixed number of non-puttable ordinary shares in the issuing entity\\\\n1052:         a fixed number of its own equity instruments in exchange for a fixed amount of cash or another financial\\\\n1062:         fixed number of its own equity instruments in exchange for delivering a fixed amount of cash or another\\\\n1284:        (a)       A contract that will be settled by the entity receiving or delivering a fixed number of its own\\\\n1285:                  shares for no future consideration, or exchanging a fixed number of its own shares for a fixed\\\\n1289:                  right to buy a fixed number of the entity’s shares for a fixed amount of cash. However, if the\\\\n1294:                  example is an entity’s obligation under a forward contract to repurchase a fixed number of its\\\\n1312:                  Similarly, a contract that will be settled in a fixed number of the entity’s own shares, but the\\\\n[{\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"FASB ASU2015-11 official PDF\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"403 in default and elevated requests; DART ASC330 primary text requires login; no bypass attempted\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Ministry of Finance standards index\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"502 in default and elevated requests; unofficial text retained with verification pending\\\\\\\"}]\\\\ndocs/design/research/source-support.json\\\\ndocs/design/research/claim-support.json\\\\n{'claim': 'ACTUS separates contract events/state/payoff and externally supplied risk factors', 'class': 'IMPLEMENTATION_EVIDENCE', 'anchor': 'research/standards/actus-techspecs.tex event/state/payoff and risk-factor interface', 'limit': 'Source inspection, not integration execution'}\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_7\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\\\nimport urllib.request,pathlib,json,hashlib,datetime\\\\nbase=pathlib.Path('docs/design/research/p08-v1');records=[]\\\\nurls=[('aasb9','https://www.aasb.gov.au/admin/file/content105/c9/AASB9_12-14_COMPdec22_01-23.pdf'),('fasb2020_06','https://storage.fasb.org/ASU%202020-06_0.pdf'),('aasb7','https://www.aasb.gov.au/admin/file/content105/c9/AASB7_08-15_COMPdec22_01-23.pdf')]\\\\nfor name,url in urls:\\\\n r={'id':name,'url':url,'retrieved_at':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat()}\\\\n try:\\\\n  with urllib.request.urlopen(urllib.request.Request(url,headers={'User-Agent':'AccDSL source research'}),timeout=20) as response:\\\\n   body=response.read();r.update(status=response.status,final_url=response.url,content_type=response.headers.get('Content-Type'))\\\\n  path=base/(name+('.pdf' if body.startswith(b'%PDF') else '.html'));path.write_bytes(body);r.update(path=str(path),sha256=hashlib.sha256(body).hexdigest(),bytes=len(body))\\\\n except Exception as e:r.update(error=str(e),access_status='unavailable')\\\\n records.append(r);print(json.dumps(r))\\\\n(base/'access-records.json').write_text(json.dumps(records,indent=2)+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n')\\\\nPY\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_7\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\\\nimport urllib.request,pathlib,json,hashlib,datetime\\\\nbase=pathlib.Path('docs/design/research/p08-v1');records=[]\\\\nurls=[('aasb9','https://www.aasb.gov.au/admin/file/content105/c9/AASB9_12-14_COMPdec22_01-23.pdf'),('fasb2020_06','https://storage.fasb.org/ASU%202020-06_0.pdf'),('aasb7','https://www.aasb.gov.au/admin/file/content105/c9/AASB7_08-15_COMPdec22_01-23.pdf')]\\\\nfor name,url in urls:\\\\n r={'id':name,'url':url,'retrieved_at':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat()}\\\\n try:\\\\n  with urllib.request.urlopen(urllib.request.Request(url,headers={'User-Agent':'AccDSL source research'}),timeout=20) as response:\\\\n   body=response.read();r.update(status=response.status,final_url=response.url,content_type=response.headers.get('Content-Type'))\\\\n  path=base/(name+('.pdf' if body.startswith(b'%PDF') else '.html'));path.write_bytes(body);r.update(path=str(path),sha256=hashlib.sha256(body).hexdigest(),bytes=len(body))\\\\n except Exception as e:r.update(error=str(e),access_status='unavailable')\\\\n records.append(r);print(json.dumps(r))\\\\n(base/'access-records.json').write_text(json.dumps(records,indent=2)+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n')\\\\nPY\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"aasb9\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"url\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"https://www.aasb.gov.au/admin/file/content105/c9/AASB9_12-14_COMPdec22_01-23.pdf\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"retrieved_at\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"2026-10-03T01:04:23.430065+00:00\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": 200, \\\\\\\"final_url\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"https://www.aasb.gov.au/admin/file/content105/c9/AASB9_12-14_COMPdec22_01-23.pdf\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"content_type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"application/pdf\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb9.pdf\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"sha256\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"8f5a87c67a76c193bedeee8ea7f3f21556b3886eee4184a62c7045256b3f84f0\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"bytes\\\\\\\": 2195229}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"fasb2020_06\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"url\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"https://storage.fasb.org/ASU%202020-06_0.pdf\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"retrieved_at\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"2026-10-03T01:04:25.541355+00:00\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"error\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"HTTP Error 403: Forbidden\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"access_status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"unavailable\\\\\\\"}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"aasb7\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"url\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"https://www.aasb.gov.au/admin/file/content105/c9/AASB7_08-15_COMPdec22_01-23.pdf\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"retrieved_at\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"2026-10-03T01:04:26.758268+00:00\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": 200, \\\\\\\"final_url\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"https://www.aasb.gov.au/admin/file/content105/c9/AASB7_08-15_COMPdec22_01-23.pdf\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"content_type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"application/pdf\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb7.pdf\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"sha256\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"215bbd5ea6850443303046ad5c8587467a5b643910d2a2b5716569be2644a1bc\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"bytes\\\\\\\": 1329611}\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_8\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The recovery snapshot matches the files: P08 has no implementation yet. The existing dossier supports the proposed arithmetic, but its subsequent-measurement authority is still missing. I’ve recorded that distinction and the acceptance vetoes in the checkpoint; source acquisition is underway.\\\\n\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_9\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '580,717p' docs/design/research/standards/aasb132.txt\\\\nsed -n '1350,1417p' docs/design/research/standards/aasb132.txt\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_9\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '580,717p' docs/design/research/standards/aasb132.txt\\\\nsed -n '1350,1417p' docs/design/research/standards/aasb132.txt\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"            instruments to be received or delivered equals the amount of the contractual right or obligation. Such a\\\\n            contractual right or obligation may be for a fixed amount or an amount that fluctuates in part or in full in\\\\n            response to changes in a variable other than the market price of the entity’s own equity instruments (eg an\\\\n            interest rate, a commodity price or a financial instrument price). Two examples are (a) a contract to deliver\\\\n            as many of the entity’s own equity instruments as are equal in value to CU100, 1 and (b) a contract to\\\\n            deliver as many of the entity’s own equity instruments as are equal in value to the value of 100 ounces of\\\\n            gold. Such a contract is a financial liability of the entity even though the entity must or can settle it by\\\\n            delivering its own equity instruments. It is not an equity instrument because the entity uses a variable\\\\n            number of its own equity instruments as a means to settle the contract. Accordingly, the contract does not\\\\n            evidence a residual interest in the entity’s assets after deducting all of its liabilities.\\\\n22          Except as stated in paragraph 22A, a contract that will be settled by the entity (receiving or) delivering a\\\\n            fixed number of its own equity instruments in exchange for a fixed amount of cash or another financial asset\\\\n            is an equity instrument. For example, an issued share option that gives the counterparty a right to buy a\\\\n            fixed number of the entity’s shares for a fixed price or for a fixed stated principal amount of a bond is an\\\\n            equity instrument. Changes in the fair value of a contract arising from variations in market interest rates that\\\\n            do not affect the amount of cash or other financial assets to be paid or received, or the number of equity\\\\n            instruments to be received or delivered, on settlement of the contract do not preclude the contract from\\\\n            being an equity instrument. Any consideration received (such as the premium received for a written option\\\\n            or warrant on the entity’s own shares) is added directly to equity. Any consideration paid (such as the\\\\n            premium paid for a purchased option) is deducted directly from equity. Changes in the fair value of an\\\\n            equity instrument are not recognised in the financial statements.\\\\n22A         If the entity’s own equity instruments to be received, or delivered, by the entity upon settlement of a\\\\n            contract are puttable financial instruments with all the features and meeting the conditions described in\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n1    In this Standard, monetary amounts are denominated in ‘currency units (CU)’.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nAASB 132-compiled                                                   12                                            STANDARD\\\\n                                         Authorised Version F2023C00406 registered 04/05/2023\\\\n\\\\f        paragraphs 16A and 16B, or instruments that impose on the entity an obligation to deliver to another party a\\\\n        pro rata share of the net assets of the entity only on liquidation with all the features and meeting the\\\\n        conditions described in paragraphs 16C and 16D, the contract is a financial asset or a financial liability.\\\\n        This includes a contract that will be settled by the entity receiving or delivering a fixed number of such\\\\n        instruments in exchange for a fixed amount of cash or another financial asset.\\\\n23      With the exception of the circumstances described in paragraphs 16A and 16B or paragraphs 16C and 16D,\\\\n        a contract that contains an obligation for an entity to purchase its own equity instruments for cash or another\\\\n        financial asset gives rise to a financial liability for the present value of the redemption amount (for example,\\\\n        for the present value of the forward repurchase price, option exercise price or other redemption amount).\\\\n        This is the case even if the contract itself is an equity instrument. One example is an entity’s obligation\\\\n        under a forward contract to purchase its own equity instruments for cash. The financial liability is\\\\n        recognised initially at the present value of the redemption amount, and is reclassified from equity.\\\\n        Subsequently, the financial liability is measured in accordance with AASB 9. If the contract expires without\\\\n        delivery, the carrying amount of the financial liability is reclassified to equity. An entity’s contractual\\\\n        obligation to purchase its own equity instruments gives rise to a financial liability for the present value of\\\\n        the redemption amount even if the obligation to purchase is conditional on the counterparty exercising a\\\\n        right to redeem (eg a written put option that gives the counterparty the right to sell an entity’s own equity\\\\n        instruments to the entity for a fixed price).\\\\n24      A contract that will be settled by the entity delivering or receiving a fixed number of its own equity\\\\n        instruments in exchange for a variable amount of cash or another financial asset is a financial asset or\\\\n        financial liability. An example is a contract for the entity to deliver 100 of its own equity instruments in\\\\n        return for an amount of cash calculated to equal the value of 100 ounces of gold.\\\\n\\\\n        Contingent settlement provisions\\\\n25      A financial instrument may require the entity to deliver cash or another financial asset, or otherwise to settle\\\\n        it in such a way that it would be a financial liability, in the event of the occurrence or non-occurrence of\\\\n        uncertain future events (or on the outcome of uncertain circumstances) that are beyond the control of both\\\\n        the issuer and the holder of the instrument, such as a change in a stock market index, consumer price index,\\\\n        interest rate or taxation requirements, or the issuer’s future revenues, net income or debt-to-equity ratio. The\\\\n        issuer of such an instrument does not have the unconditional right to avoid delivering cash or another\\\\n        financial asset (or otherwise to settle it in such a way that it would be a financial liability). Therefore, it is a\\\\n        financial liability of the issuer unless:\\\\n        (a)        the part of the contingent settlement provision that could require settlement in cash or another\\\\n                   financial asset (or otherwise in such a way that it would be a financial liability) is not genuine;\\\\n        (b)        the issuer can be required to settle the obligation in cash or another financial asset (or otherwise\\\\n                   to settle it in such a way that it would be a financial liability) only in the event of liquidation of\\\\n                   the issuer; or\\\\n        (c)        the instrument has all the features and meets the conditions in paragraphs 16A and 16B.\\\\n\\\\n        Settlement options\\\\n26      When a derivative financial instrument gives one party a choice over how it is settled (eg the issuer or\\\\n        the holder can choose settlement net in cash or by exchanging shares for cash), it is a financial asset\\\\n        or a financial liability unless all of the settlement alternatives would result in it being an equity\\\\n        instrument.\\\\n27      An example of a derivative financial instrument with a settlement option that is a financial liability is a\\\\n        share option that the issuer can decide to settle net in cash or by exchanging its own shares for cash.\\\\n        Similarly, some contracts to buy or sell a non-financial item in exchange for the entity’s own equity\\\\n        instruments are within the scope of this Standard because they can be settled either by delivery of the non-\\\\n        financial item or net in cash or another financial instrument (see paragraphs 8–10). Such contracts are\\\\n        financial assets or financial liabilities and not equity instruments.\\\\n\\\\n        Compound financial instruments (see also paragraphs AG30–\\\\n        AG35 and Illustrative Examples 9–12)\\\\n28      The issuer of a non-derivative financial instrument shall evaluate the terms of the financial\\\\n        instrument to determine whether it contains both a liability and an equity component. Such\\\\n        components shall be classified separately as financial liabilities, financial assets or equity instruments\\\\n        in accordance with paragraph 15.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nAASB 132-compiled                                          13                                                STANDARD\\\\n                                  Authorised Version F2023C00406 registered 04/05/2023\\\\n\\\\f29      An entity recognises separately the components of a financial instrument that (a) creates a financial liability\\\\n        of the entity and (b) grants an option to the holder of the instrument to convert it into an equity instrument\\\\n        of the entity. For example, a bond or similar instrument convertible by the holder into a fixed number of\\\\n        ordinary shares of the entity is a compound financial instrument. From the perspective of the entity, such an\\\\n        instrument comprises two components: a financial liability (a contractual arrangement to deliver cash or\\\\n        another financial asset) and an equity instrument (a call option granting the holder the right, for a specified\\\\n        period of time, to convert it into a fixed number of ordinary shares of the entity). The economic effect of\\\\n        issuing such an instrument is substantially the same as issuing simultaneously a debt instrument with an\\\\n        early settlement provision and warrants to purchase ordinary shares, or issuing a debt instrument with\\\\n        detachable share purchase warrants. Accordingly, in all cases, the entity presents the liability and equity\\\\n        components separately in its statement of financial position.\\\\n30      Classification of the liability and equity components of a convertible instrument is not revised as a result of\\\\n        a change in the likelihood that a conversion option will be exercised, even when exercise of the option may\\\\n        appear to have become economically advantageous to some holders. Holders may not always act in the way\\\\n        that might be expected because, for example, the tax consequences resulting from conversion may differ\\\\n        among holders. Furthermore, the likelihood of conversion will change from time to time. The entity’s\\\\n        contractual obligation to make future payments remains outstanding until it is extinguished through\\\\n        conversion, maturity of the instrument or some other transaction.\\\\n31      AASB 9 deals with the measurement of financial assets and financial liabilities. Equity instruments are\\\\n        instruments that evidence a residual interest in the assets of an entity after deducting all of its liabilities.\\\\n        Therefore, when the initial carrying amount of a compound financial instrument is allocated to its equity\\\\n        and liability components, the equity component is assigned the residual amount after deducting from the fair\\\\n        value of the instrument as a whole the amount separately determined for the liability component. The value\\\\n        of any derivative features (such as a call option) embedded in the compound financial instrument other than\\\\n        the equity component (such as an equity conversion option) is included in the liability component. The sum\\\\n        of the carrying amounts assigned to the liability and equity components on initial recognition is always\\\\n        equal to the fair value that would be ascribed to the instrument as a whole. No gain or loss arises from\\\\n        initially recognising the components of the instrument separately.\\\\n32      Under the approach described in paragraph 31, the issuer of a bond convertible into ordinary shares first\\\\n        determines the carrying amount of the liability component by measuring the fair value of a similar liability\\\\n        (including any embedded non-equity derivative features) that does not have an associated equity\\\\n        component. The carrying amount of the equity instrument represented by the option to convert the\\\\n        instrument into ordinary shares is then determined by deducting the fair value of the financial liability from\\\\n        the fair value of the compound financial instrument as a whole.\\\\n\\\\n        Treasury shares (see also paragraph AG36)\\\\n33      If an entity reacquires its own equity instruments, those instruments (‘treasury shares’) shall be\\\\n        deducted from equity. No gain or loss shall be recognised in profit or loss on the purchase, sale, issue\\\\n        or cancellation of an entity’s own equity instruments. Such treasury shares may be acquired and held\\\\n        by the entity or by other members of the consolidated group. Consideration paid or received shall be\\\\n        recognised directly in equity.\\\\n33A     Some entities operate, either internally or externally, an investment fund that provides investors with\\\\n        benefits determined by units in the fund and recognise financial liabilities for the amounts to be paid to\\\\n        those investors. Similarly, some entities issue groups of insurance contracts with direct participation\\\\n        features and those entities hold the underlying items. Some such funds or underlying items include the\\\\n        entity’s treasury shares. Despite paragraph 33, an entity may elect not to deduct from equity a treasury share\\\\n      classification of an instrument. This exception is not extended to the classification of non-controlling\\\\n      interests in the consolidated financial statements. Therefore, instruments classified as equity instruments in\\\\n      accordance with either paragraphs 16A and 16B or paragraphs 16C and 16D in the separate or individual\\\\n      financial statements that are non-controlling interests are classified as liabilities in the consolidated financial\\\\n      statements of the group.\\\\n\\\\n          Compound financial instruments (paragraphs 28–32)\\\\nAG30      Paragraph 28 applies only to issuers of non-derivative compound financial instruments. Paragraph 28 does\\\\n          not deal with compound financial instruments from the perspective of holders. AASB 9 deals with the\\\\n          classification and measurement of financial assets that are compound financial instruments from the\\\\n          holder’s perspective.\\\\nAG31      A common form of compound financial instrument is a debt instrument with an embedded conversion\\\\n          option, such as a bond convertible into ordinary shares of the issuer, and without any other embedded\\\\n          derivative features. Paragraph 28 requires the issuer of such a financial instrument to present the liability\\\\n          component and the equity component separately in the statement of financial position, as follows:\\\\n          (a)       The issuer’s obligation to make scheduled payments of interest and principal is a financial\\\\n                    liability that exists as long as the instrument is not converted. On initial recognition, the fair value\\\\n                    of the liability component is the present value of the contractually determined stream of future\\\\n                    cash flows discounted at the rate of interest applied at that time by the market to instruments of\\\\n                    comparable credit status and providing substantially the same cash flows, on the same terms, but\\\\n                    without the conversion option.\\\\n          (b)       The equity instrument is an embedded option to convert the liability into equity of the issuer. This\\\\n                    option has value on initial recognition even when it is out of the money.\\\\nAG32      On conversion of a convertible instrument at maturity, the entity derecognises the liability component and\\\\n          recognises it as equity. The original equity component remains as equity (although it may be transferred\\\\n          from one line item within equity to another). There is no gain or loss on conversion at maturity.\\\\nAG33      When an entity extinguishes a convertible instrument before maturity through an early redemption or\\\\n          repurchase in which the original conversion privileges are unchanged, the entity allocates the consideration\\\\n          paid and any transaction costs for the repurchase or redemption to the liability and equity components of the\\\\n          instrument at the date of the transaction. The method used in allocating the consideration paid and\\\\n          transaction costs to the separate components is consistent with that used in the original allocation to the\\\\n          separate components of the proceeds received by the entity when the convertible instrument was issued, in\\\\n          accordance with paragraphs 28–32.\\\\nAG34      Once the allocation of the consideration is made, any resulting gain or loss is treated in accordance with\\\\n          accounting principles applicable to the related component, as follows:\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nAASB 132-compiled                                            25                                               GUIDANCE\\\\n                                    Authorised Version F2023C00406 registered 04/05/2023\\\\n\\\\f          (a)         the amount of gain or loss relating to the liability component is recognised in profit or loss; and\\\\n          (b)         the amount of consideration relating to the equity component is recognised in equity.\\\\nAG35      An entity may amend the terms of a convertible instrument to induce early conversion, for example by\\\\n          offering a more favourable conversion ratio or paying other additional consideration in the event of\\\\n          conversion before a specified date. The difference, at the date the terms are amended, between the fair value\\\\n          of the consideration the holder receives on conversion of the instrument under the revised terms and the fair\\\\n          value of the consideration the holder would have received under the original terms is recognised as a loss in\\\\n          profit or loss.\\\\n\\\\n          Treasury shares (paragraphs 33–34)\\\\nAG36      An entity’s own equity instruments are not recognised as a financial asset regardless of the reason for which\\\\n          they are reacquired. Paragraph 33 requires an entity that reacquires its own equity instruments to deduct\\\\n          those equity instruments from equity (but see also paragraph 33A). However, when an entity holds its own\\\\n          equity on behalf of others, eg a financial institution holding its own equity on behalf of a client, there is an\\\\n          agency relationship and as a result those holdings are not included in the entity’s statement of financial\\\\n          position.\\\\n\\\\n          Interest, dividends, losses and gains (paragraphs 35–41)\\\\nAG37      The following example illustrates the application of paragraph 35 to a compound financial instrument.\\\\n          Assume that a non-cumulative preference share is mandatorily redeemable for cash in five years, but that\\\\n          dividends are payable at the discretion of the entity before the redemption date. Such an instrument is a\\\\n          compound financial instrument, with the liability component being the present value of the redemption\\\\n          amount. The unwinding of the discount on this component is recognised in profit or loss and classified as\\\\n          interest expense. Any dividends paid relate to the equity component and, accordingly, are recognised as a\\\\n          distribution of profit or loss. A similar treatment would apply if the redemption was not mandatory but at\\\\n          the option of the holder, or if the share was mandatorily convertible into a variable number of ordinary\\\\n          shares calculated to equal a fixed amount or an amount based on changes in an underlying variable (eg\\\\n          commodity). However, if any unpaid dividends are added to the redemption amount, the entire instrument is\\\\n          a liability. In such a case, any dividends are classified as interest expense.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_10\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n 'event|payoff|state transition|Risk|risk factor' docs/design/research/standards/actus-techspecs.tex | head -25\\\\nsed -n '1,65p' MISSION_CONTROL.md\\\\nrg --files /home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies\\\\nsed -n '1,55p' scripts/check_accounting_p06.py\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_10\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n 'event|payoff|state transition|Risk|risk factor' docs/design/research/standards/actus-techspecs.tex | head -25\\\\nsed -n '1,65p' MISSION_CONTROL.md\\\\nrg --files /home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies\\\\nsed -n '1,55p' scripts/check_accounting_p06.py\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"141:\\\\\\\\newcommand{\\\\\\\\payoff}[2]{F(#1,#2)}\\\\n268:In this document, we provide the technical specification of the ACTUS standards or the mathematical description of financial contracts, in other words. We start by providing some basic notations used throughout the document followed by an introduction of the generic functions upon which financial contracts build. We continue in the following sections with an introduction of some additional foundational concepts \\\\\\\\textit{Composition}, and \\\\\\\\textit{Risk Factor Observer} and \\\\\\\\textit{Child Contract Observer}. Finally, we define the various ACTUS contracts in the last section.\\\\n304:$t_0$ represents \\\\\\\\attr{SD} of a contract and marks the time as per which the terms and implied state of a contract is represented. In general, from the contractual logic we are able to derive any contractual events and resulting states for any time $t>t_0$ but not for times $s<t_0$.\\\\n311:In general, states represent certain terms of a contract that change along the contract lifetime according to either scheduled events or unscheduled events. Therefore, states representing a contractual term carry the exact same names as their term-counterpart.\\\\n320:\\\\\\\\subsection{Contract Events}\\\\\\\\label{sec:events}\\\\n322:A Contract Event (event) $e_t^k$ refers to any contractually scheduled or unscheduled event at a certain time $t$ and of a certain type $k$. Contract events mark specific points in time during the lifetime of a contract at which a cash flow is being exchanged (see section \\\\\\\\ref{sec:pof}) or the states of the contract are being updated (see section \\\\\\\\ref{sec:stf}). The dictionary lists and describes all the event types $k$ defined by the ACTUS standards (\\\\\\\\url{https://github.com/actusfrf/actus-dictionary/blob/master/actus-dictionary-event-types.json}). Throughout this document event types $k$ are written in the short form as defined in the dictionary.\\\\n324:As an event always has an associated event time $t$ and payoff $c\\\\\\\\in\\\\\\\\Real$ we define two operators allowing to retrieve these quantities for any single event $e_t^k$ or set of events $\\\\\\\\{e_t^k,e_s^j, ...\\\\\\\\}$ as follows;\\\\n336:The \\\\\\\\textit{Initial Exchange Date} event with event time $s$ is written as $e_s^{IED}$ with $\\\\\\\\tev{e_s^{IED}}=s$ and $\\\\\\\\fev{e_s^{IED}}=c$ where for any contract \\\\\\\\attr{CT} $c=\\\\\\\\pof{IED}{\\\\\\\\attr{CT}}$.\\\\n342:State Transition Functions (STF) define the transition of states from a pre-event to a post-event state when a certain event $e_t^{k}$ applies. Thereby, the pre-event and post-event times are indexed with $t^-$ and $t^+$, respectively. \\\\n344:These functions are specific to a certain event and contract. STFs are written according to the following pattern \\\\\\\\stf{[event type]}{[contract type]} where [event type] and [contract type] refer to the respective event type and contract to which the STF belongs.\\\\n347:The STF for an IP event and PAM contract is written as \\\\\\\\stf{IP}{PAM} and maps e.g. state \\\\\\\\textit{Accrued Interest} from a pre-event state $\\\\\\\\svar{Ipac}{t^-}$ to post-event state $\\\\\\\\svar{Ipac}{t^+}$.\\\\n353:Payoff Functions (POF) define how the cash flow $c\\\\\\\\in\\\\\\\\Real$ for a certain event $e_t^k$ is being derived from current states and from the contract terms. If necessary, the resulting cash flow can be indexed with the event time $c_t$. These functions are specific to a certain event and contract. POFs are written according to the following pattern \\\\\\\\pof{[event type]}{[contract type]} where [event type] and [contract type] refer to the respective event and contract to which the STF belongs.\\\\n356:The POF for an IP event $e_t^{IP}$ and PAM contract is written as \\\\\\\\pof{IP}{PAM} with $\\\\\\\\fev{e_t^{IP}}=\\\\\\\\pof{IP}{PAM}$.\\\\n373:\\\\\\\\subsection{Event Sequence}\\\\\\\\label{sec:eventseq}\\\\n375:Contract Events of different types may occur at the same time, i.e. exactly the same point in time. In this case, the sequence of evaluating their STF and POF is decisive for the resulting cash flows and state transitions. Hence, we use an event sequence indicator that can be found for each event in the event-dictionary and implies the order of executing different events at the exact same time.\\\\n384:Note that $PR^*$ refers to the PR event of a maturity contract after which \\\\\\\\textbf{Nt}=0.0 (i.e. at which the remaining outstanding principal is redeemed). Further, \\\\\\\\attr{MD}, \\\\\\\\attr{AMD}, and PR(\\\\\\\\textbf{Nt}=0.0) in the definition above do only apply for maturity contracts but have to be considered infinity in all other cases. Similarly, \\\\\\\\attr{STD} only applies for certain contracts and is considered infinity for all others. Finally, $\\\\\\\\tmax$ is a parameter that may be used to restrict the considered lifetime in an analysis. In particular, this parameter is used for contracts that do not have a \\\\\\\\textit{natural} end to their lifetime such as STK.\\\\n403:with $t_i<t_{i+1}, i=1,2,...$. While the schedule function can be used to create arbitrary sequences of times, it is usually used to generate sequences of cyclic events $\\\\\\\\vec{t}^k$ of a certain type $k$, e.g. $k=IP$ for interest payment events (see dictionary for a list of all events https://github.com/actusfrf/actus-dictionary/blob/master/actus-dictionary-event.json) and the following build inputs to the function\\\\n406:\\\\t\\\\\\\\item[$s$] $=k\\\\\\\\attr{ANX}$ with $k\\\\\\\\attr{ANX}$ attribute cycle anchor date of event type $k$\\\\n408:\\\\t\\\\\\\\item[$c$] $=k\\\\\\\\attr{CL}$ with $k\\\\\\\\attr{CL}$ event type $k$'s schedule cycle\\\\n476:In general, contract events are scheduled for business days only. Therefore, the \\\\\\\\attr{BDC} convention defines how scheduled times $t_i,i=1,2,...,n-1$ are shifted in case they fall on a non-business day:\\\\n481:\\\\t\\\\\\\\item[SCF:] Shift/Calculate following: The event is shifted to the following non working day. Calculation of the event happens after the shift\\\\n483:\\\\t\\\\\\\\item[SCMF:] Shift/Calculate modified following: The event is shifted to the following non working day. However, if the following day happens to fall into the next month, then take preceeding non-working day. Calculation of the event happens after the shift\\\\n485:\\\\t\\\\\\\\item[CSF:] Calculate/Shift following: Same like SCF however calculation of the event happens before the shift\\\\n487:\\\\t\\\\\\\\item[CSMF:] Calculate/Shift modified following: Same like SCMF however calculation of the event happens before the shift\\\\n489:\\\\t\\\\\\\\item[SCP:] Shift/Calculate preceding: The event is shifted to the last preceding non working day. Calculation of the event happens after the shift\\\\n# AccDSL mission control\\\\n\\\\nEstablished 2 October 2026 (Asia/Hong_Kong) at the user's request.\\\\nStatus: active mission; Version 1.2 is a repaired design candidate with checked\\\\nreference cases. Full product, domain and human acceptance remain pending.\\\\n\\\\n## Purpose\\\\n\\\\nDesign a system that represents a company's historical financial disclosures,\\\\npreserves economically different histories and interpretations compatible with\\\\nthe evidence, and carries those alternatives into scenario-dependent future\\\\njournals and financial statements. Preserve their separate conditional outcome\\\\ndistributions or feasible sets, including uncertainty that cannot be assigned\\\\ndefensible probabilities.\\\\n\\\\nThe immediate deliverable is a detailed, readable LaTeX product and method\\\\ndesign, with compiled PDF, supporting literature and software investigation,\\\\nprecise implementation contracts and acceptance examples. The eventual product\\\\nis the working representation and simulation engine. A document build, a small\\\\nfinancing example and an implemented prototype are different achievements.\\\\n\\\\n## Authority and origin\\\\n\\\\nThis mission records the user's existing directions; it does not replace new\\\\nuser instructions or higher-priority instructions. The three original requests\\\\nare preserved in saved session `01a0f8e0-0c0b-7332-8f7e-d6b93ce32761`, at JSONL\\\\nrecords 10, 115 and 145. They establish whole-company history, heterogeneous\\\\naccounting, preservation of alternative journals/outcomes, a broad literature\\\\nand software survey, and an implementation-governing LaTeX document. The current\\\\nrequest establishes this durable mission and a requirements-based gap audit.\\\\n\\\\nThe user's subsequent direction establishes MC35: complete feasible internal\\\\npreparation before paying for professional review. The user supplied a planning\\\\nrate of US$500–1,200/hour. This work order is binding; no estimated savings or\\\\nprofessional engagement is inferred from it.\\\\n\\\\nThe [requirements register](docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md)\\\\ndistinguishes direct user requirements from policy obligations and engineering\\\\nrequirements derived from those goals. Python, storage engines, parser design,\\\\nsolver libraries and a particular first-company example remain replaceable\\\\nimplementation proposals. Designing a DSL is part of the work; claiming it is\\\\nbetter than all alternatives is not a predetermined conclusion.\\\\n\\\\n## Main goals\\\\n\\\\n| Goal | Required outcome |\\\\n| --- | --- |\\\\n| M1 — Represent the historical record | Preserve annual, quarterly and semi-annual statements, notes, policies and relevant referenced disclosures, with their source, context, temporal meaning and unresolved content. |\\\\n| M2 — Preserve alternative explanations | Represent joint families of admissible histories, journal movements, contract states and interpretations; distinguish absent facts, accounting choices, estimates and future randomness. |\\\\n| M3 — Simulate financial evolution | Apply explicit economic scenarios and behaviour to economic state, generate admissible journal entries, and produce coherent future statements and conditional results. |\\\\n| M4 — Handle accounting and sector diversity | Accommodate IFRS, US GAAP and China GAAP/ASBE, industry and company differences, group boundaries, banks, insurers, liabilities, capital, bonds and equity. |\\\\n| M5 — Specify implementable methods and language | Define reconstruction, accounting, inference and execution procedures, types, IR, DSL, interfaces, failure behaviour and persistence precisely enough for compatible implementations. |\\\\n| M6 — Ground choices in research and reusable tools | Inspect primary literature beyond the existing collection and official software, archive relevant sources, compare credible alternatives and document justified inclusion/exclusion and reuse decisions. |\\\\n| M7 — Deliver the governing design | Produce one rigorous, understandable LaTeX/PDF argument with complete worked cases, explicit scope, source support, method details and an implementation sequence. |\\\\n| M8 — Establish evidence and maintain direction | Define conformance and release evidence, preserve reproducibility, keep engineering/accounting/scientific conclusions separate, and maintain requirements and open decisions as work proceeds. |\\\\n\\\\n## Requirements that must survive every implementation choice\\\\n\\\\n1. Source preservation is broader than numerical extraction. Account for all\\\\n   source material within the declared disclosure package, including notes and\\\\n   cross-references. Content that cannot yet be formalised stays visible with\\\\n   a reason; it is not silently excluded from a completeness claim.\\\\n2. Preserve reported assertions, derived consequences and modelling assumptions\\\\n   separately. A missing value is not zero; a reported number is not automatic\\\\n   proof of the underlying economic state. Source conflicts remain inspectable.\\\\n/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/global-scientific-coding-agent-policy.md\\\\n/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/humanizer-ai-writing-patterns.md\\\\n/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/scholarly-literature-audit-policy.md\\\\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Execute P06 deterministic checks and write conformance/result evidence.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\\\n\\\\nimport argparse\\\\nfrom collections import Counter\\\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\\\\nfrom fractions import Fraction\\\\nimport hashlib\\\\nimport io\\\\nimport json\\\\nimport os\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\nimport platform\\\\nimport shlex\\\\nimport subprocess\\\\nimport sys\\\\nimport time\\\\nimport unittest\\\\n\\\\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\\\nDEFAULT_RUN = \\\\\\\"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P06\\\\\\\"\\\\nSOURCES = [\\\\n    \\\\\\\"scripts/context_chronology_v1.py\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"scripts/check_accounting_p06.py\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"tests/test_accounting_p06.py\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"docs/design/spec/context-chronology-profile-v1.md\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"docs/design/fixtures/p06-context-chronology-cases-v1.json\\\\\\\",\\\\n]\\\\nOUTPUTS = [\\\\\\\"data/accounting-master/deliverables/P06/conformance.json\\\\\\\",\\\\n           \\\\\\\"data/accounting-master/deliverables/P06/result.md\\\\\\\"]\\\\nWRITABLE = set(SOURCES + OUTPUTS + [\\\\\\\"data/accounting-master/deliverables/P06/progress.md\\\\\\\"])\\\\nOBLIGATIONS = [\\\\\\\"MC02\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"MC05\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"MC06\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"MC07\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"MC10\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"MC11\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"MC14\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"YTD\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"APPROXIMATION\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef digest(path: Path) -> str | None:\\\\n    try:\\\\n        return hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\\\\n    except OSError:\\\\n        return None\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef unique_object(pairs):\\\\n    result = {}\\\\n    for key, value in pairs:\\\\n        if key in result:\\\\n            raise ValueError(\\\\\\\"duplicate key: \\\\\\\" + key)\\\\n        result[key] = value\\\\n    return result\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef inventory(root: Path, relative: str) -> dict[str, str]:\\\\n    path = Path(relative)\\\\n    if path.is_absolute() or \\\\\\\"..\\\\\\\" in path.parts or path.as_posix() != relative:\\\\n        raise ValueError(\\\\\\\"inventory path must be repository-relative\\\\\\\")\\\\n    data = json.loads((root / path).read_text(), object_pairs_hook=unique_object)\\\\n    if not isinstance(data, dict) or not data:\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_11\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\\\nimport urllib.request,pathlib,json,datetime,hashlib\\\\nu='https://kjs.mof.gov.cn/zhengcefabu/201704/t20170406_2579238.htm'\\\\nr={'id':'mof22_candidate','url':u,'retrieved_at':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat()}\\\\np=pathlib.Path('docs/design/research/p08-v1')\\\\ntry:\\\\n with urllib.request.urlopen(u,timeout=20) as f:b=f.read();r.update(status=f.status,final_url=f.url)\\\\n (p/'mof22_candidate.html').write_bytes(b);r.update(path=str(p/'mof22_candidate.html'),sha256=hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest());print(b.decode('utf8','replace')[:250])\\\\nexcept Exception as e:r.update(access_status='unavailable',error=str(e))\\\\na=json.loads((p/'access-records.json').read_text());a.append(r);(p/'access-records.json').write_text(json.dumps(a,indent=2)+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n');print(r)\\\\nPY\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_12\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"pdftotext -layout docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb9.pdf docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb9.txt\\\\npdftotext -layout docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb7.pdf docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb7.txt\\\\nrg -n '3.1.1 |3.3.1 |3.3.3 |4.2.1 |5.1.1 |effective interest method|amortised cost of|before 1 July' docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb9.txt | head -24\\\\nrg -n '\\\\\\\"'^7 |''^8 |''^20 |before 1 July|Tier 1'\\\\\\\"' docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb7.txt | head -15\\\\nsed -n '660,713p' docs/design/research/standards/aasb132.txt\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_12\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"pdftotext -layout docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb9.pdf docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb9.txt\\\\npdftotext -layout docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb7.pdf docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb7.txt\\\\nrg -n '3.1.1 |3.3.1 |3.3.3 |4.2.1 |5.1.1 |effective interest method|amortised cost of|before 1 July' docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb9.txt | head -24\\\\nrg -n '\\\\\\\"'^7 |''^8 |''^20 |before 1 July|Tier 1'\\\\\\\"' docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb7.txt | head -15\\\\nsed -n '660,713p' docs/design/research/standards/aasb132.txt\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"7:This compiled Standard applies to annual periods beginning on or after 1 January 2023 but before 1 July 2026.\\\\n215:This compiled version of AASB 9 applies to annual periods beginning on or after 1 January 2023 but before 1 July\\\\n284:                            requirements in paragraph 3.3.1 of this Standard; and\\\\n424:3.1.1   An entity shall recognise a financial asset or a financial liability in its statement of financial position\\\\n426:        paragraphs B3.1.1 and B3.1.2). When an entity first recognises a financial asset, it shall classify it in\\\\n429:        paragraphs 4.2.1 and 4.2.2 and measure it in accordance with paragraph 5.1.1.\\\\n630:         (a)       the amortised cost of the rights and obligations retained by the entity, if the transferred\\\\n680:3.3.1    An entity shall remove a financial liability (or a part of a financial liability) from its statement of\\\\n689:3.3.3    The difference between the carrying amount of a financial liability (or part of a financial liability)\\\\n766:4.2.1   An entity shall classify all financial liabilities as subsequently measured at amortised cost, except for:\\\\n877:5.1.1      Except for trade receivables within the scope of paragraph 5.1.3, at initial recognition, an entity shall\\\\n914:5.4.1      Interest revenue shall be calculated by using the effective interest method (see Appendix A and\\\\n918:                        shall apply the credit-adjusted effective interest rate to the amortised cost of the financial asset\\\\n933:                  entity shall apply the effective interest rate to the amortised cost of the financial asset in\\\\n935:5.4.2   An entity that, in a reporting period, calculates interest revenue by applying the effective interest method to\\\\n936:        the amortised cost of a financial asset in accordance with paragraph 5.4.1(b), shall, in subsequent reporting\\\\n1267:         Interest calculated using the effective interest method is recognised in profit or loss.\\\\n2093:                     presented as the gross carrying amount of that financial asset or the amortised cost of that\\\\n2096:                     new gross carrying amount of that financial asset or the new amortised cost of that financial\\\\n2411:amortised cost of a financial    The amount at which the financial asset or financial liability is measured at initial\\\\n2413:                                 amortisation using the effective interest method of any difference between that\\\\n2457:interest rate                    through the expected life of the financial asset to the amortised cost of a\\\\n2495:effective interest method      The method that is used in the calculation of the amortised cost of a financial\\\\n2501:                               amount of a financial asset or to the amortised cost of a financial liability.\\\\n7:This compiled Standard applies to annual periods beginning on or after 1 January 2023 but before 1 July 2026.\\\\n158:Tier 1\\\\n173:This compiled version of AASB 7 applies to annual periods beginning on or after 1 January 2023 but before 1 July\\\\n276:7        An entity shall disclose information that enables users of its financial statements to evaluate the\\\\n286:8       The carrying amounts of each of the following categories, as specified in AASB 9, shall be disclosed either\\\\n494:20      An entity shall disclose the following items of income, expense, gains or losses either in the statement of\\\\n2124:This compiled Standard applies to annual periods beginning on or after 1 January 2023 but before 1 July 2026. It takes\\\\n2152:      annual periods beginning on or after 1 January 2023 but before 1 July 2026.\\\\n2162:(f)   Entities may elect to apply this Standard to annual periods beginning before 1 July 2021.\\\\n2174:8                                            amended                                     AASB 17 [page 72]\\\\n        financial assets or financial liabilities and not equity instruments.\\\\n\\\\n        Compound financial instruments (see also paragraphs AG30–\\\\n        AG35 and Illustrative Examples 9–12)\\\\n28      The issuer of a non-derivative financial instrument shall evaluate the terms of the financial\\\\n        instrument to determine whether it contains both a liability and an equity component. Such\\\\n        components shall be classified separately as financial liabilities, financial assets or equity instruments\\\\n        in accordance with paragraph 15.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nAASB 132-compiled                                          13                                                STANDARD\\\\n                                  Authorised Version F2023C00406 registered 04/05/2023\\\\n\\\\f29      An entity recognises separately the components of a financial instrument that (a) creates a financial liability\\\\n        of the entity and (b) grants an option to the holder of the instrument to convert it into an equity instrument\\\\n        of the entity. For example, a bond or similar instrument convertible by the holder into a fixed number of\\\\n        ordinary shares of the entity is a compound financial instrument. From the perspective of the entity, such an\\\\n        instrument comprises two components: a financial liability (a contractual arrangement to deliver cash or\\\\n        another financial asset) and an equity instrument (a call option granting the holder the right, for a specified\\\\n        period of time, to convert it into a fixed number of ordinary shares of the entity). The economic effect of\\\\n        issuing such an instrument is substantially the same as issuing simultaneously a debt instrument with an\\\\n        early settlement provision and warrants to purchase ordinary shares, or issuing a debt instrument with\\\\n        detachable share purchase warrants. Accordingly, in all cases, the entity presents the liability and equity\\\\n        components separately in its statement of financial position.\\\\n30      Classification of the liability and equity components of a convertible instrument is not revised as a result of\\\\n        a change in the likelihood that a conversion option will be exercised, even when exercise of the option may\\\\n        appear to have become economically advantageous to some holders. Holders may not always act in the way\\\\n        that might be expected because, for example, the tax consequences resulting from conversion may differ\\\\n        among holders. Furthermore, the likelihood of conversion will change from time to time. The entity’s\\\\n        contractual obligation to make future payments remains outstanding until it is extinguished through\\\\n        conversion, maturity of the instrument or some other transaction.\\\\n31      AASB 9 deals with the measurement of financial assets and financial liabilities. Equity instruments are\\\\n        instruments that evidence a residual interest in the assets of an entity after deducting all of its liabilities.\\\\n        Therefore, when the initial carrying amount of a compound financial instrument is allocated to its equity\\\\n        and liability components, the equity component is assigned the residual amount after deducting from the fair\\\\n        value of the instrument as a whole the amount separately determined for the liability component. The value\\\\n        of any derivative features (such as a call option) embedded in the compound financial instrument other than\\\\n        the equity component (such as an equity conversion option) is included in the liability component. The sum\\\\n        of the carrying amounts assigned to the liability and equity components on initial recognition is always\\\\n        equal to the fair value that would be ascribed to the instrument as a whole. No gain or loss arises from\\\\n        initially recognising the components of the instrument separately.\\\\n32      Under the approach described in paragraph 31, the issuer of a bond convertible into ordinary shares first\\\\n        determines the carrying amount of the liability component by measuring the fair value of a similar liability\\\\n        (including any embedded non-equity derivative features) that does not have an associated equity\\\\n        component. The carrying amount of the equity instrument represented by the option to convert the\\\\n        instrument into ordinary shares is then determined by deducting the fair value of the financial liability from\\\\n        the fair value of the compound financial instrument as a whole.\\\\n\\\\n        Treasury shares (see also paragraph AG36)\\\\n33      If an entity reacquires its own equity instruments, those instruments (‘treasury shares’) shall be\\\\n        deducted from equity. No gain or loss shall be recognised in profit or loss on the purchase, sale, issue\\\\n        or cancellation of an entity’s own equity instruments. Such treasury shares may be acquired and held\\\\n        by the entity or by other members of the consolidated group. Consideration paid or received shall be\\\\n        recognised directly in equity.\\\\n33A     Some entities operate, either internally or externally, an investment fund that provides investors with\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_11\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\\\nimport urllib.request,pathlib,json,datetime,hashlib\\\\nu='https://kjs.mof.gov.cn/zhengcefabu/201704/t20170406_2579238.htm'\\\\nr={'id':'mof22_candidate','url':u,'retrieved_at':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat()}\\\\np=pathlib.Path('docs/design/research/p08-v1')\\\\ntry:\\\\n with urllib.request.urlopen(u,timeout=20) as f:b=f.read();r.update(status=f.status,final_url=f.url)\\\\n (p/'mof22_candidate.html').write_bytes(b);r.update(path=str(p/'mof22_candidate.html'),sha256=hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest());print(b.decode('utf8','replace')[:250])\\\\nexcept Exception as e:r.update(access_status='unavailable',error=str(e))\\\\na=json.loads((p/'access-records.json').read_text());a.append(r);(p/'access-records.json').write_text(json.dumps(a,indent=2)+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n');print(r)\\\\nPY\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"{'id': 'mof22_candidate', 'url': 'https://kjs.mof.gov.cn/zhengcefabu/201704/t20170406_2579238.htm', 'retrieved_at': '2026-10-03T01:05:21.892559+00:00', 'access_status': 'unavailable', 'error': 'HTTP Error 502: Bad Gateway'}\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_13\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\ntext=Path('docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb9.txt').read_text()\\\\nfor start,end in [('3.1.1   An entity','3.1.2'),('3.3.1    An entity','3.3.4'),('4.2.1   An entity','4.2.2'),('5.1.1      Except','5.1.1A'),('amortised cost of a financial    The amount','contract assets'),('effective interest method      The method','fair value')]:\\\\n i=text.find(start);j=text.find(end,i+len(start));print('page',text[:i].count('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\f')+1, text[i:min(j,i+1450)] if i>=0 else 'missing '+start)\\\\nPY\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_13\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\ntext=Path('docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb9.txt').read_text()\\\\nfor start,end in [('3.1.1   An entity','3.1.2'),('3.3.1    An entity','3.3.4'),('4.2.1   An entity','4.2.2'),('5.1.1      Except','5.1.1A'),('amortised cost of a financial    The amount','contract assets'),('effective interest method      The method','fair value')]:\\\\n i=text.find(start);j=text.find(end,i+len(start));print('page',text[:i].count('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\f')+1, text[i:min(j,i+1450)] if i>=0 else 'missing '+start)\\\\nPY\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"page 10 3.1.1   An entity shall recognise a financial asset or a financial liability in its statement of financial position\\\\n        when, and only when, the entity becomes party to the contractual provisions of the instrument (see\\\\n        paragraphs B3.1.1 and B\\\\npage 14 3.3.1    An entity shall remove a financial liability (or a part of a financial liability) from its statement of\\\\n         financial position when, and only when, it is extinguished – ie when the obligation specified in the\\\\n         contract is discharged or cancelled or expires.\\\\n3.3.2    An exchange between an existing borrower and lender of debt instruments with substantially\\\\n         different terms shall be accounted for as an extinguishment of the original financial liability and the\\\\n         recognition of a new financial liability. Similarly, a substantial modification of the terms of an\\\\n         existing financial liability or a part of it (whether or not attributable to the financial difficulty of the\\\\n         debtor) shall be accounted for as an extinguishment of the original financial liability and the\\\\n         recognition of a new financial liability.\\\\n3.3.3    The difference between the carrying amount of a financial liability (or part of a financial liability)\\\\n         extinguished or transferred to another party and the consideration paid, including any non-cash\\\\n         assets transferred or liabilities assumed, shall be recognised in profit or loss.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nAASB 9-compiled                                            14                                           STANDARD\\\\n                                  Authorised Version F2023C00399 registered 02/05/2023\\\\n\\\\f\\\\npage 16 4.2.1   An entity shall classify all financial liabilities as subsequently measured at amortised cost, except for:\\\\n        (a)       financial liabilities at fair value through profit or loss. Such liabilities, including derivatives\\\\n                  that are liabilities, shall be subsequently measured at fair value.\\\\n        (b)       financial liabilities that arise when a transfer of a financial asset does not qualify for\\\\n                  derecognition or when the continuing involvement approach applies. Paragraphs 3.2.15 and\\\\n                  3.2.17 apply to the measurement of such financial liabilities.\\\\n        (c)       financial guarantee contracts. After initial recognition, an issuer of such a contract shall\\\\n                  (unless paragraph 4.2.1(a) or (b) applies) subsequently measure it at the higher of:\\\\n                  (i)        the amount of the loss allowance determined in accordance with Section 5.5 and\\\\n                  (ii)       the amount initially recognised (see paragraph 5.1.1) less, when appropriate, the\\\\n                             cumulative amount of income recognised in accordance with the principles of\\\\n                             AASB 15.\\\\n        (d)       commitments to provide a loan at a below-market interest rate. An issuer of such a\\\\n                  commitment shall (unless paragraph 4.2.1(a) applies) subsequently measure it at the higher\\\\n                  of:\\\\n                  (i)     \\\\npage 18 5.1.1      Except for trade receivables within the scope of paragraph 5.1.3, at initial recognition, an entity shall\\\\n           measure a financial asset or financial liability at its fair value plus or minus, in the case of a financial\\\\n           asset or financial liability not at fair value through profit or loss, transaction costs that are directly\\\\n           attributable to the acquisition or issue of the financial asset or financial liability.\\\\n\\\\npage 44 amortised cost of a financial    The amount at which the financial asset or financial liability is measured at initial\\\\nasset or financial liability     recognition minus the principal repayments, plus or minus the cumulative\\\\n                                 amortisation using the effective interest method of any difference between that\\\\n                                 initial amount and the maturity amount and, for financial assets, adjusted for any\\\\n                                 loss allowance.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\npage 45 effective interest method      The method that is used in the calculation of the amortised cost of a financial\\\\n                               asset or a financial liability and in the allocation and recognition of the interest\\\\n                               revenue or interest expense in profit or loss over the relevant period.\\\\n\\\\neffective interest rate        The rate that exactly discounts estimated future cash payments or receipts through\\\\n                               the expected life of the financial asset or financial liability to the gross carrying\\\\n                               amount of a financial asset or to the amortised cost of a financial liability.\\\\n                               When calculating the effective interest rate, an entity shall estimate the expected\\\\n                               cash flows by considering all the contractual terms of the financial instrument (for\\\\n                               example, prepayment, extension, call and similar options) but shall not consider\\\\n                               the expected credit losses. The calculation includes all fees and points paid or\\\\n                               received between parties to the contract that are an integral part of the effective\\\\n                               interest rate (see paragraphs B5.4.1–B5.4.3), transaction costs, and all other\\\\n                               premiums or discounts. There is a presumption that the cash flows a\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_14\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\\\nimport urllib.request,pathlib,json,datetime,hashlib\\\\nu='https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32023R1803'\\\\nr={'id':'eu2023_1803','url':u,'retrieved_at':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat()};p=pathlib.Path('docs/design/research/p08-v1')\\\\ntry:\\\\n with urllib.request.urlopen(u,timeout=25) as f:b=f.read();r.update(status=f.status,final_url=f.url)\\\\n (p/'eu2023_1803.html').write_bytes(b);r.update(path=str(p/'eu2023_1803.html'),sha256=hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest(),bytes=len(b))\\\\nexcept Exception as e:r.update(access_status='unavailable',error=str(e))\\\\n(p/'eu-access.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2)+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n');print(r)\\\\nPY\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_14\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\\\nimport urllib.request,pathlib,json,datetime,hashlib\\\\nu='https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32023R1803'\\\\nr={'id':'eu2023_1803','url':u,'retrieved_at':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat()};p=pathlib.Path('docs/design/research/p08-v1')\\\\ntry:\\\\n with urllib.request.urlopen(u,timeout=25) as f:b=f.read();r.update(status=f.status,final_url=f.url)\\\\n (p/'eu2023_1803.html').write_bytes(b);r.update(path=str(p/'eu2023_1803.html'),sha256=hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest(),bytes=len(b))\\\\nexcept Exception as e:r.update(access_status='unavailable',error=str(e))\\\\n(p/'eu-access.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2)+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n');print(r)\\\\nPY\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"{'id': 'eu2023_1803', 'url': 'https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32023R1803', 'retrieved_at': '2026-10-03T01:05:57.801400+00:00', 'status': 202, 'final_url': 'https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32023R1803', 'path': 'docs/design/research/p08-v1/eu2023_1803.html', 'sha256': 'e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855', 'bytes': 0}\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_15\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The applicable AASB 9 and AASB 7 texts are now retained. AASB 9 supplies the missing amortised-cost and effective-interest support. FASB returned 403, the Ministry of Finance route returned 502, and EUR-Lex returned no text; those routes provide no comparator authority. I’ll implement the supported Australian slice and record the comparison gaps explicitly.\\\\n\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_16\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\ns=Path('docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb9.txt').read_text().splitlines()\\\\nfor a,b in [(420,431),(765,794),(2492,2518)]: print('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n'.join(s[a:b]))\\\\ns=Path('docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb7.txt').read_text().splitlines()\\\\nfor a,b in [(274,306),(493,521),(150,164)]:print('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n'.join(s[a:b]))\\\\nPY\\\\nsed -n '306,323p' docs/design/research/standards/actus-techspecs.tex\\\\nsed -n '348,360p' docs/design/research/standards/actus-techspecs.tex\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_16\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\ns=Path('docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb9.txt').read_text().splitlines()\\\\nfor a,b in [(420,431),(765,794),(2492,2518)]: print('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n'.join(s[a:b]))\\\\ns=Path('docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb7.txt').read_text().splitlines()\\\\nfor a,b in [(274,306),(493,521),(150,164)]:print('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n'.join(s[a:b]))\\\\nPY\\\\nsed -n '306,323p' docs/design/research/standards/actus-techspecs.tex\\\\nsed -n '348,360p' docs/design/research/standards/actus-techspecs.tex\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"        accordingly, is within the scope of this Standard. Other contracts to which paragraph 2.4 applies are\\\\n        evaluated to determine whether they were entered into and continue to be held for the purpose of the receipt\\\\n        or delivery of the non-financial item in accordance with the entity’s expected purchase, sale or usage\\\\n        requirements and, accordingly, whether they are within the scope of this Standard.\\\\n2.7     A written option to buy or sell a non-financial item that can be settled net in cash or another financial\\\\n        instrument, or by exchanging financial instruments, in accordance with paragraph 2.6(a) or 2.6(d) is within\\\\n        the scope of this Standard. Such a contract cannot be entered into for the purpose of the receipt or delivery\\\\n        of the non-financial item in accordance with the entity’s expected purchase, sale or usage requirements.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nChapter 3 Recognition and derecognition\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nAASB 9-compiled                                            15                                              STANDARD\\\\n                                  Authorised Version F2023C00399 registered 02/05/2023\\\\n\\\\n        Option to designate a financial asset at fair value through profit or loss\\\\n4.1.5   Despite paragraphs 4.1.1–4.1.4, an entity may, at initial recognition, irrevocably designate a financial\\\\n        asset as measured at fair value through profit or loss if doing so eliminates or significantly reduces a\\\\n        measurement or recognition inconsistency (sometimes referred to as an ‘accounting mismatch’) that\\\\n        would otherwise arise from measuring assets or liabilities or recognising the gains and losses on them\\\\n        on different bases (see paragraphs B4.1.29–B4.1.32).\\\\n\\\\n4.2 Classification of financial liabilities\\\\n4.2.1   An entity shall classify all financial liabilities as subsequently measured at amortised cost, except for:\\\\n        (a)       financial liabilities at fair value through profit or loss. Such liabilities, including derivatives\\\\n                  that are liabilities, shall be subsequently measured at fair value.\\\\n        (b)       financial liabilities that arise when a transfer of a financial asset does not qualify for\\\\n                  derecognition or when the continuing involvement approach applies. Paragraphs 3.2.15 and\\\\n                  3.2.17 apply to the measurement of such financial liabilities.\\\\n        (c)       financial guarantee contracts. After initial recognition, an issuer of such a contract shall\\\\n                  (unless paragraph 4.2.1(a) or (b) applies) subsequently measure it at the higher of:\\\\n                  (i)        the amount of the loss allowance determined in accordance with Section 5.5 and\\\\n                  (ii)       the amount initially recognised (see paragraph 5.1.1) less, when appropriate, the\\\\n                             cumulative amount of income recognised in accordance with the principles of\\\\n                             AASB 15.\\\\n        (d)       commitments to provide a loan at a below-market interest rate. An issuer of such a\\\\n                  commitment shall (unless paragraph 4.2.1(a) applies) subsequently measure it at the higher\\\\n                                 collateral held or other credit enhancements that are integral to the contractual\\\\n                                 terms. There is a presumption that the expected life of a financial instrument can\\\\n                                 be estimated reliably. However, in those rare cases when it is not possible to\\\\n                                 reliably estimate the expected life of a financial instrument, the entity shall use the\\\\n                                 remaining contractual term of the financial instrument.\\\\n\\\\ncredit-adjusted effective        The rate that exactly discounts the estimated future cash payments or receipts\\\\ninterest rate                    through the expected life of the financial asset to the amortised cost of a\\\\n                                 financial asset that is a purchased or originated credit-impaired financial\\\\n                                 asset. When calculating the credit-adjusted effective interest rate, an entity shall\\\\n                                 estimate the expected cash flows by considering all contractual terms of the\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nAASB 9-compiled                                             44                                                APPENDIX A\\\\n                                   Authorised Version F2023C00399 registered 02/05/2023\\\\n\\\\n                               financial asset (for example, prepayment, extension, call and similar options) and\\\\n                               expected credit losses. The calculation includes all fees and points paid or\\\\n                               received between parties to the contract that are an integral part of the effective\\\\n                               interest rate (see paragraphs B5.4.1‒B5.4.3), transaction costs, and all other\\\\n                               premiums or discounts. There is a presumption that the cash flows and the\\\\n                               expected life of a group of similar financial instruments can be estimated reliably.\\\\n                               However, in those rare cases when it is not possible to reliably estimate the cash\\\\n                               flows or the remaining life of a financial instrument (or group of financial\\\\n                               instruments), the entity shall use the contractual cash flows over the full\\\\n         instruments into classes that are appropriate to the nature of the information disclosed and that take into\\\\n         account the characteristics of those financial instruments. An entity shall provide sufficient information to\\\\n         permit reconciliation to the line items presented in the statement of financial position.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nSignificance of financial instruments for financial position and\\\\nperformance\\\\n7        An entity shall disclose information that enables users of its financial statements to evaluate the\\\\n         significance of financial instruments for its financial position and performance.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nAASB 7-compiled                                            7                                              STANDARD\\\\n                                  Authorised Version F2023C00392 registered 01/05/2023\\\\n\\\\n        Statement of financial position\\\\n        Categories of financial assets and financial liabilities\\\\n8       The carrying amounts of each of the following categories, as specified in AASB 9, shall be disclosed either\\\\n        in the statement of financial position or in the notes:\\\\n        (a)       financial assets measured at fair value through profit or loss, showing separately (i) those\\\\n                  designated as such upon initial recognition or subsequently in accordance with paragraph 6.7.1 of\\\\n                  AASB 9; (ii) those measured as such in accordance with the election in paragraph 3.3.5 of\\\\n                  AASB 9; (iii) those measured as such in accordance with the election in paragraph 33A of\\\\n                  AASB 132 and (iv) those mandatorily measured at fair value through profit or loss in accordance\\\\n                  with AASB 9.\\\\n        (b)–(d)   [deleted]\\\\n        (e)       financial liabilities at fair value through profit or loss, showing separately (i) those designated as\\\\n                  such upon initial recognition or subsequently in accordance with paragraph 6.7.1 of AASB 9 and\\\\n                  (ii) those that meet the definition of held for trading in AASB 9.\\\\n        (f)       financial assets measured at amortised cost.\\\\n        (g)       financial liabilities measured at amortised cost.\\\\n        (b)         the carrying amount of the loans payable in default at the end of the reporting period; and\\\\n        (c)         whether the default was remedied, or the terms of the loans payable were renegotiated, before the\\\\n                    financial statements were authorised for issue.\\\\n19      If, during the period, there were breaches of loan agreement terms other than those described in\\\\n        paragraph 18, an entity shall disclose the same information as required by paragraph 18 if those breaches\\\\n        permitted the lender to demand accelerated repayment (unless the breaches were remedied, or the terms of\\\\n        the loan were renegotiated, on or before the end of the reporting period).\\\\n\\\\n        Statement of comprehensive income\\\\n        Items of income, expense, gains or losses\\\\n20      An entity shall disclose the following items of income, expense, gains or losses either in the statement of\\\\n        comprehensive income or in the notes:\\\\n        (a)         net gains or net losses on:\\\\n                    (i)        financial assets or financial liabilities measured at fair value through profit or loss,\\\\n                               showing separately those on financial assets or financial liabilities designated as such\\\\n                               upon initial recognition or subsequently in accordance with paragraph 6.7.1 of\\\\n                               AASB 9, and those on financial assets or financial liabilities that are mandatorily\\\\n                               measured at fair value through profit or loss in accordance with AASB 9 (eg financial\\\\n                               liabilities that meet the definition of held for trading in AASB 9). For financial\\\\n                               liabilities designated as at fair value through profit or loss, an entity shall show\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nAASB 7-compiled                                              11                                           STANDARD\\\\n                                    Authorised Version F2023C00392 registered 01/05/2023\\\\n\\\\n                              separately the amount of gain or loss recognised in other comprehensive income and\\\\n                              the amount recognised in profit or loss.\\\\n\\\\nAASB 7-compiled                                            4                                           CONTENTS\\\\n                                  Authorised Version F2023C00392 registered 01/05/2023\\\\n\\\\nComparison with IFRS 7\\\\nAASB 7 Financial Instruments: Disclosures as amended incorporates IFRS 7 Financial Instruments: Disclosures as\\\\nissued and amended by the International Accounting Standards Board (IASB). Australian-specific paragraphs (which\\\\nare not included in IFRS 7) are identified with the prefix “Aus”. Paragraphs that apply only to not-for-profit entities\\\\nbegin by identifying their limited applicability.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nTier 1\\\\nFor-profit entities complying with AASB 7 also comply with IFRS 7.\\\\nNot-for-profit entities’ compliance with IFRS 7 will depend on whether any “Aus” paragraphs that specifically apply\\\\n\\\\n\\\\\\\\subsection{State Variables}\\\\\\\\label{sec:statevarsnotat}\\\\n\\\\nState Variables (states) describe the state of a contract at a certain point in time $t$ during its lifetime. Examples of such states are the (outstanding) Notional Principal, the applicable Nominal Interest Rate, or the current Contract Performance. The ACTUS dictionary (\\\\\\\\url{https://github.com/actusfrf/actus-dictionary/blob/master/actus-dictionary-states.json}) defines all states and provides further information on their data type, format, etc.\\\\n\\\\nIn general, states represent certain terms of a contract that change along the contract lifetime according to either scheduled events or unscheduled events. Therefore, states representing a contractual term carry the exact same names as their term-counterpart.\\\\n\\\\nStates are written in their short form representation with first letter capitalized, printed in bold, and indexed with time.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\\\\\begin{example}[State Variables]\\\\n$\\\\\\\\svar{Nt}{t}$ refers to the state \\\\\\\\textit{Notional Principal} observed at time $t$.\\\\n\\\\\\\\end{example}\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\\\\\subsection{Contract Events}\\\\\\\\label{sec:events}\\\\n\\\\nA Contract Event (event) $e_t^k$ refers to any contractually scheduled or unscheduled event at a certain time $t$ and of a certain type $k$. Contract events mark specific points in time during the lifetime of a contract at which a cash flow is being exchanged (see section \\\\\\\\ref{sec:pof}) or the states of the contract are being updated (see section \\\\\\\\ref{sec:stf}). The dictionary lists and describes all the event types $k$ defined by the ACTUS standards (\\\\\\\\url{https://github.com/actusfrf/actus-dictionary/blob/master/actus-dictionary-event-types.json}). Throughout this document event types $k$ are written in the short form as defined in the dictionary.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\\\\\end{example}\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\\\\\subsection{Payoff Functions}\\\\\\\\label{sec:pof}\\\\n\\\\nPayoff Functions (POF) define how the cash flow $c\\\\\\\\in\\\\\\\\Real$ for a certain event $e_t^k$ is being derived from current states and from the contract terms. If necessary, the resulting cash flow can be indexed with the event time $c_t$. These functions are specific to a certain event and contract. POFs are written according to the following pattern \\\\\\\\pof{[event type]}{[contract type]} where [event type] and [contract type] refer to the respective event and contract to which the STF belongs.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\\\\\begin{example}[Payoff Functions]\\\\nThe POF for an IP event $e_t^{IP}$ and PAM contract is written as \\\\\\\\pof{IP}{PAM} with $\\\\\\\\fev{e_t^{IP}}=\\\\\\\\pof{IP}{PAM}$.\\\\n\\\\\\\\end{example}\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\\\\\subsection{Date/Time}\\\\\\\\label{sec:time}\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_17\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"cat > scripts/corporate_financing_v1.py <<'PY'\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Bounded, exact AASB issuer compound-bond lifecycle (P08).\\\\n\\\\nEligibility and fair value/yield inputs are explicit synthetic assumptions, not\\\\ninferred accounting opinions. Annual calendar periods only; no market model.\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\\\n\\\\nfrom copy import deepcopy\\\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\\\nfrom datetime import date\\\\nfrom fractions import Fraction\\\\nfrom hashlib import sha256\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\nimport json\\\\nimport re\\\\n\\\\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\\\nREGISTER = 'docs/design/research/p08-v1/authority-register.json'\\\\nREQUIRED = ('recognition', 'classification', 'split', 'measurement', 'interest',\\\\n            'redemption', 'conversion', 'note_carrying', 'note_interest')\\\\nACCOUNTS = ('cash', 'liability', 'conversion_equity', 'share_equity',\\\\n            'opening_equity', 'interest_expense')\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nclass Unsupported(ValueError):\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"A fact, source, or event is outside the explicitly supported slice.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef rational(value):\\\\n    if isinstance(value, (bool, float)) or not isinstance(value, (str, int, Fraction)):\\\\n        raise Unsupported('amounts and rates require exact integer/rational inputs')\\\\n    try:\\\\n        return Fraction(value)\\\\n    except (ValueError, ZeroDivisionError) as exc:\\\\n        raise Unsupported('invalid rational') from exc\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef iso(value):\\\\n    try:\\\\n        result = date.fromisoformat(value)\\\\n        if result.isoformat() \\\\\\\"'!= value:\\\\n            raise ValueError('\\\\\\\"'noncanonical date')\\\\n        return result\\\\n    except (ValueError, TypeError) as exc:\\\\n        raise Unsupported('canonical ISO date required') from exc\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef wire(value):\\\\n    if isinstance(value, Fraction):\\\\n        return str(value)\\\\n    if isinstance(value, dict):\\\\n        return {key: wire(val) for key, val in value.items()}\\\\n    if isinstance(value, (list, tuple)):\\\\n        return [wire(val) for val in value]\\\\n    return value\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef normal(value):\\\\n    return re.sub(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s+', ' ', value).strip()\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nclass AuthorityBook:\\\\n    def __init__(self, root=ROOT, records=None):\\\\n        self.root = Path(root)\\\\n        self.records = deepcopy(records) if records is not None else json.loads(\\\\n            (self.root / REGISTER).read_text())\\\\n        self.validate()\\\\n\\\\n    def validate(self):\\\\n        d = self.records\\\\n        if d.get('schema_version') \\\\\\\"'!= '\\\\\\\"'accdsl.p08.authority.v1':\\\\n            raise Unsupported('authority schema')\\\\n        self.sources = {r['id']: r for r in d['authorities']}\\\\n        self.claims = {r['id']: r for r in d['claims']}\\\\n        if len(self.sources) \\\\\\\"'!= len(d['\\\\\\\"'authorities']) or len(self.claims) \\\\\\\"'!= len(d['\\\\\\\"'claims']):\\\\n            raise Unsupported('duplicate authority or claim')\\\\n        for s in self.sources.values():\\\\n            if s['access_status'] \\\\\\\"'!= '\\\\\\\"'inspected_primary':\\\\n                continue\\\\n            if s.get('kind') \\\\\\\"'!= '\\\\\\\"'primary_standard' or not s.get('inspected_at'):\\\\n                raise Unsupported('uninspected or non-primary authority')\\\\n            for key in ('retained', 'text'):\\\\n                p = Path(s[key]['path'])\\\\n                if p.is_absolute() or '..' in p.parts or (self.root / p).is_symlink():\\\\n                    raise Unsupported('unsafe source path')\\\\n                try:\\\\n                    actual = sha256((self.root / p).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\\\\n                except OSError as exc:\\\\n                    raise Unsupported('missing source') from exc\\\\n                if actual \\\\\\\"'!= s[key]['\\\\\\\"'sha256']:\\\\n                    raise Unsupported('source hash mismatch')\\\\n            iso(s['period_start_inclusive']); iso(s['period_start_exclusive'])\\\\n        for c in self.claims.values():\\\\n            s = self.sources.get(c['authority_id'])\\\\n            if not s or s['access_status'] \\\\\\\"'!= '\\\\\\\"'inspected_primary':\\\\n                raise Unsupported('claim lacks inspected primary source')\\\\n            pages = (self.root / s['text']['path']).read_text().split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\f')\\\\n            for a in c['anchors']:\\\\n                if type(a['pdf_page']) is not int or not 1 <= a['pdf_page'] <= len(pages):\\\\n                    raise Unsupported('invalid anchor page')\\\\n                page = normal(pages[a['pdf_page'] - 1])\\\\n                if normal(a['quote']) not in page or a['paragraph'] not in s['inspected_paragraphs']:\\\\n                    raise Unsupported('unresolvable quote/paragraph')\\\\n        if any(c not in self.claims for c in REQUIRED):\\\\n            raise Unsupported('missing lifecycle authority')\\\\n        if set(d['note_links']) \\\\\\\"'!= {'\\\\\\\"'financing_carrying', 'financing_interest', 'financing_equity'}:\\\\n            raise Unsupported('note schema')\\\\n        for links in d['note_links'].values():\\\\n            if not links or any(link not in self.claims for link in links):\\\\n                raise Unsupported('unresolved note claim')\\\\n\\\\n    def admit(self, contract):\\\\n        # Revalidate so a caller cannot bypass source checks by mutating records.\\\\n        self.validate()\\\\n        for key in REQUIRED:\\\\n            s = self.sources[self.claims[key]['authority_id']]\\\\n            if (contract.jurisdiction \\\\\\\"'!= s['\\\\\\\"'jurisdiction'] or contract.basis \\\\\\\"'!= '\\\\\\\"'AASB'\\\\n                    or contract.tier \\\\\\\"'!= s['\\\\\\\"'tier'] or contract.entity_scope \\\\\\\"'!= s['\\\\\\\"'entity_scope']):\\\\n                raise Unsupported('authority jurisdiction/entity/tier mismatch')\\\\n            for year in range(iso(contract.issue_date).year,\\\\n                              iso(contract.issue_date).year + contract.years):\\\\n                start = date(year, 1, 1)\\\\n                if not iso(s['period_start_inclusive']) <= start < iso(s['period_start_exclusive']):\\\\n                    raise Unsupported('edition outside reporting-period start')\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\\\\nclass Contract:\\\\n    entity: str = 'SyntheticIssuer'\\\\n    book: str = 'statutory'\\\\n    currency: str = 'AUD'\\\\n    functional_currency: str = 'AUD'\\\\n    jurisdiction: str = 'AU'\\\\n    basis: str = 'AASB'\\\\n    tier: str = 'Tier 1'\\\\n    entity_scope: str = 'for-profit'\\\\n    issue_date: str = '2024-01-01'\\\\n    years: int = 2\\\\n    principal: str = '100'\\\\n    proceeds: str = '100'\\\\n    instrument_fair_value: str = '100'\\\\n    annual_coupon: str = '5'\\\\n    comparable_yield: str = '1/10'\\\\n    conversion_shares: int = 10\\\\n    conversion_right: str = 'maturity_only_fixed_for_fixed_nonputtable_ordinary'\\\\n    measurement: str = 'amortised_cost'\\\\n    unsupported_features: tuple = ()\\\\n\\\\n    def validate(self):\\\\n        if not self.entity or not self.book or not re.fullmatch('[A-Z]{3}', self.currency):\\\\n            raise Unsupported('entity/book/currency required')\\\\n        if self.currency \\\\\\\"'!= self.functional_currency:\\\\n            raise Unsupported('\\\\\\\"'FX unsupported')\\\\n        if (type(self.years) is not int or not 1 <= self.years <= 10\\\\n                or type(self.conversion_shares) is not int or self.conversion_shares <= 0):\\\\n            raise Unsupported('invalid term or shares')\\\\n        start = iso(self.issue_date)\\\\n        if (start.month, start.day) \\\\\\\"'!= (1, 1):\\\\n            raise Unsupported('\\\\\\\"'annual calendar periods only')\\\\n        if self.conversion_right \\\\\\\"'!= '\\\\\\\"'maturity_only_fixed_for_fixed_nonputtable_ordinary':\\\\n            raise Unsupported('unsupported conversion terms')\\\\n        if self.measurement \\\\\\\"'!= '\\\\\\\"'amortised_cost' or self.unsupported_features:\\\\n            raise Unsupported('fees/tax/options/modifications/default and other features excluded')\\\\n        p, proceeds, fair, coupon, rate = map(rational, (\\\\n            self.principal, self.proceeds, self.instrument_fair_value,\\\\n            self.annual_coupon, self.comparable_yield))\\\\n        if p <= 0 or proceeds <= 0 or coupon < 0 or rate < 0 or proceeds \\\\\\\"'!= fair:\\\\n            raise Unsupported('\\\\\\\"'positive principal/proceeds, fair-value proceeds and nonnegative coupon/yield required')\\\\n        liability = sum((coupon / (1 + rate) ** n for n in range(1, self.years + 1)), Fraction(0))\\\\n        liability += p / (1 + rate) ** self.years\\\\n        if liability > proceeds:\\\\n            raise Unsupported('negative residual equity: assumptions need reassessment')\\\\n        return liability\\\\n\\\\n    def coupon_dates(self):\\\\n        y = iso(self.issue_date).year\\\\n        return [date(y + i, 12, 31).isoformat() for i in range(self.years)]\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nclass BondBook:\\\\n    def __init__(self, contract, authority=None, opening_cash='20'):\\\\n        liability = contract.validate()\\\\n        self.authority = authority or AuthorityBook()\\\\n        self.authority.admit(contract)\\\\n        self.contract = contract\\\\n        self.initial_liability = liability\\\\n        opening = rational(opening_cash)\\\\n        if opening < 0:\\\\n            raise Unsupported('negative opening funding')\\\\n        self._ledger = {k: Fraction(0) for k in ACCOUNTS}\\\\n        self._ledger.update(cash=opening, opening_equity=-opening)\\\\n        self._journal = []\\\\n        self._used = set()\\\\n        self._position = 0\\\\n        self._shares = 0\\\\n        self._principal = Fraction(0)\\\\n        self._events = [('issue', contract.issue_date)]\\\\n        for day in contract.coupon_dates():\\\\n            self._events.extend([('accrue', day), ('coupon', day)])\\\\n        self._events.append(('settle', contract.coupon_dates()[-1]))\\\\n\\\\n    @property\\\\n    def state(self):\\\\n        return deepcopy({'ledger': self._ledger, 'position': self._position,\\\\n                         'shares': self._shares, 'principal_outstanding': self._principal,\\\\n                         'journal': self._journal, 'used_event_ids': sorted(self._used)})\\\\n\\\\n    def apply(self, event_id, kind, day):\\\\n        if not isinstance(event_id, str) or not event_id.strip() or event_id in self._used:\\\\n            raise Unsupported('missing/duplicate event identity')\\\\n        iso(day)\\\\n        if self._position >= len(self._events):\\\\n            raise Unsupported('already settled')\\\\n        expected, expected_day = self._events[self._position]\\\\n        if day \\\\\\\"'!= expected_day or (kind != expected and not (expected == '\\\\\\\"'settle' and kind in ('redeem', 'convert'))):\\\\n            raise Unsupported('out-of-order or conflicting event')\\\\n        c = self.contract\\\\n        ledger = deepcopy(self._ledger)\\\\n        shares, principal = self._shares, self._principal\\\\n        postings = {}\\\\n        claims = []\\\\n        if kind == 'issue':\\\\n            postings = {'cash': rational(c.proceeds), 'liability': -self.initial_liability,\\\\n                        'conversion_equity': -(rational(c.proceeds) - self.initial_liability)}\\\\n            principal = rational(c.principal)\\\\n            claims = ['recognition', 'classification', 'split']\\\\n        elif kind == 'accrue':\\\\n            interest = -ledger['liability'] * rational(c.comparable_yield)\\\\n            postings = {'interest_expense': interest, 'liability': -interest}\\\\n            claims = ['measurement', 'interest']\\\\n        elif kind == 'coupon':\\\\n            coupon = rational(c.annual_coupon)\\\\n            postings = {'liability': coupon, 'cash': -coupon}\\\\n            claims = ['measurement', 'redemption']\\\\n        elif kind in ('redeem', 'convert'):\\\\n            carrying = -ledger['liability']\\\\n            if carrying \\\\\\\"'!= rational(c.principal):\\\\n                raise Unsupported('\\\\\\\"'maturity liability does not equal principal')\\\\n            postings = {'liability': carrying, 'cash' if kind == 'redeem' else 'share_equity': -carrying}\\\\n            if kind == 'convert':\\\\n                shares += c.conversion_shares\\\\n            principal = Fraction(0)\\\\n            claims = ['redemption' if kind == 'redeem' else 'conversion']\\\\n        else:\\\\n            raise Unsupported('unsupported event')\\\\n        for account, amount in postings.items():\\\\n            ledger[account] += amount\\\\n        if sum(postings.values()) or sum(ledger.values()) or ledger['cash'] < 0 or ledger['liability'] > 0:\\\\n            raise Unsupported('journal/state/funding invariant')\\\\n        # Commit only after all validation, including funding and measurement.\\\\n        entry = {'id': event_id, 'kind': kind, 'date': day, 'entity': c.entity,\\\\n                 'book': c.book, 'currency': c.currency, 'postings_debit_positive': postings,\\\\n                 'claims': claims, 'state_after': deepcopy(ledger)}\\\\n        self._ledger, self._shares, self._principal = ledger, shares, principal\\\\n        self._journal.append(entry)\\\\n        self._used.add(event_id)\\\\n        self._position += 1\\\\n        return deepcopy(entry)\\\\n\\\\n    def notes(self):\\\\n        periods = []\\\\n        opening_carrying = Fraction(0)\\\\n        for year in range(iso(self.contract.issue_date).year,\\\\n                          iso(self.contract.issue_date).year + self.contract.years):\\\\n            rows = [x for x in self._journal if x['date'].startswith(str(year))]\\\\n            if not rows:\\\\n                continue\\\\n            def movement(kind, account):\\\\n                return sum((x['postings_debit_positive'].get(account, Fraction(0))\\\\n                            for x in rows if x['kind'] == kind), Fraction(0))\\\\n            issued = -movement('issue', 'liability')\\\\n            interest = movement('accrue', 'interest_expense')\\\\n            coupons = movement('coupon', 'liability')\\\\n            settled = movement('redeem', 'liability') + movement('convert', 'liability')\\\\n            closing = -rows[-1]['state_after']['liability']\\\\n            if opening_carrying + issued + interest - coupons - settled \\\\\\\"'!= closing:\\\\n                raise Unsupported('\\\\\\\"'note roll-forward mismatch')\\\\n            periods.append({'period_start': f'{year}-01-01', 'period_end': f'{year}-12-31',\\\\n                            'opening_liability': opening_carrying, 'issue_liability': issued,\\\\n                            'interest_expense': interest, 'coupons': coupons, 'settlement_liability': settled,\\\\n                            'closing_liability': closing, 'event_ids': [x['id'] for x in rows]})\\\\n            opening_carrying = closing\\\\n        return {'periods': periods, 'links': deepcopy(self.authority.records['note_links']),\\\\n                'mandatory_disclosure_scope': 'selected carrying amount and interest only; not a complete AASB 7 note',\\\\n                'conversion_equity': -self._ledger['conversion_equity'],\\\\n                'issued_share_equity': -self._ledger['share_equity'], 'issued_shares': self._shares}\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef run_case(contract=None, settlement='redeem', opening_cash='20', authority=None):\\\\n    c = contract or Contract()\\\\n    book = BondBook(c, authority, opening_cash)\\\\n    book.apply('issue', 'issue', c.issue_date)\\\\n    for i, day in enumerate(c.coupon_dates(), 1):\\\\n        book.apply(f'accrue-{i}', 'accrue', day)\\\\n        book.apply(f'coupon-{i}', 'coupon', day)\\\\n    book.apply('settlement', settlement, c.coupon_dates()[-1])\\\\n    return wire({'contract': vars(c), 'settlement': settlement, 'opening_cash': rational(opening_cash),\\\\n                 'initial_liability': book.initial_liability, 'state': book.state, 'notes': book.notes()})\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef compare_same_facts(contract=None, authority=None):\\\\n    c = contract or Contract()\\\\n    facts = wire(vars(c))\\\\n    # Hash common economics without changing terms for an unavailable rule set.\\\\n    economic = {k: v for k, v in facts.items() if k not in ('basis', 'jurisdiction', 'tier', 'entity_scope', 'book')}\\\\n    digest = sha256(json.dumps(economic, sort_keys=True).encode()).hexdigest()\\\\n    case = run_case(c, authority=authority)\\\\n    rows = [{'standard': 'AASB', 'jurisdiction': 'AU', 'facts_sha256': digest,\\\\n             'status': 'supported_bounded', 'initial_liability': case['initial_liability'],\\\\n             'initial_equity': str(rational(c.proceeds) - rational(case['initial_liability'])),\\\\n             'total_interest': case['state']['ledger']['interest_expense'],\\\\n             'claims': list(REQUIRED)}]\\\\n    for standard, jurisdiction, missing in [\\\\n        ('US GAAP', 'US', 'Applicable ASC 470/815 and ASU 2020-06 text, adoption and exceptions uninspected; official PDF 403.'),\\\\n        ('ASBE', 'CN', 'Official CAS 22/37 text, applicable edition and entity transition uninspected; MoF route 502.'),\\\\n        ('EU-endorsed IFRS', 'EU', 'Applicable endorsed IAS 32/IFRS 9 text and amendments uninspected; EUR-Lex returned empty 202.')]:\\\\n        rows.append({'standard': standard, 'jurisdiction': jurisdiction, 'facts_sha256': digest,\\\\n                     'status': 'unresolved', 'initial_liability': None, 'initial_equity': None,\\\\n                     'total_interest': None, 'claims': [], 'missing': missing})\\\\n    return {'economic_facts': economic, 'rows': rows, 'supported_difference': None,\\\\n            'criterion_status': 'incomplete: no second inspected applicable standard',\\\\n            'interpretation': 'No numerical difference or equivalence is established; Australian adoption is not universal IFRS authority.'}\\\\nPY\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_17\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"cat > scripts/corporate_financing_v1.py <<'PY'\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Bounded, exact AASB issuer compound-bond lifecycle (P08).\\\\n\\\\nEligibility and fair value/yield inputs are explicit synthetic assumptions, not\\\\ninferred accounting opinions. Annual calendar periods only; no market model.\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\\\n\\\\nfrom copy import deepcopy\\\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\\\nfrom datetime import date\\\\nfrom fractions import Fraction\\\\nfrom hashlib import sha256\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\nimport json\\\\nimport re\\\\n\\\\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\\\nREGISTER = 'docs/design/research/p08-v1/authority-register.json'\\\\nREQUIRED = ('recognition', 'classification', 'split', 'measurement', 'interest',\\\\n            'redemption', 'conversion', 'note_carrying', 'note_interest')\\\\nACCOUNTS = ('cash', 'liability', 'conversion_equity', 'share_equity',\\\\n            'opening_equity', 'interest_expense')\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nclass Unsupported(ValueError):\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"A fact, source, or event is outside the explicitly supported slice.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef rational(value):\\\\n    if isinstance(value, (bool, float)) or not isinstance(value, (str, int, Fraction)):\\\\n        raise Unsupported('amounts and rates require exact integer/rational inputs')\\\\n    try:\\\\n        return Fraction(value)\\\\n    except (ValueError, ZeroDivisionError) as exc:\\\\n        raise Unsupported('invalid rational') from exc\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef iso(value):\\\\n    try:\\\\n        result = date.fromisoformat(value)\\\\n        if result.isoformat() \\\\\\\"'!= value:\\\\n            raise ValueError('\\\\\\\"'noncanonical date')\\\\n        return result\\\\n    except (ValueError, TypeError) as exc:\\\\n        raise Unsupported('canonical ISO date required') from exc\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef wire(value):\\\\n    if isinstance(value, Fraction):\\\\n        return str(value)\\\\n    if isinstance(value, dict):\\\\n        return {key: wire(val) for key, val in value.items()}\\\\n    if isinstance(value, (list, tuple)):\\\\n        return [wire(val) for val in value]\\\\n    return value\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef normal(value):\\\\n    return re.sub(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s+', ' ', value).strip()\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nclass AuthorityBook:\\\\n    def __init__(self, root=ROOT, records=None):\\\\n        self.root = Path(root)\\\\n        self.records = deepcopy(records) if records is not None else json.loads(\\\\n            (self.root / REGISTER).read_text())\\\\n        self.validate()\\\\n\\\\n    def validate(self):\\\\n        d = self.records\\\\n        if d.get('schema_version') \\\\\\\"'!= '\\\\\\\"'accdsl.p08.authority.v1':\\\\n            raise Unsupported('authority schema')\\\\n        self.sources = {r['id']: r for r in d['authorities']}\\\\n        self.claims = {r['id']: r for r in d['claims']}\\\\n        if len(self.sources) \\\\\\\"'!= len(d['\\\\\\\"'authorities']) or len(self.claims) \\\\\\\"'!= len(d['\\\\\\\"'claims']):\\\\n            raise Unsupported('duplicate authority or claim')\\\\n        for s in self.sources.values():\\\\n            if s['access_status'] \\\\\\\"'!= '\\\\\\\"'inspected_primary':\\\\n                continue\\\\n            if s.get('kind') \\\\\\\"'!= '\\\\\\\"'primary_standard' or not s.get('inspected_at'):\\\\n                raise Unsupported('uninspected or non-primary authority')\\\\n            for key in ('retained', 'text'):\\\\n                p = Path(s[key]['path'])\\\\n                if p.is_absolute() or '..' in p.parts or (self.root / p).is_symlink():\\\\n                    raise Unsupported('unsafe source path')\\\\n                try:\\\\n                    actual = sha256((self.root / p).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\\\\n                except OSError as exc:\\\\n                    raise Unsupported('missing source') from exc\\\\n                if actual \\\\\\\"'!= s[key]['\\\\\\\"'sha256']:\\\\n                    raise Unsupported('source hash mismatch')\\\\n            iso(s['period_start_inclusive']); iso(s['period_start_exclusive'])\\\\n        for c in self.claims.values():\\\\n            s = self.sources.get(c['authority_id'])\\\\n            if not s or s['access_status'] \\\\\\\"'!= '\\\\\\\"'inspected_primary':\\\\n                raise Unsupported('claim lacks inspected primary source')\\\\n            pages = (self.root / s['text']['path']).read_text().split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\f')\\\\n            for a in c['anchors']:\\\\n                if type(a['pdf_page']) is not int or not 1 <= a['pdf_page'] <= len(pages):\\\\n                    raise Unsupported('invalid anchor page')\\\\n                page = normal(pages[a['pdf_page'] - 1])\\\\n                if normal(a['quote']) not in page or a['paragraph'] not in s['inspected_paragraphs']:\\\\n                    raise Unsupported('unresolvable quote/paragraph')\\\\n        if any(c not in self.claims for c in REQUIRED):\\\\n            raise Unsupported('missing lifecycle authority')\\\\n        if set(d['note_links']) \\\\\\\"'!= {'\\\\\\\"'financing_carrying', 'financing_interest', 'financing_equity'}:\\\\n            raise Unsupported('note schema')\\\\n        for links in d['note_links'].values():\\\\n            if not links or any(link not in self.claims for link in links):\\\\n                raise Unsupported('unresolved note claim')\\\\n\\\\n    def admit(self, contract):\\\\n        # Revalidate so a caller cannot bypass source checks by mutating records.\\\\n        self.validate()\\\\n        for key in REQUIRED:\\\\n            s = self.sources[self.claims[key]['authority_id']]\\\\n            if (contract.jurisdiction \\\\\\\"'!= s['\\\\\\\"'jurisdiction'] or contract.basis \\\\\\\"'!= '\\\\\\\"'AASB'\\\\n                    or contract.tier \\\\\\\"'!= s['\\\\\\\"'tier'] or contract.entity_scope \\\\\\\"'!= s['\\\\\\\"'entity_scope']):\\\\n                raise Unsupported('authority jurisdiction/entity/tier mismatch')\\\\n            for year in range(iso(contract.issue_date).year,\\\\n                              iso(contract.issue_date).year + contract.years):\\\\n                start = date(year, 1, 1)\\\\n                if not iso(s['period_start_inclusive']) <= start < iso(s['period_start_exclusive']):\\\\n                    raise Unsupported('edition outside reporting-period start')\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\\\\nclass Contract:\\\\n    entity: str = 'SyntheticIssuer'\\\\n    book: str = 'statutory'\\\\n    currency: str = 'AUD'\\\\n    functional_currency: str = 'AUD'\\\\n    jurisdiction: str = 'AU'\\\\n    basis: str = 'AASB'\\\\n    tier: str = 'Tier 1'\\\\n    entity_scope: str = 'for-profit'\\\\n    issue_date: str = '2024-01-01'\\\\n    years: int = 2\\\\n    principal: str = '100'\\\\n    proceeds: str = '100'\\\\n    instrument_fair_value: str = '100'\\\\n    annual_coupon: str = '5'\\\\n    comparable_yield: str = '1/10'\\\\n    conversion_shares: int = 10\\\\n    conversion_right: str = 'maturity_only_fixed_for_fixed_nonputtable_ordinary'\\\\n    measurement: str = 'amortised_cost'\\\\n    unsupported_features: tuple = ()\\\\n\\\\n    def validate(self):\\\\n        if not self.entity or not self.book or not re.fullmatch('[A-Z]{3}', self.currency):\\\\n            raise Unsupported('entity/book/currency required')\\\\n        if self.currency \\\\\\\"'!= self.functional_currency:\\\\n            raise Unsupported('\\\\\\\"'FX unsupported')\\\\n        if (type(self.years) is not int or not 1 <= self.years <= 10\\\\n                or type(self.conversion_shares) is not int or self.conversion_shares <= 0):\\\\n            raise Unsupported('invalid term or shares')\\\\n        start = iso(self.issue_date)\\\\n        if (start.month, start.day) \\\\\\\"'!= (1, 1):\\\\n            raise Unsupported('\\\\\\\"'annual calendar periods only')\\\\n        if self.conversion_right \\\\\\\"'!= '\\\\\\\"'maturity_only_fixed_for_fixed_nonputtable_ordinary':\\\\n            raise Unsupported('unsupported conversion terms')\\\\n        if self.measurement \\\\\\\"'!= '\\\\\\\"'amortised_cost' or self.unsupported_features:\\\\n            raise Unsupported('fees/tax/options/modifications/default and other features excluded')\\\\n        p, proceeds, fair, coupon, rate = map(rational, (\\\\n            self.principal, self.proceeds, self.instrument_fair_value,\\\\n            self.annual_coupon, self.comparable_yield))\\\\n        if p <= 0 or proceeds <= 0 or coupon < 0 or rate < 0 or proceeds \\\\\\\"'!= fair:\\\\n            raise Unsupported('\\\\\\\"'positive principal/proceeds, fair-value proceeds and nonnegative coupon/yield required')\\\\n        liability = sum((coupon / (1 + rate) ** n for n in range(1, self.years + 1)), Fraction(0))\\\\n        liability += p / (1 + rate) ** self.years\\\\n        if liability > proceeds:\\\\n            raise Unsupported('negative residual equity: assumptions need reassessment')\\\\n        return liability\\\\n\\\\n    def coupon_dates(self):\\\\n        y = iso(self.issue_date).year\\\\n        return [date(y + i, 12, 31).isoformat() for i in range(self.years)]\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nclass BondBook:\\\\n    def __init__(self, contract, authority=None, opening_cash='20'):\\\\n        liability = contract.validate()\\\\n        self.authority = authority or AuthorityBook()\\\\n        self.authority.admit(contract)\\\\n        self.contract = contract\\\\n        self.initial_liability = liability\\\\n        opening = rational(opening_cash)\\\\n        if opening < 0:\\\\n            raise Unsupported('negative opening funding')\\\\n        self._ledger = {k: Fraction(0) for k in ACCOUNTS}\\\\n        self._ledger.update(cash=opening, opening_equity=-opening)\\\\n        self._journal = []\\\\n        self._used = set()\\\\n        self._position = 0\\\\n        self._shares = 0\\\\n        self._principal = Fraction(0)\\\\n        self._events = [('issue', contract.issue_date)]\\\\n        for day in contract.coupon_dates():\\\\n            self._events.extend([('accrue', day), ('coupon', day)])\\\\n        self._events.append(('settle', contract.coupon_dates()[-1]))\\\\n\\\\n    @property\\\\n    def state(self):\\\\n        return deepcopy({'ledger': self._ledger, 'position': self._position,\\\\n                         'shares': self._shares, 'principal_outstanding': self._principal,\\\\n                         'journal': self._journal, 'used_event_ids': sorted(self._used)})\\\\n\\\\n    def apply(self, event_id, kind, day):\\\\n        if not isinstance(event_id, str) or not event_id.strip() or event_id in self._used:\\\\n            raise Unsupported('missing/duplicate event identity')\\\\n        iso(day)\\\\n        if self._position >= len(self._events):\\\\n            raise Unsupported('already settled')\\\\n        expected, expected_day = self._events[self._position]\\\\n        if day \\\\\\\"'!= expected_day or (kind != expected and not (expected == '\\\\\\\"'settle' and kind in ('redeem', 'convert'))):\\\\n            raise Unsupported('out-of-order or conflicting event')\\\\n        c = self.contract\\\\n        ledger = deepcopy(self._ledger)\\\\n        shares, principal = self._shares, self._principal\\\\n        postings = {}\\\\n        claims = []\\\\n        if kind == 'issue':\\\\n            postings = {'cash': rational(c.proceeds), 'liability': -self.initial_liability,\\\\n                        'conversion_equity': -(rational(c.proceeds) - self.initial_liability)}\\\\n            principal = rational(c.principal)\\\\n            claims = ['recognition', 'classification', 'split']\\\\n        elif kind == 'accrue':\\\\n            interest = -ledger['liability'] * rational(c.comparable_yield)\\\\n            postings = {'interest_expense': interest, 'liability': -interest}\\\\n            claims = ['measurement', 'interest']\\\\n        elif kind == 'coupon':\\\\n            coupon = rational(c.annual_coupon)\\\\n            postings = {'liability': coupon, 'cash': -coupon}\\\\n            claims = ['measurement', 'redemption']\\\\n        elif kind in ('redeem', 'convert'):\\\\n            carrying = -ledger['liability']\\\\n            if carrying \\\\\\\"'!= rational(c.principal):\\\\n                raise Unsupported('\\\\\\\"'maturity liability does not equal principal')\\\\n            postings = {'liability': carrying, 'cash' if kind == 'redeem' else 'share_equity': -carrying}\\\\n            if kind == 'convert':\\\\n                shares += c.conversion_shares\\\\n            principal = Fraction(0)\\\\n            claims = ['redemption' if kind == 'redeem' else 'conversion']\\\\n        else:\\\\n            raise Unsupported('unsupported event')\\\\n        for account, amount in postings.items():\\\\n            ledger[account] += amount\\\\n        if sum(postings.values()) or sum(ledger.values()) or ledger['cash'] < 0 or ledger['liability'] > 0:\\\\n            raise Unsupported('journal/state/funding invariant')\\\\n        # Commit only after all validation, including funding and measurement.\\\\n        entry = {'id': event_id, 'kind': kind, 'date': day, 'entity': c.entity,\\\\n                 'book': c.book, 'currency': c.currency, 'postings_debit_positive': postings,\\\\n                 'claims': claims, 'state_after': deepcopy(ledger)}\\\\n        self._ledger, self._shares, self._principal = ledger, shares, principal\\\\n        self._journal.append(entry)\\\\n        self._used.add(event_id)\\\\n        self._position += 1\\\\n        return deepcopy(entry)\\\\n\\\\n    def notes(self):\\\\n        periods = []\\\\n        opening_carrying = Fraction(0)\\\\n        for year in range(iso(self.contract.issue_date).year,\\\\n                          iso(self.contract.issue_date).year + self.contract.years):\\\\n            rows = [x for x in self._journal if x['date'].startswith(str(year))]\\\\n            if not rows:\\\\n                continue\\\\n            def movement(kind, account):\\\\n                return sum((x['postings_debit_positive'].get(account, Fraction(0))\\\\n                            for x in rows if x['kind'] == kind), Fraction(0))\\\\n            issued = -movement('issue', 'liability')\\\\n            interest = movement('accrue', 'interest_expense')\\\\n            coupons = movement('coupon', 'liability')\\\\n            settled = movement('redeem', 'liability') + movement('convert', 'liability')\\\\n            closing = -rows[-1]['state_after']['liability']\\\\n            if opening_carrying + issued + interest - coupons - settled \\\\\\\"'!= closing:\\\\n                raise Unsupported('\\\\\\\"'note roll-forward mismatch')\\\\n            periods.append({'period_start': f'{year}-01-01', 'period_end': f'{year}-12-31',\\\\n                            'opening_liability': opening_carrying, 'issue_liability': issued,\\\\n                            'interest_expense': interest, 'coupons': coupons, 'settlement_liability': settled,\\\\n                            'closing_liability': closing, 'event_ids': [x['id'] for x in rows]})\\\\n            opening_carrying = closing\\\\n        return {'periods': periods, 'links': deepcopy(self.authority.records['note_links']),\\\\n                'mandatory_disclosure_scope': 'selected carrying amount and interest only; not a complete AASB 7 note',\\\\n                'conversion_equity': -self._ledger['conversion_equity'],\\\\n                'issued_share_equity': -self._ledger['share_equity'], 'issued_shares': self._shares}\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef run_case(contract=None, settlement='redeem', opening_cash='20', authority=None):\\\\n    c = contract or Contract()\\\\n    book = BondBook(c, authority, opening_cash)\\\\n    book.apply('issue', 'issue', c.issue_date)\\\\n    for i, day in enumerate(c.coupon_dates(), 1):\\\\n        book.apply(f'accrue-{i}', 'accrue', day)\\\\n        book.apply(f'coupon-{i}', 'coupon', day)\\\\n    book.apply('settlement', settlement, c.coupon_dates()[-1])\\\\n    return wire({'contract': vars(c), 'settlement': settlement, 'opening_cash': rational(opening_cash),\\\\n                 'initial_liability': book.initial_liability, 'state': book.state, 'notes': book.notes()})\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef compare_same_facts(contract=None, authority=None):\\\\n    c = contract or Contract()\\\\n    facts = wire(vars(c))\\\\n    # Hash common economics without changing terms for an unavailable rule set.\\\\n    economic = {k: v for k, v in facts.items() if k not in ('basis', 'jurisdiction', 'tier', 'entity_scope', 'book')}\\\\n    digest = sha256(json.dumps(economic, sort_keys=True).encode()).hexdigest()\\\\n    case = run_case(c, authority=authority)\\\\n    rows = [{'standard': 'AASB', 'jurisdiction': 'AU', 'facts_sha256': digest,\\\\n             'status': 'supported_bounded', 'initial_liability': case['initial_liability'],\\\\n             'initial_equity': str(rational(c.proceeds) - rational(case['initial_liability'])),\\\\n             'total_interest': case['state']['ledger']['interest_expense'],\\\\n             'claims': list(REQUIRED)}]\\\\n    for standard, jurisdiction, missing in [\\\\n        ('US GAAP', 'US', 'Applicable ASC 470/815 and ASU 2020-06 text, adoption and exceptions uninspected; official PDF 403.'),\\\\n        ('ASBE', 'CN', 'Official CAS 22/37 text, applicable edition and entity transition uninspected; MoF route 502.'),\\\\n        ('EU-endorsed IFRS', 'EU', 'Applicable endorsed IAS 32/IFRS 9 text and amendments uninspected; EUR-Lex returned empty 202.')]:\\\\n        rows.append({'standard': standard, 'jurisdiction': jurisdiction, 'facts_sha256': digest,\\\\n                     'status': 'unresolved', 'initial_liability': None, 'initial_equity': None,\\\\n                     'total_interest': None, 'claims': [], 'missing': missing})\\\\n    return {'economic_facts': economic, 'rows': rows, 'supported_difference': None,\\\\n            'criterion_status': 'incomplete: no second inspected applicable standard',\\\\n            'interpretation': 'No numerical difference or equivalence is established; Australian adoption is not universal IFRS authority.'}\\\\nPY\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_18\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\nfor name, needles in [('aasb9',['3.1.1   An entity','4.2.1   An entity','effective interest method      The method']),('aasb7',['8       The carrying','total interest expense'])]:\\\\n s=Path(f'docs/design/research/p08-v1/{name}.txt').read_text()\\\\n for needle in needles:\\\\n  i=s.find(needle); print(name,'page',s[:i].count('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\f')+1,repr(s[i:i+1250]))\\\\ns=Path('docs/design/research/standards/aasb132.txt').read_text()\\\\nfor needle in ['28      The issuer','35      Interest','AG32      On conversion']:\\\\n i=s.find(needle);print('132 page',s[:i].count('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\f')+1,repr(s[i:i+750]))\\\\nPY\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_18\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\nfor name, needles in [('aasb9',['3.1.1   An entity','4.2.1   An entity','effective interest method      The method']),('aasb7',['8       The carrying','total interest expense'])]:\\\\n s=Path(f'docs/design/research/p08-v1/{name}.txt').read_text()\\\\n for needle in needles:\\\\n  i=s.find(needle); print(name,'page',s[:i].count('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\f')+1,repr(s[i:i+1250]))\\\\ns=Path('docs/design/research/standards/aasb132.txt').read_text()\\\\nfor needle in ['28      The issuer','35      Interest','AG32      On conversion']:\\\\n i=s.find(needle);print('132 page',s[:i].count('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\f')+1,repr(s[i:i+750]))\\\\nPY\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"aasb9 page 10 '3.1.1   An entity shall recognise a financial asset or a financial liability in its statement of financial position\\\\\\\\n        when, and only when, the entity becomes party to the contractual provisions of the instrument (see\\\\\\\\n        paragraphs B3.1.1 and B3.1.2). When an entity first recognises a financial asset, it shall classify it in\\\\\\\\n        accordance with paragraphs 4.1.1–4.1.5 and measure it in accordance with paragraphs 5.1.1–5.1.3.\\\\\\\\n        When an entity first recognises a financial liability, it shall classify it in accordance with\\\\\\\\n        paragraphs 4.2.1 and 4.2.2 and measure it in accordance with paragraph 5.1.1.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n        Regular way purchase or sale of financial assets\\\\\\\\n3.1.2   A regular way purchase or sale of financial assets shall be recognised and derecognised, as applicable,\\\\\\\\n        using trade date accounting or settlement date accounting (see paragraphs B3.1.3–B3.1.6).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3.2 Derecognition of financial assets\\\\\\\\n3.2.1   In consolidated financial statements, paragraphs 3.2.2–3.2.9, B3.1.1, B3.1.2 and B3.2.1–B3.2.17 are applied\\\\\\\\n        at a consolidated level. Hence, an entity first consolidates all subsidiaries in accordance with AASB 10 and\\\\\\\\n        then applies those paragraphs to the resulting group.\\\\\\\\n3.2.2   Before ev'\\\\naasb9 page 16 '4.2.1   An entity shall classify all financial liabilities as subsequently measured at amortised cost, except for:\\\\\\\\n        (a)       financial liabilities at fair value through profit or loss. Such liabilities, including derivatives\\\\\\\\n                  that are liabilities, shall be subsequently measured at fair value.\\\\\\\\n        (b)       financial liabilities that arise when a transfer of a financial asset does not qualify for\\\\\\\\n                  derecognition or when the continuing involvement approach applies. Paragraphs 3.2.15 and\\\\\\\\n                  3.2.17 apply to the measurement of such financial liabilities.\\\\\\\\n        (c)       financial guarantee contracts. After initial recognition, an issuer of such a contract shall\\\\\\\\n                  (unless paragraph 4.2.1(a) or (b) applies) subsequently measure it at the higher of:\\\\\\\\n                  (i)        the amount of the loss allowance determined in accordance with Section 5.5 and\\\\\\\\n                  (ii)       the amount initially recognised (see paragraph 5.1.1) less, when appropriate, the\\\\\\\\n                             cumulative amount of income recognised in accordance with the principles of\\\\\\\\n                             AASB 15.\\\\\\\\n        (d)       commitments to provide a loan at a below'\\\\naasb9 page 45 'effective interest method      The method that is used in the calculation of the amortised cost of a financial\\\\\\\\n                               asset or a financial liability and in the allocation and recognition of the interest\\\\\\\\n                               revenue or interest expense in profit or loss over the relevant period.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\neffective interest rate        The rate that exactly discounts estimated future cash payments or receipts through\\\\\\\\n                               the expected life of the financial asset or financial liability to the gross carrying\\\\\\\\n                               amount of a financial asset or to the amortised cost of a financial liability.\\\\\\\\n                               When calculating the effective interest rate, an entity shall estimate the expected\\\\\\\\n                               cash flows by considering all the contractual terms of the financial instrument (for\\\\\\\\n                               example, prepayment, extension, call and similar options) but shall not consider\\\\\\\\n                               the expected credit losses. The calculation includes all fees and points paid or\\\\\\\\n                               received between parties to the contract that are an integral part of the effective\\\\\\\\n        '\\\\naasb7 page 8 '8       The carrying amounts of each of the following categories, as specified in AASB 9, shall be disclosed either\\\\\\\\n        in the statement of financial position or in the notes:\\\\\\\\n        (a)       financial assets measured at fair value through profit or loss, showing separately (i) those\\\\\\\\n                  designated as such upon initial recognition or subsequently in accordance with paragraph 6.7.1 of\\\\\\\\n                  AASB 9; (ii) those measured as such in accordance with the election in paragraph 3.3.5 of\\\\\\\\n                  AASB 9; (iii) those measured as such in accordance with the election in paragraph 33A of\\\\\\\\n                  AASB 132 and (iv) those mandatorily measured at fair value through profit or loss in accordance\\\\\\\\n                  with AASB 9.\\\\\\\\n        (b)–(d)   [deleted]\\\\\\\\n        (e)       financial liabilities at fair value through profit or loss, showing separately (i) those designated as\\\\\\\\n                  such upon initial recognition or subsequently in accordance with paragraph 6.7.1 of AASB 9 and\\\\\\\\n                  (ii) those that meet the definition of held for trading in AASB 9.\\\\\\\\n        (f)       financial assets measured at amortised cost.\\\\\\\\n        (g)       financial liabilities measured at amortised cost.\\\\\\\\n     '\\\\naasb7 page 12 'total interest expense (calculated using the effective interest method) for\\\\\\\\n                  financial assets that are measured at amortised cost or that are measured at fair value through\\\\\\\\n                  other comprehensive income in accordance with paragraph 4.1.2A of AASB 9 (showing these\\\\\\\\n                  amounts separately); or financial liabilities that are not measured at fair value through profit or\\\\\\\\n                  loss.\\\\\\\\n        (c)       fee income and expense (other than amounts included in determining the effective interest rate)\\\\\\\\n                  arising from:\\\\\\\\n                  (i)         financial assets and financial liabilities that are not at fair value through profit or loss;\\\\\\\\n                              and\\\\\\\\n                  (ii)        trust and other fiduciary activities that result in the holding or investing of assets on\\\\\\\\n                              behalf of individuals, trusts, retirement benefit plans, and other institutions.\\\\\\\\n        (d)       [deleted]\\\\\\\\n        (e)       [deleted]\\\\\\\\n20A     An entity shall disclose an analysis of the gain or loss recognised in the statement of comprehensive income\\\\\\\\n        arising from the derecognition of financial assets measured at amortised cost, showing separatel'\\\\n132 page 13 '28      The issuer of a non-derivative financial instrument shall evaluate the terms of the financial\\\\\\\\n        instrument to determine whether it contains both a liability and an equity component. Such\\\\\\\\n        components shall be classified separately as financial liabilities, financial assets or equity instruments\\\\\\\\n        in accordance with paragraph 15.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAASB 132-compiled                                          13                                                STANDARD\\\\\\\\n                                  Authorised Version F2023C00406 registered 04/05/2023\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\x0c29      An entity recognises separately the components of a financial instrument that (a) creates a financial liability\\\\\\\\n        of the entity and (b) grants an option to the holder of t'\\\\n132 page 15 '35      Interest, dividends, losses and gains relating to a financial instrument or a component that is a\\\\\\\\n        financial liability shall be recognised as income or expense in profit or loss. Distributions to holders of\\\\\\\\n        an equity instrument shall be recognised by the entity directly in equity. Transaction costs of an\\\\\\\\n        equity transaction shall be accounted for as a deduction from equity.\\\\\\\\n35A     Income tax relating to distributions to holders of an equity instrument and to transaction costs of an equity\\\\\\\\n        transaction shall be accounted for in accordance with AASB 112 Income Taxes.\\\\\\\\n36      The classification of a financial instrument as a financial liability or an equity instrument determines\\\\\\\\n        whether interest, d'\\\\n132 page 25 'AG32      On conversion of a convertible instrument at maturity, the entity derecognises the liability component and\\\\\\\\n          recognises it as equity. The original equity component remains as equity (although it may be transferred\\\\\\\\n          from one line item within equity to another). There is no gain or loss on conversion at maturity.\\\\\\\\nAG33      When an entity extinguishes a convertible instrument before maturity through an early redemption or\\\\\\\\n          repurchase in which the original conversion privileges are unchanged, the entity allocates the consideration\\\\\\\\n          paid and any transaction costs for the repurchase or redemption to the liability and equity components of the\\\\\\\\n          instrument at the date of the transaction. The meth'\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_19\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"cat > /tmp/p08_register.py <<'PY'\\\\nimport json,hashlib,datetime,pathlib,re\\\\nroot=pathlib.Path('.');base=root/'docs/design/research/p08-v1'\\\\ndef asset(p):return {'path':p,'sha256':hashlib.sha256((root/p).read_bytes()).hexdigest()}\\\\ndef norm(s):return re.sub(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s+',' ',s).strip()\\\\nnow=datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat()\\\\nrecords=json.loads((base/'access-records.json').read_text())+[json.loads((base/'eu-access.json').read_text())]\\\\nauthorities=[]\\\\nfor id,stem,title,pars in [\\\\n ('aasb132','docs/design/research/standards/aasb132','AASB 132 Financial Instruments: Presentation',['22','22A','25–27','28–32','35','AG30–AG35']),\\\\n ('aasb9','docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb9','AASB 9 Financial Instruments',['3.1.1','3.3.1–3.3.3','4.2.1','5.1.1','Appendix A: amortised cost','Appendix A: effective interest']),\\\\n ('aasb7','docs/design/research/p08-v1/aasb7','AASB 7 Financial Instruments: Disclosures',['7','8(g)','20(b)'])]:\\\\n access=next((a for a in records if a['id']==id),None)\\\\n authorities.append({'id':id,'title':title,'issuer':'Australian Accounting Standards Board','kind':'primary_standard','access_status':'inspected_primary',\\\\n 'official_url':access['url'] if access else 'https://www.aasb.gov.au/admin/file/content105/c9/AASB132_08-15_COMPdec22_01-23.pdf',\\\\n 'retrieved_at':access['retrieved_at'] if access else '2026-10-02 (prior archive; time not recorded)',\\\\n 'inspected_at':now,'retained':asset(stem+'.pdf'),'text':asset(stem+'.txt'),\\\\n 'edition':'31 December 2022 compilation; amendments through 15 December 2022',\\\\n 'jurisdiction':'AU','entity_scope':'for-profit','tier':'Tier 1',\\\\n 'period_start_inclusive':'2023-01-01','period_start_exclusive':'2026-07-01',\\\\n 'transition_conditions':'Use this compilation only for annual periods with start in the stated interval; no optional early adoption of subsequent amendments. Synthetic cases use calendar 2024 and 2025.',\\\\n 'applicability_anchor':'Cover and compilation preamble; Comparison with IAS/IFRS, Tier 1.',\\\\n 'inspected_paragraphs':pars,'limits':'Only listed paragraphs inspected. Official Australian adoption; no universal IFRS jurisdiction conclusion.'})\\\\nclaims=[]\\\\ndef claim(id,source,para,quote,meaning):\\\\n s=next(x for x in authorities if x['id']==source)\\\\n pages=(root/s['text']['path']).read_text().split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\f')\\\\n found=[i+1 for i,p in enumerate(pages) if norm(quote) in norm(p)]\\\\n if len(found)\\\\\\\"'!=1:raise ValueError((id,found))\\\\n claims.append({'\\\\\\\"'id':id,'authority_id':source,'anchors':[{'paragraph':para,'pdf_page':found[0],'quote':quote}],\\\\n                'supported_statement':meaning,'status':'inspected_primary_conditional'})\\\\nclaim('recognition','aasb9','3.1.1','when, and only when, the entity becomes party to the contractual provisions of the instrument','Recognise the contractual financial liability when the issuer becomes party; proceeds are assumed equal to instrument fair value.')\\\\nclaim('fair_value','aasb9','5.1.1','measure a financial asset or financial liability at its fair value plus or minus','Initial measurement uses fair value; this slice assumes proceeds equal fair value and no transaction costs.')\\\\nclaim('classification','aasb132','22','fixed number of its own equity instruments in exchange for a fixed amount of cash or another financial asset is an equity instrument.','Fixed-for-fixed equity classification, conditional on ordinary non-puttable shares, functional currency and exclusion of settlement alternatives/contingencies.')\\\\nclaim('split','aasb132','AG30–AG35','On initial recognition, the fair value of the liability component is the present value of the contractually determined stream of future cash flows','AG31(a): discount liability cash flows at comparable non-convertible market yield; paragraphs 28–32 allocate residual proceeds to equity.')\\\\nclaim('residual_equity','aasb132','28–32','the equity component is assigned the residual amount after deducting from the fair value of the instrument as a whole','Paragraph 31 supplies residual allocation. Equity is not remeasured; retained on expiry is a local deduction from paragraph 22 and liability-only extinguishment, not a separate quoted redemption rule.')\\\\nclaim('measurement','aasb9','4.2.1','An entity shall classify all financial liabilities as subsequently measured at amortised cost, except for:','Ordinary liability uses amortised cost. Exclude fair-value designation/trading, derivatives, guarantees, transfer liabilities, below-market commitments and business-combination contingent consideration.')\\\\nclaim('interest','aasb9','Appendix A: effective interest','the allocation and recognition of the interest revenue or interest expense in profit or loss over the relevant period.','Effective-interest method allocates interest expense; use opening liability times the assumed exact annual effective yield.')\\\\nclaim('amortised_cost','aasb9','Appendix A: amortised cost','minus the principal repayments, plus or minus the cumulative amortisation using the effective interest method','Amortised cost roll-forward follows contractual payments and cumulative effective-interest amortisation.')\\\\nclaim('redemption','aasb9','3.3.1–3.3.3','when, and only when, it is extinguished – ie when the obligation specified in the contract is discharged or cancelled or expires.','Remove the discharged liability; paragraph 3.3.3 difference is profit/loss. At this exact maturity, consideration equals carrying amount, so zero settlement gain/loss.')\\\\nclaim('conversion','aasb132','AG30–AG35','On conversion of a convertible instrument at maturity, the entity derecognises the liability component and recognises it as equity.','AG32: maturity conversion reclassifies liability to equity, leaves original equity within equity and produces no gain/loss.')\\\\nclaim('note_carrying','aasb7','8(g)','financial liabilities measured at amortised cost.','8(g), read with paragraph 8 lead-in: disclose carrying amounts of financial liabilities at amortised cost on the face or in notes.')\\\\nclaim('note_interest','aasb7','20(b)','total interest revenue and total interest expense (calculated using the effective interest method)','20(b): disclose effective-interest totals for liabilities not measured at fair value through profit/loss. This is selected note content only.')\\\\nresearch={'source':'docs/design/research/standards/actus-techspecs.tex','sha256':hashlib.sha256((root/'docs/design/research/standards/actus-techspecs.tex').read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\\\\n 'inspected_sections':['State Variables (sec:statevarsnotat)','Contract Events (sec:events)','Payoff Functions (sec:pof)'],\\\\n 'decision':'defer integration; no ACTUS algorithm, schedule, code or forecast mechanism adopted',\\\\n 'support':'Retained technical specification distinguishes dated events, state changes and cash-flow functions.',\\\\n 'transfer_limit':'Implementation uses an explicit user-specified annual schedule and local accounting transitions. No ACTUS compatibility, official-code equivalence, empirical evaluation or company-simulation validity claim. Broader method/theory/evaluation and code audit required before future adoption.'}\\\\nqueue=[]\\\\nfor method,boundary,missing,interpretation,case,req,gap in [\\\\n ('revenue','single contract, performance obligation, delivery/collection','Applicable AASB 15/ASC 606/ASBE 14 primary paragraphs','Distinct promises, variable-consideration constraint and timing','Two obligations, advance cash, partial delivery and refund','MC15/MC19','G4/G7'),\\\\n ('tax','current tax and one temporary difference','Applicable AASB 112/ASC 740/ASBE 18 and tax law','Tax base, enacted rates and deferred-tax recoverability','Two-year depreciation difference and loss carryforward','MC15/MC19','G4/G7'),\\\\n ('leases','lessee recognition through one remeasurement','Applicable 