ire-sales are triggered by the drop in the stock of funding. The inﬂow of funding\ndocs/design/research/text/halaj2016.txt:346:      portfolio and funding).\ndocs/design/research/text/halaj2016.txt:362:the inﬂuences of the funding risk on the asset structures. Moreover, the current setup helps to keep\ndocs/design/research/text/halaj2016.txt:393:loans, the value of securities, the change in funding and the P&L impact of the ﬁre-sales. Notably,\ndocs/design/research/text/halaj2016.txt:394:the total reinvestment portfolio is impacted by the change in funding asymmetrically depending on\ndocs/design/research/text/halaj2016.txt:395:the sign of the change: the change of the reinvestment portfolio related to funding is equal to\ndocs/design/research/text/halaj2016.txt:399:In case of the funding outﬂow, the bank “ﬁre-sales” its securities to meet the obligations. The price\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
