15|MC16|MC17|MC18|MC28|G4|G5|G14|G18' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"36:to the [initial gap audit](../design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md); G11–G18 refer\\n55:| MC01 | Account for complete annual, quarterly and semi-annual disclosure packages, including notes and relevant referenced material. U1, U3. | Define the source inventory, coverage units, cross-reference closure and disposition rules. A worked filing package must account for retained, structured, duplicated and unresolved content without treating page extraction as semantic completion. | Specified procedure; acquired-file inventory checked. Ch. 2 Apple and Ch. 3 coverage; `cases/apple/manifest.json` accounts for 121 annual pages, 13 annual notes and 10 interim notes. External incorporated documents and full semantic translation remain incomplete. G5, G11. The added source corpus now has 192 checked annual/interim files across nine issuers and 2018–2025; incorporated-package closure and semantic annotation remain open. |\\n59:| MC05 | Represent economic, reporting, publication/availability and system times; preserve original and revised history. U1, U3, D. | Specify original, latest-available and harmonised queries, cutoffs, supersession, calendar/interval rules and retrospective/prospective changes. Include exact annual/interim/restatement fixtures. | Specified in Chs. 2–3 and EvidenceView/Time contracts. Four publication/ingestion queries and compatible annual-minus-interim subtraction are reference-checked in `temporal.json`. Debt dates, periods, publication/ingestion/review cutoffs now have semantic rejection checks. General calendar and standards-transition implementations remain pending. G2, G4, G13. The accepted corpus records sourced filing dates for 56 reports and explicitly unverified publication dates for 136; as-of forecasting remains blocked where availability is unknown. |\\n60:| MC06 | Distinguish legal entities, ownership, control, group perimeter and consolidation. U1, D. | Provide dated entity/control and adjustment-book types, acquisition/disposal and intragroup examples, and rules preventing unexplained consolidation plugs. | Specified structural control/elimination model; Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` check a simplified 80% acquisition, intragroup loan and full disposal. Actual control conclusions, goodwill/tax/FX and complex retained interests need further authority and operations. G4, G7, G12. |\\n77:| MC13 | Drive economic events from contract state and explicit behaviour, then apply accounting rules and atomic journal/state updates. U2, D. | Specify one reference economic model, event payloads, recognition/measurement operations, preconditions, ordering and atomic transitions. Prove the stated bookkeeping invariant and separately define admissibility. | Specified Northstar economic decisions, event preconditions and operations in Chs. 2, 8. Reference journals, atomic rejection and idempotency checks pass. This verifies the bounded oracle, not a production event engine or accounting compliance. G2, G4, G6. |\\n78:| MC14 | Give scenarios and decision information explicit meanings. U2, P, D. | Define supported exogenous stress, observational-conditioning and intervention modes, or explicitly scope unsupported modes; enforce information dates and distinguish real-world from pricing measures. | Specified exogenous stress, observational conditioning, intervention preconditions and information capabilities in Ch. 8/Core 0. Finite conditioning, an information-date example and debt stress typing/provenance are checked; causal intervention execution and arbitrary information-policy enforcement remain pending. G6, G14. |\\n79:| MC15 | Specify ordinary corporate operations and accounting across periods. U1, U2, U3, D. | Provide a bounded coherent package for revenue/collections, purchases/payments, inventory/costs, assets/depreciation, payroll, financing and applicable closing/tax assumptions, with explicit exclusions. | Specified bounded corporate package in Chs. 2, 8 with exact annual/interim and forecast fixtures. Delivery, collection, purchase, payment, costs, plant, payroll, debt, simple tax and closing reconcile. Real tax/revenue/lease/FX packages remain separate work. G4, G5. |\\n80:| MC16 | Produce coherent financial statements, movements and supported note schedules from the same underlying history/path. U1, U2, D. | Define balance sheet, income/comprehensive income, cash flow and equity mappings, non-cash movements, closing and note relationships; supply a full set of expected outputs. | Reference-checked complete Northstar balance sheet, income/zero OCI, direct/indirect cash flow and equity from common journals; Chs. 2, 8 and `northstar.json`. Apple checks a coherent marginal financing stress only. General note schedules and report engine remain pending. G4, G5, G6. |\\n81:| MC17 | Represent financing instruments and their economic/accounting lifecycles, particularly bonds and equity. U1, U2, D. | Specify proceeds, principal, carrying/fair values, rates, calendars, maturities, rights and share quantities; work issuance, accrual, settlement and relevant modification/conversion/default cases under declared treatments. | Partially specified and reference-checked: Chs. 8–9 distinguish principal/carrying/fair values and work ordinary and convertible bond issue, accrual, redemption/conversion, shares and funding default. Detailed modification, early repurchase and other-basis hybrid classification remain open. G4, G7. |\\n82:| MC18 | Preserve joint conditional future outcomes, honest bounds and distinct failure/completeness states. U2, P, D. | Define result payloads and queries that retain branch/path dependence, distinguish sampled ranges from certified bounds and distinguish default from unsupported/numerically failed output without silent dropping or renormalisation. | Specified result cells, branch statuses, strict bound attainment and unresolved mass in Chs. 6, 8, 10/Core 0. Exact linear, joint-output and funding/default reference checks pass; general simulation/result-query implementation remains pending. G2, G3, G6. |\\n99:| MC25 | Specify APIs, adapters, storage, versioning, identity and deterministic recovery. U3, P, D. | Define complete arguments/results, state ownership, migration semantics, evidence/model/run identity, event idempotency, random-stream allocation and replay requirements with examples. | Specified APIs, ownership, canonical identity, migration/replay and stream keying in Ch. 10/Core 0; concrete adapter exchanges included. Reference identity, replay/conflict, stream and bounded frozen-export integrity checks pass; transactional storage, migrations and non-Z3 adapters remain unimplemented. G2, G9, G18. |\\n102:| MC28 | Connect the full design through complete synthetic and real disclosure cases. U1, U2, U3, D. | Supply a known-history synthetic company and a named annual/interim real package across multiple dates; trace representative notes through records, constraints, alternatives and all affected future statements. Add structural finance/sector cases before fixing the core types. | Reference cases delivered in Ch. 2: complete synthetic Northstar history/revision/forecast and named Apple annual/interim inventory, notes and conditional stress. Ch. 9 supplies sector/finance structures. Real-company full semantic closure and independent case annotation remain open; no complete Apple forecast is claimed. G4, G5, G7. Nine eight-year report sequences are now source-checked; report-wide semantic cases and executable oracles remain to be prepared. |\\n116:| MC32 | Deliver a detailed, readable LaTeX/PDF document that governs the intended implementation. U3, P. | Explain the whole problem, justify chosen methods, stage mathematical prerequisites, define supported behaviour and disclose open scope; connect derivations and sources to complete examples and interfaces. Preserve mathematical/source fidelity during revisions and inspect the rendered result. | Revised Version 1.2 candidate, 11 chapters plus two appendices, full cases and supporting normative files. Build, rendered inspection and baseline-preservation review are recorded in `review/author-review.md`. Human comprehension, domain review and independent implementability acceptance remain pending. G1, G2, G4, G5, G7, G10. |\\n122:| MC33 | Define meaningful acceptance and separate engineering, accounting and scientific evidence. U3, P, D. | Provide canonical conformance inputs/outputs, corpus/annotation rules, justified release-specific criteria, review status and later forecast baselines/uncertainty protocols. Existing arithmetic/build checks keep their limited meanings. | Specified fixtures, corpus strata, annotation/adjudication/split protocol, hard conformance vetoes and provisional workload limits in Ch. 11/`corpus-protocol.json`. Reference checks, new debt semantic rejection cases, accounting dossiers and author review recorded; the 192-report source panel now passes acquisition acceptance and independent integrity checks. Annotation protocol/schema and provisional family roles exist; adjudication, performance and release validation remain pending. G5, G10. |\\n123:| MC34 | Stage implementation without losing the full mission or concealing unresolved decisions. U1, U2, U3, P, D. | Maintain requirement-to-section/case/gap traceability, explicit current-versus-later support, dependency order, workload assumptions and open decisions. Re-audit after material changes and test interactions, not just individual rows. | Original 34 requirement/acceptance pairs preserved; assessments updated and MC35 added from U4. The reviewed repair plan and G1–G18 result map preserve current/later/source-blocked obligations; implementation order remains in Ch. 11. Wider mission and acceptance stay active. G1–G18. |\\n124:| MC35 | Complete feasible internal preparation before paid professional review and minimise avoidable reviewer effort. U4. | Allocate every residual gap to internal work or a specific professional judgment; supply checked facts, dated sources, a proposed answer, counterargument and consequences before referral. Any later engagement has explicit user authority and an agreed bounded scope/cost. Keep human acceptance separate from continued internal work. | Standing rule installed in mission/AGENTS. All G1–G18 allocated in `review/internal-before-expert.md`; debt semantic checks, three source dossiers, journal checks and manuscript corrections completed. The review brief is unsent; actual-company facts, source and implementation tasks remain internal. No paid-review readiness, spending authority or savings estimate is claimed. The eight-year corpus, provenance checks, 20 regression tests and annotation preparation format were completed internally without professional engagement. |\\n141:MC28, MC30 and MC33–35 without closing semantic, accounting or forecast\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '77,85p;108,111p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md; sed -n '1,190p' docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,150p' scripts/check_repair_conformance.py; sed -n '178,240p' scripts/reconstruction_v1.py\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,150p' scripts/check_repair_conformance.py; sed -n '178,240p' scripts/reconstruction_v1.py\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Deterministic reference checks for the design, not a product test suite.\\n\\nUses independently authored expectations and exact arithmetic. Z3 checks the\\ndocument's supported rational-linear constraints; no statistical claim follows.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom collections import defaultdict\\nfrom copy import deepcopy\\nfrom fractions import Fraction as Q\\nimport hashlib\\nimport json\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport platform\\nimport time\\nimport z3\\n\\nROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\nFIX=ROOT/'docs/design/fixtures'\\nchecks=[]\\n\\ndef load(name): return json.loads((FIX/name).read_text())\\ndef check(name, condition, detail):\\n    checks.append(dict(name=name,passed=bool(condition),detail=detail))\\n    if not condition: raise AssertionError(name+': '+str(detail))\\n\\ndef post(state, e, committed):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Local oracle for atomic double-entry/idempotency, deliberately small.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    payload=json.dumps(e,sort_keys=True,separators=(',',':'))\\n    if e['id'] in committed:\\n        if committed[e['id']]!=payload: raise ValueError('EventIdentityConflict')\\n        return\\n    entries=[(p['account'],Q(p['signed_amount'])) for p in e['postings']]\\n    if sum(v for _,v in entries)!=0: raise ValueError('UnbalancedBatch')\\n    proposed=deepcopy(state)\\n    for a,v in entries: proposed[a]+=v\\n    state.clear(); state.update(proposed); committed[e['id']]=payload\\n\\ndef report_close(state, events, roles, period):\\n    selected=[e for e in events if e['period']==period]\\n    flows=defaultdict(Q)\\n    for e in selected:\\n        for p in e['postings']:\\n            if p['account']=='cash' and e['cash_class']:\\n                flows[e['cash_class']]+=Q(p['signed_amount'])\\n    profit=-sum(v for a,v in state.items() if roles[a] in ['income','expense'])\\n    revenue=-state['revenue']\\n    interest,tax=state['interest'],state['tax']\\n    # Closing is independent of the event generator; no cash arises here.\\n    for a in list(state):\\n        if roles[a] in ['income','expense']:\\n            state['retained']+=state[a];state[a]=Q(0)\\n    result=dict(cash=state['cash'],receivables=state['receivables'],inventory=state['inventory'],\\n        plant_net=state['plant_cost']+state['accum_depreciation'],tax_prepaid=state['tax_prepaid'],\\n        assets=sum(v for a,v in state.items() if roles[a] in ['asset','contra_asset']),\\n        payables=-state['payables'],debt=-state['debt'],\\n        equity=-sum(v for a,v in state.items() if roles[a]=='equity'),\\n        revenue=revenue,profit=profit,interest=interest,tax=tax,\\n        operating_cash=flows['operating'],investing_cash=flows['investing'],financing_cash=flows['financing'])\\n    check('balanced_'+period,sum(state.values())==0 and result['assets']==result['payables']+result['debt']+result['equity'],str(result))\\n    return result\\n\\ndef compare(name,actual,expected):\\n    check(name,all(actual[k]==Q(v) for k,v in expected.items()),{k:str(actual[k]) for k in expected})\\n\\ndef corporate():\\n    f=load('northstar.json'); state=defaultdict(Q,{k:Q(v) for k,v in f['opening'].items()}); committed={}\\n    check('opening_balance',sum(state.values())==0,'Signed account total is zero')\\n    periods={}\\n    for period in ['2024H1','2024H2']:\\n        for e in f['historical_events']:\\n            if e['period']==period:post(state,e,committed)\\n        periods[period]=report_close(state,f['historical_events'],f['accounts'],period)\\n        compare(period,periods[period],f['expected'][period])\\n    annual={k:sum(r[k] for r in periods.values()) for k in ['revenue','profit','operating_cash','investing_cash','financing_cash']}\\n    annual['cash_change']=state['cash']-Q(f['opening']['cash'])\\n    compare('annual_statements',annual,f['expected']['2024FY'])\\n    # Inverse construction from observed bridges. F,V remain a joint family.\\n    sales,collection,purchase,payment,cost,F,V=z3.Reals('sales collection purchase payment cost F V')\\n    constraints=[sales==260,35==20+sales-collection,20==30+purchase-cost,\\n        30==20+purchase-payment,cost==165,F>=0,V>=0,F+V==100,QZ('0.05')*(F+V)==5]\\n    solver=z3.Solver();solver.add(*constraints)\\n    check('reconstruction_feasible',solver.check()==z3.sat,'Closed scope annual bridge family')\\n    for x,value in [(collection,245),(purchase,155),(payment,145)]:\\n        solver.push();solver.add(x!=value); r=solver.check();solver.pop()\\n        check('recovered_'+str(x),r==z3.unsat,str(value))\\n    for fixed in [0,25,100]:\\n        solver.push();solver.add(F==fixed);r=solver.check();solver.pop()\\n        check('family_retains_fixed_'+str(fixed),r==z3.sat,'Different exposures with same historical interest')\\n    solver.push();solver.add(F==101);r=solver.check();solver.pop()\\n    check('impossible_debt_mix_rejected',r==z3.unsat,'Nonnegative floating amount forbids F=101')\\n    forecast=f['forecast']\\n    for branch,interest in [('fixed',Q(5)),('floating',Q(7))]:\\n        s=deepcopy(state); events=[]\\n        def e(name,entries,cls=None):\\n            record=dict(id='2025.'+name,period='2025_'+branch,date='2025-12-31',cash_class=cls,\\n                        postings=[dict(account=a,signed_amount=str(v)) for a,v in entries])\\n            events.append(record); post(s,record,{})\\n        demand=Q(forecast['demand_units']);price=Q(forecast['price']);cost=Q(forecast['unit_cost'])\\n        purchases=(demand+Q(forecast['target_inventory_units'])-s['inventory']/cost)*cost\\n        sales=demand*price; cogs=demand*cost\\n        collections=Q(forecast['current_sales_collection_fraction'])*sales+Q(forecast['legacy_receivable_collections'])\\n        suppliers=Q(forecast['old_payables_paid'])+Q(forecast['new_purchases_paid'])\\n        depreciation=Q(10)+Q(10)/5+Q(12)/12\\n        tax=(sales-cogs-Q(forecast['payroll'])-depreciation-interest)*Q(forecast['tax_rate'])\\n        e('sale',[('receivables',sales),('revenue',-sales)])\\n        e('collect',[('cash',collections),('receivables',-collections)],'operating')\\n        e('purchase',[('inventory',purchases),('payables',-purchases)])\\n        e('supplier',[('payables',suppliers),('cash',-suppliers)],'operating')\\n        e('deliver',[('cost_of_sales',cogs),('inventory',-cogs)])\\n        e('payroll',[('payroll',50),('cash',-50)],'operating')\\n        e('capex',[('plant_cost',20),('cash',-20)],'investing')\\n        e('depreciate',[('depreciation',depreciation),('accum_depreciation',-depreciation)])\\n        e('interest',[('interest',interest),('cash',-interest)],'operating')\\n        e('tax',[('tax',tax),('cash',-tax)],'operating')\\n        e('dividend',[('retained',8),('cash',-8)],'financing')\\n        result=report_close(s,events,f['accounts'],'2025_'+branch)\\n        compare('forecast_'+branch,result,f['expected']['2025_'+branch])\\n        check('direct_indirect_cash_'+branch,\\n              result['operating_cash']==result['profit']+depreciation-(s['receivables']-state['receivables'])-(s['inventory']-state['inventory'])-(s['payables']-state['payables']),\\n              'Profit + noncash depreciation - asset increases + liability increases')\\n    # Failure checks exercise atomicity and replay, not just successful sums.\\n    s=defaultdict(Q);done={}; good=dict(id='e',postings=[dict(account='cash',signed_amount='1'),dict(account='capital',signed_amount='-1')])\\n    post(s,good,done);post(s,good,done)\\n    check('event_idempotency',s['cash']==1,'Second identical event is a no-op')\\n    changed=deepcopy(good);changed['postings'][0]['signed_amount']='2'\\n    try:post(s,changed,done);raise AssertionError('Expected identity error')\\n    except ValueError as ex:check('event_identity_conflict',str(ex)=='EventIdentityConflict' and s['cash']==1,'Same ID different inputs rejected')\\n    changed['id']='bad'\\n    try:post(s,changed,done);raise AssertionError('Expected imbalance')\\n    except ValueError as ex:check('atomic_rejection',str(ex)=='UnbalancedBatch' and s['cash']==1 and 'bad' not in done,'No partial state/journal mutation')\\n\\ndef QZ(x):\\n    q=Q(x);return z3.RealVal(str(q.numerator)+'/'+str(q.denominator))\\n\\ndef bounds_and_weights():\\n    f=load('borrowings.json');F,V=z3.Reals('rounded_F rounded_V');D=F+V\\n    c=[F>=0,V>=0,D>=QZ('99.5'),D<QZ('100.5'),QZ('0.05')*D>=QZ('4.5'),QZ('0.05')*D<QZ('5.5')]\\n    I=QZ('.05')*F+QZ('.07')*V;s=z3.Solver();s.add(*c)\\n    for label,bound,comparison,attained in [('infimum','4.975',I<QZ('4.975'),True),('supremum','7.035',I>QZ('7.035'),False)]:\\n        s.push();s.add(comparison);r=s.check();s.pop()\\n        check('rounded_'+label+'_bound',r==z3.unsat,'Exact rational no-better-point certificate')\\n        s.push();s.add(I==QZ(bound));r=s.check();s.pop()\\n        check('rounded_'+label+'_attainment',(r==z3.sat)==attained,'Strict upper endpoint is not attained')\\n    # A sequence approaching the open supremum establishes sharpness, alongside its bound proof.\\n    for n in [10,100,1000]:\\n        s.push();s.add(F==0,D==QZ('100.5')-QZ(Q(1,n)));r=s.check();s.pop()\\n        check('upper_approach_'+str(n),r==z3.sat,'V = 100.5 - 1/n')\\n    prior=list(map(Q,f['mixture']['prior']));lik=list(map(Q,f['mixture']['likelihood_new_evidence']))\\n    mass=[a*b for a,b in zip(prior,lik)];postr=[x/sum(mass) for x in mass]\\n    check('finite_bayes',postr==list(map(Q,f['mixture']['expected_posterior'])),'New evidence changes weights; stress selection alone does not')\\ndef from_p03(ir, bindings, template_bindings):\\n    from core0_ir_v1 import validate_ir\\n    valid = validate_ir(ir, bindings)\\n    if not valid.valid:\\n        raise ValueError('P03 IR failed validation: ' + str(valid.diagnostics))\\n    if set(template_bindings) != {'DemoDebt@1/DebtMix'} or template_bindings['DemoDebt@1/DebtMix'] != 'fixed-floating-amounts-v1':\\n        raise ValueError('explicit supported template binding required')\\n    family = ir['historyFamilies'][0]; scope = ir['modelScopes'][0]\\n    p = Problem(scope['id'], family['evidence_view'], exclusions=scope['exclusions'], obligations=scope['obligations'])\\n    p.provenance = {'p03_ir_sha256': hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(ir,sort_keys=True).encode()).hexdigest(),\\n                    'template_bindings': dict(template_bindings), 'observation_ids': [x['id'] for x in ir['observations']],\\n                    'source_refs': ir['contracts'][0]['source_refs']}\\n    for row in ir['symbols']:\\n        v = z3.Real(row['id']); p.variables[row['id']] = v\\n        p.add('domain:'+row['id'],domain_formula(v,row['domain']))\\n    observations = {r['id']: r for r in ir['observations']}\\n    exprs = {r['id']:r for r in ir['expressions']}\\n    def lower(name):\\n        row=exprs[name]; op=row['op']\\n        if op=='literal':\\n            if row['type']=='Bool': return z3.BoolVal(row['text']=='true')\\n            return q(row['rational'])\\n        if op=='ref':\\n            if row['target'] in p.variables:return p.variables[row['target']]\\n            return lower(row['target'])\\n        if op=='value':\\n            target=exprs[row['args'][0]]['target'] if row['args'] else row['target']\\n            return q(observations[target]['domain']['lower'])\\n        if op=='call' and row['target']=='builtin:value@1':\\n            return q(observations[exprs[row['args'][0]]['target']]['domain']['lower'])\\n        args=[lower(a) for a in row['args']]\\n        if op=='call' and row['target']=='builtin:constant@1':return args[0]\\n        if op in ('constant','neg','not'):\\n            return args[0] if op=='constant' else -args[0] if op=='neg' else z3.Not(args[0])\\n        operations={'add':lambda a,b:a+b,'sub':lambda a,b:a-b,'mul':lambda a,b:a*b,'div':lambda a,b:a/b,\\n                    'eq':lambda a,b:a==b,'lt':lambda a,b:a<b,'le':lambda a,b:a<=b,\\n                    'gt':lambda a,b:a>b,'ge':lambda a,b:a>=b,'and':lambda *a:z3.And(*a),'or':lambda *a:z3.Or(*a)}\\n        if op not in operations:raise UnsupportedFragment('P03 operation: '+op)\\n        return operations[op](*args)\\n    try:\\n        rows={r['id']:r for r in ir['constraints']}\\n        for cid in family['constraints']: p.add(cid,lower(rows[cid]['expression']))\\n        for view in ir['alternatives']:\\n            if view['choice_group'] is not None:raise UnsupportedFragment('P03 choice group requires explicit partition')\\n            p.views[view['id']]=z3.And(*[lower(rows[c]['expression']) for c in view['constraints']])\\n        fields={f['name']:lower(f['expression']) for f in ir['contracts'][0]['fields']}\\n        from rational_solver_v1 import fraction\\n        principal=fraction(fields['principal'])\\n        if principal<=0:raise UnsupportedFragment('amount/fraction adapter requires positive exact principal')\\n        fixed=z3.Real('amount:fixed'); floating=z3.Real('amount:floating')\\n        p.variables.update({'amount:fixed':fixed,'amount:floating':floating})\\n        p.add('template:principal', fixed+floating==q(principal))\\n        p.add('template:fixed', fixed==q(principal)*fields['fixed_fraction'])\\n        p.add('template:amounts',z3.And(fixed>=0,floating>=0))\\n        rate=lower(ir['scenarios'][0]['drivers'][0]['expression'])\\n        p.outputs={'interest':fields['fixed_rate']*fixed+rate*floating,\\n                   'fixed':fixed,'floating':floating,'principal':fixed+floating}\\n        p.slots=1\\n    except UnsupportedFragment as exc:p.unsupported.append(str(exc))\\n    return p\\n\\n\\nclass FiniteMeasure:\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '77,85p;108,111p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md; sed -n '1,190p' docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"| MC13 | Drive economic events from contract state and explicit behaviour, then apply accounting rules and atomic journal/state updates. U2, D. | Specify one reference economic model, event payloads, recognition/measurement operations, preconditions, ordering and atomic transitions. Prove the stated bookkeeping invariant and separately define admissibility. | Specified Northstar economic decisions, event preconditions and operations in Chs. 2, 8. Reference journals, atomic rejection and idempotency checks pass. This verifies the bounded oracle, not a production event engine or accounting compliance. G2, G4, G6. |\\n| MC14 | Give scenarios and decision information explicit meanings. U2, P, D. | Define supported exogenous stress, observational-conditioning and intervention modes, or explicitly scope unsupported modes; enforce information dates and distinguish real-world from pricing measures. | Specified exogenous stress, observational conditioning, intervention preconditions and information capabilities in Ch. 8/Core 0. Finite conditioning, an information-date example and debt stress typing/provenance are checked; causal intervention execution and arbitrary information-policy enforcement remain pending. G6, G14. |\\n| MC15 | Specify ordinary corporate operations and accounting across periods. U1, U2, U3, D. | Provide a bounded coherent package for revenue/collections, purchases/payments, inventory/costs, assets/depreciation, payroll, financing and applicable closing/tax assumptions, with explicit exclusions. | Specified bounded corporate package in Chs. 2, 8 with exact annual/interim and forecast fixtures. Delivery, collection, purchase, payment, costs, plant, payroll, debt, simple tax and closing reconcile. Real tax/revenue/lease/FX packages remain separate work. G4, G5. |\\n| MC16 | Produce coherent financial statements, movements and supported note schedules from the same underlying history/path. U1, U2, D. | Define balance sheet, income/comprehensive income, cash flow and equity mappings, non-cash movements, closing and note relationships; supply a full set of expected outputs. | Reference-checked complete Northstar balance sheet, income/zero OCI, direct/indirect cash flow and equity from common journals; Chs. 2, 8 and `northstar.json`. Apple checks a coherent marginal financing stress only. General note schedules and report engine remain pending. G4, G5, G6. |\\n| MC17 | Represent financing instruments and their economic/accounting lifecycles, particularly bonds and equity. U1, U2, D. | Specify proceeds, principal, carrying/fair values, rates, calendars, maturities, rights and share quantities; work issuance, accrual, settlement and relevant modification/conversion/default cases under declared treatments. | Partially specified and reference-checked: Chs. 8–9 distinguish principal/carrying/fair values and work ordinary and convertible bond issue, accrual, redemption/conversion, shares and funding default. Detailed modification, early repurchase and other-basis hybrid classification remain open. G4, G7. |\\n| MC18 | Preserve joint conditional future outcomes, honest bounds and distinct failure/completeness states. U2, P, D. | Define result payloads and queries that retain branch/path dependence, distinguish sampled ranges from certified bounds and distinguish default from unsupported/numerically failed output without silent dropping or renormalisation. | Specified result cells, branch statuses, strict bound attainment and unresolved mass in Chs. 6, 8, 10/Core 0. Exact linear, joint-output and funding/default reference checks pass; general simulation/result-query implementation remains pending. G2, G3, G6. |\\n\\n## M4 — Standards, sectors and company variation\\n\\n| MC29 | Conduct a broad, technically grounded literature survey beyond the original collection. U3, P. | Inspect relevant primary methods/theory/evaluation/appendices and official code where available; compare direct alternatives; make genuine backward/forward screening, source-specific omissions, corrections and claim support inspectable. | Partially repaired: 179 individual title/metadata decisions across 194 occurrences/72 searches replace generic exclusions; generation rejects unscreened candidates. Mack and selected rule sources add inspected technical support. All-candidate full-text review and later module literature are not complete. G8. |\\n| MC30 | Preserve the relevant source library and precise provenance. U3, P. | Archive accessible relevant papers under the required naming convention, retain exact versions/anchors, preserve original files, and document unavailable sources without relying on their uninspected claims. | 32 catalogued paper PDFs verified by hash/page count, with original collection preserved; Apple filings and selected standards archived separately. Version/authority limits and four blocked papers remain recorded. Mechanical integrity does not certify every technical claim. G8. The additional financial-report corpus preserves 244 original versions, source/index/discovery hashes and an append-only attempt history; 192 target slots pass source acceptance. |\\n| MC31 | Survey open-source tools and define evidence-based reuse boundaries. U3, P, D. | Inspect official interfaces/licences, identify supported subsets, specify adapter exchanges and version assumptions, and separate inspected capabilities from later integration/performance evidence. | Inspected software snapshots/licences retained; Ch. 10/Core 0 specify typed exchanges, errors and concrete examples. Z3 is exercised. Arelle/ACTUS/QuantLib/Docling/ledger integrations and pinned deployment combinations remain pending. G9. |\\n\\n\\\\chapter{Reconstruction and execution procedures}\\n\\\\label{ch:execution}\\n\\n\\\\section{Ingest, reconcile and construct histories}\\n\\nThe historical procedure starts with a filing manifest. It records documents,\\nreporting dates, publication dates, revisions and expected statements and\\nnotes. Tagged filings are parsed through an XBRL adapter; PDF and HTML sources\\nare segmented into text, tables, captions and references. The original bytes\\nand extraction output remain immutable. Re-running an improved extractor\\ncreates a new extraction version with links to the same source.\\n\\nFor each table, the importer first resolves headers, units, signs, periods and\\ndimensions. It then proposes concept mappings. A deterministic validator checks\\nsubtotal arithmetic, duplicate facts, comparative consistency and cross-note\\nreferences. Every proposed repair creates a new reading. The system may suggest\\nthat an OCR value is 10 rather than 70, but only a reviewed correction or an\\nexplicit alternative allows that reading into a validated model.\\n\\nReconciliation proceeds from local totals to movement schedules. A debt bridge\\nmay contain opening debt, issuance, repayment, acquired debt, interest\\naccretion, currency effects, fair-value changes and closing debt. Every\\ncomponent receives a movement type. An unexplained residual is stored as a\\nresidual with a source and period; it is not automatically classified as\\nrepayment or issuance. A model can introduce an unknown decomposition of that\\nresidual, subject to evidence and economic constraints.\\n\\nThe reconstruction engine then performs the following finite procedure within\\na declared model scope:\\n\\\\begin{enumerate}\\n\\\\item Build shared variables for observations, opening states, contract terms\\nand supported movement amounts. Attach original rounding domains.\\n\\\\item Add identities, roll-forwards, account restrictions, contractual\\nrelationships and cross-period links. Add each semantic reading as a condition\\non the same joint model.\\n\\\\item Propagate types, units, intervals and simple equalities. Reject context\\nmismatches before invoking a numerical solver.\\n\\\\item Ask the solver for feasibility. On infeasibility, return a sufficient\\nconflicting subset of constraints, its source spans and model assumptions.\\nA solver's conflict core need not be the smallest possible explanation.\\n\\\\item Retain finite alternatives and continuous solution families symbolically.\\nMaterialise example histories only when needed for review or execution.\\n\\\\item Check whether each requested simulation has sufficient economic state.\\nMissing maturities, reset dates or cohort composition become declared\\nassumptions or explicit unresolved inputs.\\n\\\\end{enumerate}\\n\\nUnrestricted journal enumeration would be unbounded: arbitrary offsetting\\ntransactions can be inserted without changing reports. The model therefore\\ndeclares allowed event types, time resolution, relevant accounts, lot/cohort\\nresolution and limits on latent contract instances. These limits describe the\\nrepresented family; they are not evidence that all real possibilities were\\nsearched. The compiler canonicalises syntactic duplicates and equivalences\\nestablished by its supported rewrite rules. It does not decide arbitrary\\neconomic equivalence. Probability measures attach to declared economic\\nhypotheses or parameters, never to a count of encodings; adding a duplicate\\nrepresentation therefore cannot create extra probability mass or coverage.\\n\\nThe first implementation uses symbolic linear bridges and finite structural\\nchoices. Nonlinear economic models can be evaluated on feasible states through\\nplugins. A solver timeout preserves the unresolved family and returns\\n\\\\code{SolverIncomplete}; it does not prune the family as impossible. Search\\nbudgets belong to run configuration and are recorded with the results.\\n\\n\\\\section{Condition a run without rewriting history}\\n\\nA run selects an evidence view and cutoff, a historical family, a forecast\\nstarting date, scenario definitions, accounting packages, management policies,\\noutput queries and numerical settings. A run may use a concrete history,\\nan exact symbolic family, a finite set of conditional histories, or weighted\\ndraws from a declared distribution. The output records which mode was used.\\n\\nSuppose no debt maturity is disclosed. An analyst may run a conditional case\\nthat assumes all debt matures after the forecast horizon. The run is valid\\nunder that assumption even though the historical representation remains\\nincomplete. The interface must display the assumption next to the result and\\nprovide sensitivity cases when the assumption is material. It must not label\\nthe assumed maturity as a discovered historical fact.\\n\\nManagement behaviour normally uses only information available at the decision\\ndate. A perfect-foresight stress case is a separate, explicitly labelled\\npolicy. Scenarios should share the same underlying innovations when estimating\\npaired differences where appropriate, with stable stream identifiers so\\nbranch order does not change the draws. Common random numbers improve the\\ncomparability of paired simulations; they do not imply that every branch has\\nthe same economic event counts or shock distribution.\\n\\n\\\\section{Schedule and commit events}\\n\\nEach event carries an economic occurrence time, accrual interval when relevant,\\nsettlement time, entity, contract or cohort identifier, currency, inputs and\\nprovenance. Its ordering key consists of date, declared phase, dependency edges\\nand a deterministic tie identifier. The reference phases are: opening and\\nscheduled contractual changes; market observations and rate resets; business\\nevents and decisions; accrual and measurement; settlement; period closing and\\nreporting. A contract can require a more specific dependency. These phases are\\nan engineering starting point, not a universal description of market timing.\\n\\nTwo events may share a tie order only if their order is either specified or\\nirrelevant to the result. If payment before remeasurement and payment after\\nremeasurement differ, an unresolved ordering is a model ambiguity or an error.\\nThe engine does not conceal it behind alphabetical event IDs.\\n\\n\\\\begin{lstlisting}\\nexecute_event(event, state, run_context):\\n    verify prerequisites and information availability\\n    resolve applicable measurement and recognition rules\\n    compute proposed economic changes and measurements\\n    compute proposed journal batch(es)\\n    validate types, contexts, balance, constraints and idempotency\\n    atomically commit state, journals and explanation edges\\n    return new state, emitted dependent events, diagnostics\\n\\\\end{lstlisting}\\n\\nThe atomic unit includes the economic state and its accounting effects.\\nIf posting fails, neither state changes. A repeated event ID with identical\\ninputs returns the existing result; the same ID with different inputs is a\\nconflict. Consolidation runs after entity books reach the required date and\\nstores its adjustments separately. A failure in one scenario branch cannot\\nmutate another branch's state.\\n\\n\\\\section{Funding, tax and other simultaneous relations}\\n\\nSome financial models have circular dependencies. Interest affects taxable\\nprofit; tax and investment affect funding needs; funding affects interest.\\nThe reference executor first tries to resolve these through explicit timing.\\nFor example, beginning-of-period debt can determine current interest, with\\nnew borrowing affecting the next accrual period. That is acceptable only when\\nthe model's timing assumption is stated and appropriate.\\n\\nWhere the economic model genuinely requires simultaneous decisions, the\\ndependency graph identifies the strongly connected component and delegates it\\nto a declared equation or optimisation solver. The solver must return a\\nsolution, residuals, admissibility checks and uniqueness or multiplicity\\nstatus. A contraction iteration requires a justified convergence condition;\\nan arbitrary fixed iteration count is not a mathematical solution. Multiple\\nadmissible equilibria become alternatives when material. No solution produces\\na model outcome such as financing failure, or an explicit numerical failure,\\ndepending on the cause.\\n\\nFunding policy must include available facilities, limits, covenants, collateral\\nand allowed capital actions. The program cannot issue unlimited debt to keep\\ncash positive. An inability to meet payments may be a legitimate default\\noutcome. Default ends or changes contractual and accounting processes under\\nthe relevant event rules; it is not quietly discarded as a bad simulation draw.\\n\\n\\\\section{Worked example: identical history, different future journals}\\n\\nReturn to the company in Chapter~\\\\ref{ch:purpose}. Immediately after the\\nhistorical interest payment and closing, cash is 95, debt is 100 and equity\\nis $-5$. There are no other assets, liabilities or transactions. Next year's\\nexpense is 5 in the all-fixed branch and 7 in the all-floating branch under\\nthe rate shock. The generated entries and closing statements are:\\n\\n\\\\begin{center}\\n\\\\begin{tabular}{lrr}\\n\\\\toprule Output & All fixed & All floating\\\\\\\\\\\\midrule\\nDebit interest expense / credit cash &5&7\\\\\\\\\\nClosing cash &90&88\\\\\\\\\\nClosing debt &100&100\\\\\\\\\\nCurrent-year profit & $-5$ & $-7$\\\\\\\\\\nClosing equity after profit transfer &$-10$&$-12$\\\\\\\\\\nCash change &$-5$&$-7$\\\\\\\\\\\\bottomrule\\n\\\\end{tabular}\\n\\\\end{center}\\nThe balance-sheet identity holds in each branch: $90=100-10$ and\\n$88=100-12$. The demonstration reporting profile classifies interest paid as\\noperating cash flow. A different permitted reporting profile changes that\\nclassification, while preserving the cash movement and source event. This\\nexample proves the intended distinction and its arithmetic; it does not\\nestimate the probability that either debt structure describes a real company.\\n\\n\\\\section{Worked example: a bond has several relevant amounts}\\n\\nA two-period zero-coupon bond raises cash of 100 and promises 110.25 at maturity.\\nAssume a 5\\\\% effective rate per period, no transaction costs, no default, and\\namortised-cost treatment under a demonstration rule. The effective-interest\\nschedule follows directly from $100(1.05)^2=110.25$:\\n\\\\begin{center}\\n\\\\begin{tabular}{lrrr}\\n\\\\toprule Date & Opening liability & Interest accretion & Closing liability\\\\\\\\\\\\midrule\\nIssue &0&0&100\\\\\\\\\\nEnd of period 1 &100&5&105\\\\\\\\\\nEnd of period 2, before payment &105&5.25&110.25\\\\\\\\\\nRedemption &110.25&0&0\\\\\\\\\\\\bottomrule\\n\\\\end{tabular}\\n\\\\end{center}\\nIssuance debits cash and credits the liability by 100. Each accretion debits\\ninterest expense and credits the liability. Redemption debits the liability\\nand credits cash by 110.25. Legal face amount, carrying amount and market\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"rg -n 'Northstar|14575|14,575|13/52|200|joint|half|prepaid|behaviour|interest|rate' docs/design/chapters/13-reference-company.tex\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"rg -n 'Northstar|14575|14,575|13/52|200|joint|half|prepaid|behaviour|interest|rate' docs/design/chapters/13-reference-company.tex\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"6:Northstar Components is a synthetic seller of one homogeneous good. Its\\n15:At the beginning of 2024, Northstar holds cash of 60, receivables of 20,\\n24:periods. Here the chosen accrual convention assigns one half-year to each.\\n25:Cash-flow dates within a half-year are not recovered from a period aggregate;\\n32:\\\\toprule Movement & First half & Second half\\\\\\\\\\\\midrule\\n52:the payable. Delivery separately removes inventory at cost. Plant purchases\\n55:one unit of second-half depreciation. The addition of 12 enters service after\\n58:Tax is deliberately simple: 20\\\\% of positive profit before tax, with all these\\n59:expenses deductible and no deferred tax. The first-half payment exceeds its\\n60:tax expense by 2, leaving prepaid tax; that prepayment is used in the second\\n61:half. A genuine corporate tax package would need jurisdiction, tax basis,\\n69:totals are hidden. Under Northstar's explicit no-write-off, no-acquisition and\\n86:Both endpoints and every intermediate allocation survive. Northstar therefore\\n88:in the same joint historical family. A solver must not turn its convenient\\n92:settlement, payroll, plant addition, depreciation, interest, tax payment and\\n93:dividend per half-year. Each slot represents a classified aggregate event.\\n102:expense accounts close to retained earnings at each half-year boundary;\\n124:interest 5 gives profit before tax of 37. Tax expense is 7.4 and profit is 29.6.\\n130:245 less supplier payments 145, payroll 42, interest 5 and tax payments 7.4\\n135:The prepaid-tax balance is zero at both annual endpoints. The two cash routes\\n144:prepaid tax of 2. Corrected interim profit is 6 and equity is 72, as above.\\n145:The original statement remains an accurate record of what was published, even\\n157:\\\\code{v2}, so second-half revenue is $260-110=150$. Subtracting the original\\n176:$\\\\alpha=F/100$. With the floating rate resetting to 7\\\\%, interest is\\n199:The joint symbolic result is cash $93.6+1.6\\\\alpha$, profit\\n219:It records internal cross-references and externally incorporated material,\\n225:every incorporated external document.\\n232:85,750. Fair value is separately disclosed as 88.4 billion. None of these\\n235:Note 9 identifies the notes as fixed-rate, then states that interest-rate\\n236:swaps effectively convert a portion to floating rates. Note 4 reports\\n237:interest-rate contract notional of 14,575 at the annual date. A notional is\\n239:interest sensitivity: reset timing, remaining periods, curve conventions and\\n250:To demonstrate a source-to-forecast calculation, freeze the interim balance\\n252:period: a 200-basis-point rate increase, no principal change, no offsetting\\n255:produces $0.02\\\\times(13/52)E=72.875$ million additional interest. This exposure\\n257:interim net sensitivity. Under that condition, debit interest expense and\\n264:conditional added interest lies in $[0,72.875]$ before monetary rounding. That\\n267:coherent marginal propagation. Northstar supplies the complete-company\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nimport json,pathlib\\nfor f in ['docs/design/fixtures/northstar.json','docs/design/fixtures/temporal.json']:\\n d=json.loads(pathlib.Path(f).read_text()); print(f, 'keys',list(d))\\n for k in d:\\n  if k not in ['historical_events','forecast_events','expected','scenarios']: print(k, str(d[k])[:1700])\\n print('expected',str(d.get('expected'))[:1000])\\nfor f in ['data/accounting-master/deliverables/P05/execution.json','data/accounting-master/deliverables/P05/result.md','tests/test_accounting_p05.py']:\\n print(f,'exists',pathlib.Path(f).exists())\\nPY\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nimport json,pathlib\\nfor f in ['docs/design/fixtures/northstar.json','docs/design/fixtures/temporal.json']:\\n d=json.loads(pathlib.Path(f).read_text()); print(f, 'keys',list(d))\\n for k in d:\\n  if k not in ['historical_events','forecast_events','expected','scenarios']: print(k, str(d[k])[:1700])\\n print('expected',str(d.get('expected'))[:1000])\\nfor f in ['data/accounting-master/deliverables/P05/execution.json','data/accounting-master/deliverables/P05/result.md','tests/test_accounting_p05.py']:\\n print(f,'exists',pathlib.Path(f).exists())\\nPY\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"docs/design/fixtures/northstar.json keys ['schema', 'entity', 'currency', 'units', 'basis', 'disclosure_scope', 'assumptions', 'accounts', 'opening', 'historical_events', 'expected', 'forecast', 'coverage_units']\\nschema accdsl-design-fixture/1\\nentity Northstar Components (synthetic)\\ncurrency USD\\nunits one currency unit\\nbasis DemoCorporate/1; not GAAP certification\\ndisclosure_scope Closed synthetic goods company; the listed source package is complete by construction\\nassumptions {'historical_resolution': 'half-year aggregate flows; existence of intraperiod schedules required, not recovered invoices', 'inventory': 'one homogeneous good at cost 5; purchases before delivery; quantities equal costs/5', 'sales': 'delivery transfers control; no returns, services, variable consideration or foreign currency', 'tax': '20% positive taxable profit, all expenses deductible, no deferred tax; excess payment is prepaid tax', 'plant': 'opening cost 100, annual depreciation 10; end-H1 addition 10 lives 5 years; end-H2 addition 12 lives 12 years; zero residuals', 'debt': '100 throughout; fixed and floating both 5% in 2024; fixed 5%, floating resets to 7% in 2025; all maturities after forecast', 'time': 'half-year accrual fractions 1/2, annual 1; explicit teaching convention', 'closing': 'temporary accounts closed after each H1/H2; annual income uses movements excluding closing', 'universe': 'no omitted company, OCI, acquisition, tax or off-balance-sheet operations inside this synthetic package'}\\naccounts {'cash': 'asset', 'receivables': 'asset', 'inventory': 'asset', 'plant_cost': 'asset', 'accum_depreciation': 'contra_asset', 'tax_prepaid': 'asset', 'payables': 'liability', 'debt': 'liability', 'capital': 'equity', 'retained': 'equity', 'revenue': 'income', 'cost_of_sales': 'expense', 'payroll': 'expense', 'depreciation': 'expense', 'interest': 'expense', 'tax': 'expense'}\\nopening {'cash': '60', 'receivables': '20', 'inventory': '30', 'plant_cost': '100', 'accum_depreciation': '-20', 'tax_prepaid': '0', 'payables': '-20', 'debt': '-100', 'capital': '-50', 'retained': '-20'}\\nforecast {'start': '2025-01-01', 'end_exclusive': '2026-01-01', 'demand_units': '30', 'price': '10', 'unit_cost': '5', 'target_inventory_units': '8', 'current_sales_collection_fraction': '0.9', 'legacy_receivable_collections': '10', 'old_payables_paid': '30', 'new_purchases_paid': '130', 'payroll': '50', 'capex_at_period_end': '20', 'dividend': '8', 'tax_rate': '0.2', 'funding_limit': '0'}\\ncoverage_units [{'id': 'NS.opening', 'kind': 'statement', 'disposition': 'structured', 'content': 'Opening balance sheet and account balances'}, {'id': 'NS.h1.original', 'kind': 'statement', 'disposition': 'superseded_reading_preserved', 'content': 'Originally revenue 120, receivables 30, tax expense/payment 3.5, profit 14, equity 80'}, {'id': 'NS.h1.correction', 'kind': 'note', 'disposition': 'structured', 'content': 'Premature invoice 10: reverse revenue and receivable; reduce tax expense 2 into tax prepayment; corrected profit 6'}, {'id': 'NS.fy', 'kind': 'statement', 'disposition': 'structured', 'content': 'Annual and revised interim statements derived from listed events'}, {'id': 'NS.operations', 'kind': 'policy', 'disposition': 'structured', 'content': 'Goods, inventory, asset and working-capital assumptions above'}, {'id': 'NS.debt', 'kind': 'note', 'disposition': 'alternative_family', 'content': 'Principal 100, interest 5; fixed/floating composition undisclosed'}, {'id': 'NS.equity', 'kind': 'note', 'disposition': 'structured', 'content': 'Capital 50; original retained 20; dividends H1 4, H2 5'}, {'id': 'NS.reference', 'kind': 'cross_reference', 'disposition': 'resolved', 'target': 'NS.debt', 'content': 'Financing note applies to debt and interest in every statement'}]\\nexpected {'2024H1': {'cash': '65', 'receivables': '20', 'inventory': '25', 'plant_net': '85', 'tax_prepaid': '2', 'assets': '197', 'payables': '25', 'debt': '100', 'equity': '72', 'revenue': '110', 'profit': '6', 'operating_cash': '19', 'investing_cash': '-10', 'financing_cash': '-4'}, '2024H2': {'cash': '74.6', 'receivables': '35', 'inventory': '20', 'plant_net': '91', 'tax_prepaid': '0', 'assets': '220.6', 'payables': '30', 'debt': '100', 'equity': '90.6', 'revenue': '150', 'profit': '23.6', 'operating_cash': '26.6', 'investing_cash': '-12', 'financing_cash': '-5'}, '2024FY': {'revenue': '260', 'profit': '29.6', 'operating_cash': '45.6', 'investing_cash': '-22', 'financing_cash': '-9', 'cash_change': '14.6'}, '2025_fixed': {'cash': '95.2', 'receivables': '55', 'inventory': '40', 'plant_net': '98', 'tax_prepaid': '0', 'assets': '288.2', 'payables': '40', 'debt': '100', 'equity': '148.2', 'revenue': '300', 'profit': '65.6', 'interest': '5', 'tax': '16.4', 'operating_cash': '48.6', 'investing_ca\\ndocs/design/fixtures/temporal.json keys ['availability_policy', 'assertions', 'queries', 'expected_valid_h2', 'incompatible_vintage_h2']\\navailability_policy date-only filing is available at next midnight in stated reporting timezone\\nassertions [{'id': 'h1-original', 'key': 'revenue:H1:USD:NS:Demo', 'value': '120', 'available': '2024-08-01T00:00:00Z', 'ingested': '2024-08-03T00:00:00Z', 'vintage': 'v1', 'supersedes': []}, {'id': 'h1-restated', 'key': 'revenue:H1:USD:NS:Demo', 'value': '110', 'available': '2025-03-02T00:00:00Z', 'ingested': '2025-03-05T00:00:00Z', 'vintage': 'v2', 'supersedes': ['h1-original']}, {'id': 'fy', 'key': 'revenue:FY:USD:NS:Demo', 'value': '260', 'available': '2025-03-02T00:00:00Z', 'ingested': '2025-03-05T00:00:00Z', 'vintage': 'v2', 'supersedes': []}]\\nqueries [{'cutoff': '2024-09-01T00:00:00Z', 'system_as_of': None, 'expect': ['h1-original']}, {'cutoff': '2025-03-03T00:00:00Z', 'system_as_of': None, 'expect': ['h1-restated', 'fy']}, {'cutoff': '2025-03-03T00:00:00Z', 'system_as_of': '2025-03-04T00:00:00Z', 'expect': ['h1-original']}, {'cutoff': '2025-03-06T00:00:00Z', 'system_as_of': None, 'mode': 'original', 'expect': ['h1-original', 'fy']}]\\nexpected_valid_h2 150\\nincompatible_vintage_h2 140 must be rejected\\nexpected None\\ndata/accounting-master/deliverables/P05/execution.json exists False\\ndata/accounting-master/deliverables/P05/result.md exists False\\ntests/test_accounting_p05.py exists False\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,64p;160,206p;250,270p' docs/design/chapters/13-reference-company.tex; sed -n '178,194p;240,285p' scripts/reconstruction_v1.py\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,64p;160,206p;250,270p' docs/design/chapters/13-reference-company.tex; sed -n '178,194p;240,285p' scripts/reconstruction_v1.py\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\\\\chapter{A complete company and a real disclosure}\\n\\\\label{ch:case}\\n\\n\\\\section{What a balance must remember}\\n\\nNorthstar Components is a synthetic seller of one homogeneous good. Its\\ndisclosures, transactions and contract terms are specified together, so we can\\ncheck whether reconstruction preserves a known possible history. All amounts\\nin this example are currency units, not thousands. The company has no foreign\\ncurrency, subsidiaries, leases, returns or other comprehensive income. These\\nare declared features of the example, not assumptions to impose on an imported\\ncompany. Its source package and expected results are supplied in\\n\\\\code{fixtures/northstar.json}.\\n\\nAt the beginning of 2024, Northstar holds cash of 60, receivables of 20,\\ninventory of 30 and plant costing 100 with accumulated depreciation of 20.\\nIt owes suppliers 20 and lenders 100. Share capital is 50 and retained earnings\\nare 20. Thus assets of 190 equal liabilities of 120 plus equity of 70.\\nInventory consists of six units costing 5 each. The existing plant depreciates\\nby 10 a year, with no residual value. The loan remains outstanding throughout\\n2024; both possible contract types charge 5\\\\% during that year.\\n\\nThe six months ending June and December provide two successive observation\\nperiods. Here the chosen accrual convention assigns one half-year to each.\\nCash-flow dates within a half-year are not recovered from a period aggregate;\\nthe synthetic history supplies a feasible ordering in which inventory is\\npurchased before delivery and customer receipts precede the payments they fund.\\nMore detailed liquidity questions require more detailed dates.\\n\\n\\\\begin{center}\\n\\\\begin{tabular}{lrr}\\n\\\\toprule Movement & First half & Second half\\\\\\\\\\\\midrule\\nDelivered sales on credit &110&150\\\\\\\\\\nCustomer collections &110&135\\\\\\\\\\nInventory purchases on credit &70&85\\\\\\\\\\nSupplier payments &65&80\\\\\\\\\\nCost of goods delivered &75&90\\\\\\\\\\nPayroll paid &20&22\\\\\\\\\\nPlant purchased at period end &10&12\\\\\\\\\\nDepreciation &5&6\\\\\\\\\\nInterest accrued and paid &2.5&2.5\\\\\\\\\\nTax expense &1.5&5.9\\\\\\\\\\nTax paid &3.5&3.9\\\\\\\\\\nDividends paid &4&5\\\\\\\\\\\\bottomrule\\n\\\\end{tabular}\\n\\\\end{center}\\n\\nEach row has an economic meaning before it has a posting. Delivery of the\\ngood transfers control and creates an unconditional receivable; invoicing is\\nassumed simultaneous in this example. Collection settles that receivable.\\nPurchases increase inventory and trade payables; paying the supplier settles\\nthe payable. Delivery separately removes inventory at cost. Plant purchases\\nare capital expenditure, while depreciation consumes its service potential.\\nThe addition of 10 enters service after June and has a five-year life, producing\\none unit of second-half depreciation. The addition of 12 enters service after\\nDecember and has a twelve-year life.\\n\\nTax is deliberately simple: 20\\\\% of positive profit before tax, with all these\\nexpenses deductible and no deferred tax. The first-half payment exceeds its\\ntax expense by 2, leaving prepaid tax; that prepayment is used in the second\\nhalf. A genuine corporate tax package would need jurisdiction, tax basis,\\nlosses, timing differences and payment schedules. The example's tax rule\\ngoverns its own numbers only.\\n\\nsupports it. A later date alone does not establish such a relationship.\\n\\n\\\\section{One economic scenario, several complete futures}\\n\\nFor 2025, assume demand for 30 units at price 10, unit purchase cost 5 and a\\ntarget closing inventory of eight units. Opening inventory is four units, so\\nthe purchase decision is $30+8-4=34$ units, costing 170. Deliveries cost 150,\\nleaving inventory of 40. Collect 90\\\\% of current sales and 10 of old\\nreceivables: $270+10=280$, leaving receivables of 55. Pay old suppliers 30\\nand 130 of the new purchases, leaving payables of 40. Payroll is 50, capital\\nexpenditure of 20 occurs at year-end and dividends are 8.\\n\\nThese decisions are inputs to a conditional forecast. They are not estimates\\nof demand or optimal management responses. No new borrowing is available.\\nUnder the existing asset schedules, depreciation is $10+10/5+12/12=13$.\\nThe new year-end asset begins depreciation in the next period. Let\\n$\\\\alpha=F/100$. With the floating rate resetting to 7\\\\%, interest is\\n$I=7-2\\\\alpha$. Profit before tax is\\n$300-150-50-13-I=80+2\\\\alpha$, giving tax $16+0.4\\\\alpha$ and profit\\n$64+1.6\\\\alpha$.\\n\\n\\\\begin{center}\\n\\\\begin{tabular}{lrr}\\n\\\\toprule 2025 statement amount & All fixed & All floating\\\\\\\\\\\\midrule\\nRevenue &300&300\\\\\\\\\\nInterest expense &5&7\\\\\\\\\\nTax expense &16.4&16\\\\\\\\\\nProfit and comprehensive income &65.6&64\\\\\\\\\\nOperating cash flow &48.6&47\\\\\\\\\\nInvesting cash flow &$-20$&$-20$\\\\\\\\\\nFinancing cash flow &$-8$&$-8$\\\\\\\\\\\\midrule\\nClosing cash &95.2&93.6\\\\\\\\\\nReceivables / inventory / net plant &55 / 40 / 98&55 / 40 / 98\\\\\\\\\\nAssets &288.2&286.6\\\\\\\\\\nPayables / debt &40 / 100&40 / 100\\\\\\\\\\nEquity &148.2&146.6\\\\\\\\\\\\bottomrule\\n\\\\end{tabular}\\n\\\\end{center}\\n\\nThe joint symbolic result is cash $93.6+1.6\\\\alpha$, profit\\n$64+1.6\\\\alpha$ and equity $146.6+1.6\\\\alpha$, with the same\\n$\\\\alpha\\\\in[0,1]$ throughout. Selecting the smallest cash and largest equity\\nindependently would describe no feasible company. A requested distribution\\nrequires a measure over that same historical family; the accounting equations\\ndo not supply one.\\n\\n\\\\section{Apple: source labels do not identify exposure}\\nTo demonstrate a source-to-forecast calculation, freeze the interim balance\\nsheet and apply a \\\\emph{marginal} financing stress for a following 13-week\\nperiod: a 200-basis-point rate increase, no principal change, no offsetting\\nhedge beyond the explicitly selected exposure, immediate cash settlement and\\nno tax effect. An assumed effective floating exposure $E=14{,}575$ million\\nproduces $0.02\\\\times(13/52)E=72.875$ million additional interest. This exposure\\nuses the annual notional as a conditional input; it is not asserted to be the\\ninterim net sensitivity. Under that condition, debit interest expense and\\ncredit cash by 72.875. The resulting marginal statements have cash 30,226.125,\\nassets 344,012.125, liabilities 277,327, equity 66,685.125, profit and comprehensive\\nincome of $-72.875$, and operating cash flow of $-72.875$ relative to the frozen\\nbaseline. The balance-sheet difference equals the equity difference exactly.\\n\\nIf exposure is instead only restricted to $0\\\\leq E\\\\leq14{,}575$, the\\nconditional added interest lies in $[0,72.875]$ before monetary rounding. That\\nrestriction is a stress assumption and is not claimed to bound every real\\nApple exposure. This real case verifies evidence, context, mappings and a\\ncoherent marginal propagation. Northstar supplies the complete-company\\nforecast; a complete Apple forecast remains dependent on its unmodelled\\noperations and undisclosed terms.\\ndef from_p03(ir, bindings, template_bindings):\\n    from core0_ir_v1 import validate_ir\\n    valid = validate_ir(ir, bindings)\\n    if not valid.valid:\\n        raise ValueError('P03 IR failed validation: ' + str(valid.diagnostics))\\n    if set(template_bindings) != {'DemoDebt@1/DebtMix'} or template_bindings['DemoDebt@1/DebtMix'] != 'fixed-floating-amounts-v1':\\n        raise ValueError('explicit supported template binding required')\\n    family = ir['historyFamilies'][0]; scope = ir['modelScopes'][0]\\n    p = Problem(scope['id'], family['evidence_view'], exclusions=scope['exclusions'], obligations=scope['obligations'])\\n    p.provenance = {'p03_ir_sha256': hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(ir,sort_keys=True).encode()).hexdigest(),\\n                    'template_bindings': dict(template_bindings), 'observation_ids': [x['id'] for x in ir['observations']],\\n                    'source_refs': ir['contracts'][0]['source_refs']}\\n    for row in ir['symbols']:\\n        v = z3.Real(row['id']); p.variables[row['id']] = v\\n        p.add('domain:'+row['id'],domain_formula(v,row['domain']))\\n    observations = {r['id']: r for r in ir['observations']}\\n    exprs = {r['id']:r for r in ir['expressions']}\\nclass FiniteMeasure:\\n    def __init__(self, atoms, justification, used=()):\\n        if not justification:raise ValueError('explicit joint-measure justification required')\\n        self.atoms=deepcopy(atoms);self.justification=justification;self.used=set(used)\\n        ids=[a['id'] for a in atoms]\\n        if len(ids)!=len(set(ids)) or not atoms:raise ValueError('distinct joint atoms required')\\n        hypotheses = [a.get('hypothesis') for a in atoms]\\n        if any(not isinstance(h, dict) or not h for h in hypotheses):\\n            raise ValueError('explicit complete finite economic assignments required')\\n        keys = set(hypotheses[0])\\n        if any(set(h) != keys or any(isinstance(v, (dict,list)) for v in h.values()) for h in hypotheses):\\n            raise ValueError('joint hypotheses require the same complete scalar coordinates')\\n        if len({json.dumps(h,sort_keys=True) for h in hypotheses}) != len(hypotheses):\\n            raise ValueError('overlapping identical economic hypotheses')\\n        weights=[rational(a['weight']) for a in atoms]\\n        if any(w<0 for w in weights) or sum(weights)!=1:raise ValueError('joint weights must sum to one')\\n    def update(self, likelihood, information_blocks):\\n        blocks=set(information_blocks)\\n        if not blocks or len(blocks) != len(information_blocks) or blocks & self.used:raise ValueError('repeated/missing information block')\\n        if set(likelihood)!={a['id'] for a in self.atoms}:raise ValueError('likelihood must cover every atom')\\n        ls={k:rational(v) for k,v in likelihood.items()}\\n        if any(v<0 or v>1 for v in ls.values()):raise ValueError('invalid event likelihood')\\n        weights=[rational(a['weight'])*ls[a['id']] for a in self.atoms]; total=sum(weights)\\n        if total==0:raise ValueError('zero-probability conditioning')\\n        new=[dict(a,weight=str(w/total)) for a,w in zip(self.atoms,weights)]\\n        return FiniteMeasure(new,self.justification,self.used|blocks)\\n    def event(self, ids):\\n        ids=set(ids)\\n        if ids-{a['id'] for a in self.atoms}:raise ValueError('unknown atom')\\n        return sum((rational(a['weight']) for a in self.atoms if a['id'] in ids),F(0))\\n    def summary(self):\\n        mass={};mean=F(0);available=True\\n        for a in self.atoms:\\n            w=rational(a['weight']); status=a['status'];mass[status]=mass.get(status,F(0))+w\\n            if a.get('outcome') is None:\\n                if w:available=False\\n            else:mean+=w*rational(a['outcome'])\\n        return {'mass':{k:str(v) for k,v in mass.items()},'mean':str(mean) if available else None,\\n                'normalised_over_successful_only':False}\\n\\n\\ndef weighted_summary(measure):\\n    if not isinstance(measure,FiniteMeasure):raise ValueError('unweighted families have no mean')\\n    return measure.summary()\\n\\n\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nimport json,pathlib\\nfor p in ['data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03/conformance.json','data/accounting-master/deliverables/P04/conformance.json','data/accounting-master/deliverables/P02/case.json']:\\n d=json.loads(pathlib.Path(p).read_text());print(p,'keys',list(d))\\n for k in ['status','summary','issues','residuals','unsupported','obligations']:\\n  if k in d:print(k,str(d[k])[:1800])\\nPY\\nrg -n 'from_p03|DemoDebt|p03|principal|joint' tests/test_accounting_p04.py\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nimport json,pathlib\\nfor p in ['data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03/conformance.json','data/accounting-master/deliverables/P04/conformance.json','data/accounting-master/deliverables/P02/case.json']:\\n d=json.loads(pathlib.Path(p).read_text());print(p,'keys',list(d))\\n for k in ['status','summary','issues','residuals','unsupported','obligations']:\\n  if k in d:print(k,str(d[k])[:1800])\\nPY\\nrg -n 'from_p03|DemoDebt|p03|principal|joint' tests/test_accounting_p04.py\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03/conformance.json keys ['schema_version', 'passed', 'profile', 'manifest', 'tests', 'observations', 'hashes', 'checked_input_integrity', 'protected_files', 'requirement_coverage', 'unsupported', 'acceptance']\\nunsupported ['general package loading and overrides', 'events, rules, postings, journals and runtime execution', 'records, arrays, field selection and finite choices', 'multiple books/entities/observations, other currencies and calendars', 'cross-company mappings and broader uncertainty categories', 'reconstruction, feasibility proof, accounting validity and forecast validity']\\ndata/accounting-master/deliverables/P04/conformance.json keys ['schema_version', 'passed', 'obligation_status', 'tests', 'observations', 'protection', 'code_stable_during_check', 'provenance', 'input_source_test_hashes', 'manifest', 'requirement_coverage', 'unsupported', 'acceptance']\\nunsupported ['arbitrary histories and template discovery', 'nonlinear solving and continuous probability inference', 'unbounded integer search', 'general accounting validity and forecast validity', 'general aggregation equivalence and human acceptance']\\ndata/accounting-master/deliverables/P02/case.json keys ['acceptance', 'anchor_count', 'coverage', 'external', 'filing_availability', 'fiscal_calendar', 'mapping_contract', 'notes', 'observations', 'p01_register', 'plan_sha256', 'policies', 'reconciliations', 'recovery_plan_sha256', 'representation_comparison', 'rounding_model', 'schema_version', 'scope', 'source_acquisition', 'source_bindings', 'source_pins', 'unidentified_histories']\\n19:from test_accounting_p03 import bindings, BASE\\n60:    def test_p03_parent_views(self):\\n65:            p=from_p03(c.ir,bindings(),{'DemoDebt@1/DebtMix':'fixed-floating-amounts-v1'})\\n77:        self.record('p03_views',results)\\n131:        measure=FiniteMeasure([{'id':'fixed','hypothesis':{'economic_state':'fixed'},'weight':'3/5','status':'complete','outcome':'5'}, {'id':'floating','hypothesis':{'economic_state':'floating'},'weight':'2/5','status':'unsupported','outcome':None}], 'explicit synthetic joint prior')\\n137:        contracts=[{'id':str(i),'principal':str(10+i),'rate':'1/20','reset':'fixed','maturity':'2030','hedge':'none'} for i in range(2)]\\n146:    def test_view_union_order_and_joint_outputs(self):\\n148:        p=from_p03(compile_source(source,bindings()).ir,bindings(),{'DemoDebt@1/DebtMix':'fixed-floating-amounts-v1'})\\n156:        pp=from_p03(compile_source(swapped,bindings()).ir,bindings(),{'DemoDebt@1/DebtMix':'fixed-floating-amounts-v1'})\\n158:        joint=solve(p,B,extra=[p.outputs['fixed']==100,p.outputs['floating']==100])\\n159:        self.assertEqual(joint['status'],'Infeasible')\\n161:        self.record('view_union_joint',{'parent':parent,'intersection':intersection,'union':union,'incompatible_marginals':joint})\\n248:        m=FiniteMeasure([{'id':'a','hypothesis':{'economic_state':'a'},'weight':'1/4','status':'default','outcome':None}, {'id':'b','hypothesis':{'economic_state':'b'},'weight':'1/4','status':'unresolved','outcome':None}, {'id':'c','hypothesis':{'economic_state':'c'},'weight':'1/2','status':'complete','outcome':'10'}], 'synthetic disjoint economic hypotheses')\\n273:        contracts=[{'id':'duplicate','principal':'10','rate':'1/20','reset':'fixed','maturity':'2030','hedge':'none'}]*2\\n299:    def test_p03_changed_principal_and_rates(self):\\n301:        for principal,fixed,stress in ((150,'0.04','0.09'),(80,'0.06','0.03')):\\n302:            source=BASE.replace('100 USD',f'{principal} USD').replace('0.05 per year',fixed+' per year').replace('0.07 per year',stress+' per year')\\n303:            bound=bindings(principal);compiled=compile_source(source,bound)\\n305:            p=from_p03(compiled.ir,bound,{'DemoDebt@1/DebtMix':'fixed-floating-amounts-v1'})\\n307:            endpoints=sorted([F(principal)*F(fixed),F(principal)*F(stress)])\\n310:            self.assertEqual([F(conditional['bounds'][d]['value']) for d in ('lower','upper')],[F(principal)*F(fixed)]*2)\\n313:            self.assertEqual(F(middle['cells'][0]['outputs']['interest']),F(principal)*(F(fixed)+F(stress))/2)\\n314:            evidence.append({'principal':principal,'rates':[fixed,stress],'oracle_endpoints':list(map(str,endpoints)),\\n316:        self.record('p03_metamorphic_rates',evidence)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"The plan correctly identifies the main baseline risk: the current Northstar checker replays supplied postings. P05 proposes separate economic inputs and independent journal and statement checks. The recovery record also matches the filesystem: implementation deliverables are still absent. I’m checking the history adapter and information-date rules for remaining material objections.\\n\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,90p' tests/test_accounting_p04.py; sed -n '1,62p' tests/test_accounting_p03.py; sed -n '1,78p' docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,90p' tests/test_accounting_p04.py; sed -n '1,62p' tests/test_accounting_p03.py; sed -n '1,78p' docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Independent input replay and exact algebra; P04 executed obligations.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport copy\\nfrom contextlib import redirect_stderr, redirect_stdout\\nfrom dataclasses import replace\\nfrom fractions import Fraction as F\\nfrom itertools import product\\nimport json\\nimport hashlib\\nimport io\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport sys\\nimport tempfile\\nimport unittest\\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\\nsys.path.insert(0,str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]/'scripts'))\\nimport z3\\nfrom rational_solver_v1 import *\\nfrom reconstruction_v1 import *\\nfrom test_accounting_p03 import bindings, BASE\\nfrom core0_frontends_v1 import compile_source\\nROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\nOBSERVATIONS=[]\\nB=Budget(20,10000,500,500,20000,1000,1000000)\\n\\n\\ndef spec():\\n    return json.loads((ROOT/'docs/design/fixtures/p04-reconstruction-cases-v1.json').read_text())['input_fixture']\\n\\n\\ndef observation(s,amount):\\n    return {'id':'cash-note','context':copy.deepcopy(s['context']),'action':'Accept','source':['synthetic:cash-note'],\\n            'mapping':'cash','domain':{'lower':str(amount),'upper':str(amount),'lower_closed':True,'upper_closed':True}}\\n\\n\\nclass ReconstructionTests(unittest.TestCase):\\n    def record(self,name,result):OBSERVATIONS.append({'obligation':name,'passed':True,'result':result})\\n    def test_independent_enumeration(self):\\n        evidence=[]\\n        # Oracle replays original template incidence; no production expressions or Z3.\\n        for opening,total,limit,coefficient in [(10,13,3,1),(4,8,4,1),(7,13,3,2)]:\\n            s=spec();s['opening']={'Cash':str(opening),'Equity':str(-opening)}\\n            s['templates']['sale']['postings']={'Cash':str(coefficient),'Equity':str(-coefficient)}\\n            for row in s['slots']:row['integer_bounds']=[0,limit]\\n            s['observations']=[observation(s,total)]\\n            p=construct(s);r=solve(p,B)\\n            actual={(int(F(c['witness']['a'])),int(F(c['witness']['b']))) for c in r['cells'] if c['feasibility']=='sat'}\\n            expected=set()\\n            for a,b in product(range(limit+1),repeat=2):\\n                cash=F(opening)\\n                for amount in (a,b):cash+=F(coefficient)*amount\\n                if cash==total:expected.add((a,b))\\n            self.assertEqual(actual,expected);self.assertEqual(r['status'],'ExactWithinScope')\\n            for c in r['cells']:\\n                if c['feasibility']=='sat':self.assertEqual(F(c['outputs']['cash'])+F(c['outputs']['equity']),0)\\n            s['slots'].reverse();rr=solve(construct(s),B)\\n            self.assertEqual({tuple(c['witness'][n] for n in ('a','b')) for c in rr['cells'] if c['feasibility']=='sat'},\\n                             {tuple(c['witness'][n] for n in ('a','b')) for c in r['cells'] if c['feasibility']=='sat'})\\n            evidence.append({'inputs':s,'oracle':sorted(expected),'actual':r})\\n        self.record('enumeration',evidence)\\n    def test_p03_parent_views(self):\\n        source=BASE.replace('alternative allFixed { assume alpha == 1; }','alternative allFixed { assume alpha <= 0.75; }').replace('alternative allFloating { assume alpha == 0; }','alternative allFloating { assume alpha >= 0.25; }')\\n        results=[]\\n        for text in (BASE,source):\\n            c=compile_source(text,bindings());self.assertTrue(c.ok)\\n            p=from_p03(c.ir,bindings(),{'DemoDebt@1/DebtMix':'fixed-floating-amounts-v1'})\\n            self.assertFalse(p.unsupported)\\n            r=solve(p,B,p.outputs['interest']);self.assertEqual(r['bounds']['lower']['value'],'5');self.assertEqual(r['bounds']['upper']['value'],'7')\\n            self.assertEqual(r['coverage']['total'],1)\\n            half=p.variables['alpha']==q('1/2')\\n            self.assertEqual(solve(p,B,extra=[half])['feasibility'],'Feasible')\\n            both=solve(p,B,selected_views=['allFixed','allFloating'],view_operator='intersection',extra=[half])\\n            self.assertEqual(both['feasibility'],'Infeasible' if text==BASE else 'Feasible')\\n            fixed=solve(p,B,selected_views=['allFixed'],extra=[half])\\n            self.assertEqual(fixed['feasibility'],'Infeasible' if text==BASE else 'Feasible')\\n            self.assertEqual(solve(p,B,extra=[half])['feasibility'],'Feasible')\\n            results.append({'parent':r,'intersection':both,'conditional':fixed})\\n        self.record('p03_views',results)\\n    def test_rounded_strict_and_unbounded(self):\\n        fixture=json.loads((ROOT/'docs/design/fixtures/borrowings.json').read_text())['rounded']\\n        p=Problem('rounded-debt','fixture');f,v=z3.Reals('F V');p.variables={'F':f,'V':v}\\n        p.add('amounts',z3.And(f>=0,v>=0));p.add('debt-note',z3.And(f+v>=q(fixture['debt'][0]),f+v<q(fixture['debt'][1])))\\n        p.add('interest-note',z3.And(q('.05')*(f+v)>=q(fixture['interest'][0]),q('.05')*(f+v)<q(fixture['interest'][1])))\\n        r=solve(p,B,q('.05')*f+q('.07')*v)\\n        self.assertEqual(r['bounds']['lower']['value'],'199/40');self.assertTrue(r['bounds']['lower']['attained'])\\n        self.assertEqual(r['bounds']['upper']['value'],'1407/200');self.assertFalse(r['bounds']['upper']['attained'])\\n        x=z3.Real('x');empty=Problem('empty','fixture',variables={'x':x});empty.add('strict',x>0);empty.add('closed',x<=0)\\n        self.assertEqual(solve(empty,B,x)['status'],'Infeasible')\\n        u=Problem('unbounded','fixture',variables={'x':x});u.add('positive',x>0)\\n        un=solve(u,B,x);self.assertEqual(un['bounds']['upper']['status'],'Unbounded');self.assertFalse(un['bounds']['lower']['attained'])\\n        const=solve(u,B,q(2));self.assertTrue(const['bounds']['lower']['attained'])\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Executed P03 obligations; authored typed inputs never pass through the parser.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport copy\\nfrom dataclasses import replace\\nfrom fractions import Fraction as F\\nimport hashlib\\nimport json\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport sys\\nimport tempfile\\nimport unittest\\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\\n\\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / 'scripts'))\\nimport core0_ir_v1 as ir\\nfrom core0_frontends_v1 import compile_source\\nimport jsonschema\\n\\nOBSERVATIONS = []\\nBASE = (ROOT / 'docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc').read_text()\\nREASON = 'Fixed-rate proportion not disclosed'\\nRENAMED = '''module FinancingStudy version \\\"2\\\";\\nuse DemoDebt version \\\"1\\\";\\nsource disclosure = external(\\\"synthetic-note-7\\\");\\nentity Beta functional USD;\\nbook Statutory entity Beta basis DemoDebt version \\\"1\\\";\\naccount Cash : Asset book Statutory;\\naccount Debt : Liability book Statutory;\\naccount InterestExpense : Expense book Statutory;\\naccount Retained : Equity book Statutory;\\nopening carried for Statutory from external(\\\"after-2025-close\\\");\\nobservation borrowing : Money<USD> instant @2025-12-31 = 150 USD from disclosure;\\nsymbol share : Real in [0, 1] because \\\"Fixed-rate proportion not disclosed\\\";\\ncontract facility : DebtMix book Statutory {\\n principal = value(borrowing); fixed_fraction = share;\\n fixed_rate = 0.05 per year; initial_floating_rate = 0.05 per year;\\n}\\nalternative fixed { assume share == 1; }\\nalternative floating { assume share == 0; }\\nscenario shock { set market_rate = constant(0.08 per year); }\\nreport financials for Statutory { mapping = external(\\\"DemoDebt.statements.v1\\\"); }\\n'''\\n\\n\\ndef bindings(principal=100, renamed=False):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Explicit synthetic evidence, separately authored from source and expected IR.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    p = F(principal); stamp = '2026-01-01T00:00:00Z'\\n    book, symbol = ('Statutory', 'share') if renamed else ('Local', 'alpha')\\n    names = ('fixed', 'floating') if renamed else ('allFixed', 'allFloating')\\n    package_path = ROOT / 'docs/design/fixtures/demo-debt-package.json'\\n    return ir.CompileBindings(\\n        packages=[ir.PackageBinding('DemoDebt', '1', hashlib.sha256(package_path.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\\n            'DemoDebt', '2025-01-01', '2028-01-01', ['reset','accrue_and_pay','close','statements'],\\n            ['builtin:Core0@1','DemoCalendar@1'], ['fixture:demo-debt-package.json'])],\\n        readings=[ir.ReadingBinding('synthetic-note-7', f'Synthetic disclosed debt {p} USD; split undisclosed', p,\\n            'USD', '2025-12-31', 'fixture:p03-synthetic', 'synthetic-2025', stamp, stamp,\\n            'synthetic-author', stamp, 'Explicit synthetic acceptance, not human approval', stamp,\\n            system_as_of=stamp, action='Accept')],\\n        openings=[ir.OpeningBinding('after-2025-close', '2025-12-31',\\n            {'Cash':p-5, 'Debt':-p, 'InterestExpense':0, 'Retained':5}, book=book)],\\n        reports=[ir.ReportBinding('DemoDebt.statements.v1','DemoDebt.statements.v1',\\n            'interest_operating','close',['accrue_and_pay'])],\\n\\\\chapter{Reconstruction and execution procedures}\\n\\\\label{ch:execution}\\n\\n\\\\section{Ingest, reconcile and construct histories}\\n\\nThe historical procedure starts with a filing manifest. It records documents,\\nreporting dates, publication dates, revisions and expected statements and\\nnotes. Tagged filings are parsed through an XBRL adapter; PDF and HTML sources\\nare segmented into text, tables, captions and references. The original bytes\\nand extraction output remain immutable. Re-running an improved extractor\\ncreates a new extraction version with links to the same source.\\n\\nFor each table, the importer first resolves headers, units, signs, periods and\\ndimensions. It then proposes concept mappings. A deterministic validator checks\\nsubtotal arithmetic, duplicate facts, comparative consistency and cross-note\\nreferences. Every proposed repair creates a new reading. The system may suggest\\nthat an OCR value is 10 rather than 70, but only a reviewed correction or an\\nexplicit alternative allows that reading into a validated model.\\n\\nReconciliation proceeds from local totals to movement schedules. A debt bridge\\nmay contain opening debt, issuance, repayment, acquired debt, interest\\naccretion, currency effects, fair-value changes and closing debt. Every\\ncomponent receives a movement type. An unexplained residual is stored as a\\nresidual with a source and period; it is not automatically classified as\\nrepayment or issuance. A model can introduce an unknown decomposition of that\\nresidual, subject to evidence and economic constraints.\\n\\nThe reconstruction engine then performs the following finite procedure within\\na declared model scope:\\n\\\\begin{enumerate}\\n\\\\item Build shared variables for observations, opening states, contract terms\\nand supported movement amounts. Attach original rounding domains.\\n\\\\item Add identities, roll-forwards, account restrictions, contractual\\nrelationships and cross-period links. Add each semantic reading as a condition\\non the same joint model.\\n\\\\item Propagate types, units, intervals and simple equalities. Reject context\\nmismatches before invoking a numerical solver.\\n\\\\item Ask the solver for feasibility. On infeasibility, return a sufficient\\nconflicting subset of constraints, its source spans and model assumptions.\\nA solver's conflict core need not be the smallest possible explanation.\\n\\\\item Retain finite alternatives and continuous solution families symbolically.\\nMaterialise example histories only when needed for review or execution.\\n\\\\item Check whether each requested simulation has sufficient economic state.\\nMissing maturities, reset dates or cohort composition become declared\\nassumptions or explicit unresolved inputs.\\n\\\\end{enumerate}\\n\\nUnrestricted journal enumeration would be unbounded: arbitrary offsetting\\ntransactions can be inserted without changing reports. The model therefore\\ndeclares allowed event types, time resolution, relevant accounts, lot/cohort\\nresolution and limits on latent contract instances. These limits describe the\\nrepresented family; they are not evidence that all real possibilities were\\nsearched. The compiler canonicalises syntactic duplicates and equivalences\\nestablished by its supported rewrite rules. It does not decide arbitrary\\neconomic equivalence. Probability measures attach to declared economic\\nhypotheses or parameters, never to a count of encodings; adding a duplicate\\nrepresentation therefore cannot create extra probability mass or coverage.\\n\\nThe first implementation uses symbolic linear bridges and finite structural\\nchoices. Nonlinear economic models can be evaluated on feasible states through\\nplugins. A solver timeout preserves the unresolved family and returns\\n\\\\code{SolverIncomplete}; it does not prune the family as impossible. Search\\nbudgets belong to run configuration and are recorded with the results.\\n\\n\\\\section{Condition a run without rewriting history}\\n\\nA run selects an evidence view and cutoff, a historical family, a forecast\\nstarting date, scenario definitions, accounting packages, management policies,\\noutput queries and numerical settings. A run may use a concrete history,\\nan exact symbolic family, a finite set of conditional histories, or weighted\\ndraws from a declared distribution. The output records which mode was used.\\n\\nSuppose no debt maturity is disclosed. An analyst may run a conditional case\\nthat assumes all debt matures after the forecast horizon. The run is valid\\nunder that assumption even though the historical representation remains\\nincomplete. The interface must display the assumption next to the result and\\nprovide sensitivity cases when the assumption is material. It must not label\\nthe assumed maturity as a discovered historical fact.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_12\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nimport json,pathlib\\np=pathlib.Path('data/accounting-master/deliverables/P02/case.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text())\\nprint('rounding',d['rounding_model']); print('observations type',type(d['observations']).__name__)\\nrows=d['observations']; rows=rows.values() if isinstance(rows,dict) else rows\\nfor r in rows:\\n if any(x in str(r.get('concept','')).lower() for x in ['cash','assets','liabilities','equity','notional']):\\n  print({k:r.get(k) for k in ['id','concept','value','scale','quantum','context','measurement']})\\nprint('acceptance',d['acceptance'])\\nPY\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_12\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nimport json,pathlib\\np=pathlib.Path('data/accounting-master/deliverables/P02/case.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text())\\nprint('rounding',d['rounding_model']); print('observations type',type(d['observations']).__name__)\\nrows=d['observations']; rows=rows.values() if isinstance(rows,dict) else rows\\nfor r in rows:\\n if any(x in str(r.get('concept','')).lower() for x in ['cash','assets','liabilities','equity','notional']):\\n  print({k:r.get(k) for k in ['id','concept','value','scale','quantum','context','measurement']})\\nprint('acceptance',d['acceptance'])\\nPY\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"rounding {'arithmetic': 'exact rational USD', 'inference': 'compatibility only; no distribution or identified underlying exact amounts', 'issuer_tie_rule': 'unknown', 'model': 'closed half-unit nearest-rounding intervals'}\\nobservations type list\\n{'id': 'annual.bs.2024-09-28.assets', 'concept': 'us-gaap:Assets', 'value': None, 'scale': 6, 'quantum': None, 'context': {'basis': 'US GAAP', 'currency': 'USD', 'dimensions': {}, 'entity': '0000320193', 'entity_scheme': 'http://www.sec.gov/CIK', 'perimeter': 'consolidated', 'period': {'instant': '2024-09-28'}}, 'measurement': 'carrying_amount'}\\n{'id': 'annual.bs.2024-09-28.liabilities', 'concept': 'us-gaap:Liabilities', 'value': None, 'scale': 6, 'quantum': None, 'context': {'basis': 'US GAAP', 'currency': 'USD', 'dimensions': {}, 'entity': '0000320193', 'entity_scheme': 'http://www.sec.gov/CIK', 'perimeter': 'consolidated', 'period': {'instant': '2024-09-28'}}, 'measurement': 'carrying_amount'}\\n{'id': 'annual.bs.2024-09-28.equity', 'concept': 'us-gaap:StockholdersEquity', 'value': None, 'scale': 6, 'quantum': None, 'context': {'basis': 'US GAAP', 'currency': 'USD', 'dimensions': {}, 'entity': '0000320193', 'entity_scheme': 'http://www.sec.gov/CIK', 'perimeter': 'consolidated', 'period': {'instant': '2024-09-28'}}, 'measurement': 'carrying_amount'}\\n{'id': 'annual.bs.2024-09-28.cash', 'concept': 'us-gaap:CashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue', 'value': None, 'scale': 6, 'quantum': None, 'context': {'basis': 'US GAAP', 'currency': 'USD', 'dimens